{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles","id":230252,"title":"What do you want to see in the Firestorm Chronicles?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-16T08:48:22-07:00","id":230252,"title":"What do you want to see in the Firestorm Chronicles?","content":"Every other subforum's doing it, and we've actually got a date for this one!<br /> <br /> Okay, so we're about to be blessed with the second edition of Promethean. Along the lines of the badassness we've already gotten in the Strix chronicles and has been teased at us for Idigam and Fallen World, what would you like to see changed for our favorite sad hobo corpses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T09:08:53-07:00","id":230286,"title":"","content":"Fucking <i>awesome</i>!<br /> Personally I'll say a little prayer for more character creation options: new Transmutations/Bestowments would be great, as would generally more customization. I always loved how weird Prometheans are, hopefully I'll get some new weird stuff to confuse my players with in this, hehe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T10:12:02-07:00","id":230315,"title":"","content":"I'd like it if Golems and Muses are made from Clay/Marble by default.<br /> <br /> I'd quite like it if Promethians start with a few Persistant Conditions that get resolved as they get closer to humanity to represent physically becoming more human. Maybe one sevear one that should go away in the first session, two that last a bit longer.<br /> <br /> I'd really like it if <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Ben Qou's humanity rules</a> were adopted. However I would like a bit more benefit in there for having a human mentor - you've got to be able to have Rabbi Meyer (If you haven't read The Golem and the Jinn; it is the most Promethian book in existence)<br /> <br /> Having a big list of options for the Principle is great. Having nearly all of them boil down to &quot;status qoe&quot; is bad. More diversity please; and at least one of those options should be &quot;the Abrahamic God&quot;.<br /> <br /> And I really want to feel like the Fire is Divine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T13:44:04-07:00","id":230505,"title":"","content":"All this book needs to do is make my group want to play <i>Promethean</i>. As it stands, they universally find the game an unplayable thought experiment that doesn't function as a roleplaying game. While I don't agree with them, making it a bit more accessible (or at least adding the options to make it so) would be thoroughly appreciated. Adding more toolkit options to all of the games is a good thing, and a sliding scale of just <i>how</i> <i>shitty </i>is it to be a Promethean in my chronicle?&quot; is something I'd love to see.<br /> <br /> That, and a list of developer-approved musical inspirations would make my day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 08-16-2014, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T13:54:56-07:00","id":230515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230505#post230505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All this book needs to do is make my group want to play <i>Promethean</i>. As it stands, they universally find the game an unplayable thought experiment that doesn't fuction as a roleplaying game. While I don't agree with them, making it a bit more accessible (or adding the options to make it so) would be thoroughly appreciated. Adding more toolkit options to all of the games is a good thing, and a sliding scale of just <i>how</i> <i>shitty </i>is it to be a Promethean in my chronicle?&quot; is something I'd love to see.<br /> <br /> That, and a list of developer-approved musical inspirations would make my day.</div> </div> </div> </div>First and foremost, Disquiet needs to be toned down a bit. It directly gets in the way of roleplaying and the like. Same with the Wasteland which causes headaches for the player and the GM due to the constant need to move around. I understand the thematic need for it (Prommies are the Hobos of nWoD) but most of the time, it simply gets in the way. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:00:54-07:00","id":230523,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, I think they'll be hard-pressed to change the game so drastically as to make someone go from &quot;unplayable thought experiment&quot; to &quot;I'll play that&quot;. Though, I basically felt the same way based off of synopsis and so forth, and came around completely upon actually reading the book (which I only did because I wanted to read about the Principal). <br /> <br /> I love the idea of having those Lineages start as stone/marble. That feels better.<br /> <br /> I don't think that they should list off the Abrahamic God as an option for what the Principal, mostly because that seems super direct and is already hinted at as being the source of that myth. So I could see and like them saying that the quashallim being what inspired the Abrahamic Religions, as well as mortal's failed interpretation of what the hell they wanted.<br /> <br /> But I don't feel super strongly about it, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:09:37-07:00","id":230532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230523#post230523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, I think they'll be hard-pressed to change the game so drastically as to make someone go from &quot;unplayable thought experiment&quot; to &quot;I'll play that&quot;. Though, I basically felt the same way based off of synopsis and so forth, and came around completely upon actually reading the book (which I only did because I wanted to read about the Principal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying to remove it. I'm saying that a modular approach would be best, allowing Storytellers to fine-tune the game until it becomes what they need it to be for their chronicle. <i>Danse Macabre</i> is my favorite book for VtR because it gave thematic and mechanical support for Tier 1 &quot;holy shit, I have just been Embraced and what is going on&quot; play as well as &quot;I am a dread and ancient elder embroiled in globe-spanning conspiracies.&quot; More toolkit options like that in the core books would make me so happy; in Promethean's case, that would be options for how severely Disquiet and Wasteland impact the world around you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:30:22-07:00","id":230560,"title":"","content":"Mostly, just want to see Disquiet toned down. It is a major game limiter, perhaps make it much more minor at lower Azoth. I'd like to see it completely revamped to make it more group friendly and allow for a little more stationary games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T15:52:13-07:00","id":230629,"title":"","content":"What I want to see? Lineages be less pronounced so that every Promethean is truly a unique, individual creature which represents just how ingenuitive and exceptional their creation was. I also want to see more 'magic and setting content.' Vampire was very bland in that regard to me, when it first came out, but Wicked Dead and B&amp;S did a lot to change that for me. Expand on kyptae and flux-tainted areas and people, show more rules for qashmalim with the new ephemeral rules. I want to see Humanity be more tied to Promethean nature and not just 'regular' Integrity; start it off low like a Mummy, and maybe have one track for Humanity/Integrity like Mummy has Memory/Morality.<br /> <br /> Also, I hope the example settings are some kind of iteration of 'Pilgrimmage Paths' because they wouldn't be a static city, but rather a path of a larger region.<br /> <br /> What I <b>don't</b> want to see is Wasteland and Disquiet tuned down","signature":"","edited":{"userid":638,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","user":"reseru","date":". 08-16-2014, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T17:16:36-07:00","id":230709,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve stated what I want elsewhere. Summarizing:<br /> <br /> \u2022 More choices in terms of how a Promethean is made. In particular, incorporate much of the demiurge material from <b>Saturnine Night</b>, and/or provide ways for mortals to gather Azoth and imbue a creation with it. In keeping with the title, one possible source of Pyros would be a Firestorm. <br /> <br /> \u2022 More options for what a Promethean is made of. Flesh should be the best \u201cconductor\u201d for Pyros; but constructs should also be options. Unfleshed should be a subset of constructs, with the creator being rewarded for his efforts if he incorporates articulated joints, motors to move the joints, a power system to drive the motors, a brain of some sort to direct them, sensors to provide feedback, and so on. Likewise, starting out with a humanoid form should be encouraged by means of simulating any inhuman features with Pandoran Transmutations that both increase the likelihood of the Generative Act going bad and interfere with the final Crucible. This is somewhat less important to me than the first option; but especially in the God Machine era, the Unfleshed option should be given more prominence. <br /> <br /> \u2022 A build-your-own-Lineage system, with the five Lineages from the orignal game being presented as worked examples. The way the Unfleshed are done in <b>Saturnine Night</b> would be a reasonable approach to use. However, I\u2019d avoid the \u201cmake your own Humour\u201d stuff from <b>Saturnine Night</b>\u2019s demiurges section, or at least relegate it to a box to the effect of \u201cfive Humours aren\u2019t enough for you, then make up more of your own.\u201d In effect, the Humours should take the role that Lineages currently hold as the five-way division of most Created in terms of what they are. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Humanity should start at 3 and build up from there. One of the Promethean\u2019s Aspirations should be replaced by a Purpose, which works the same way for the most part but represents the \u201cprogramming\u201d the Promethean was created with. The Purpose should also have a compulsory facet to it, which can be overcome using Humanity. Possibly give the Promethean\u2019s creator the ability to make the Purpose harder to resist, to facilitate \u201crebellion against my maker\u201d story options. Conversely, let the Purpose help the Promethean resist the throes of Torment, with it being more effective with the creator boosting it, so that neither the Purpose nor the creator\u2019s resulting influence over his creation are entirely bad things. <br /> <br /> \u2022 There should be \u201cHumanity 0 Prometheans\u201d akin to <b>Blood and Smoke</b>\u2019s Revenants: \u201corganic machines\u201d (or not-so-organic, if the construct/Unfleshed options are supported) that behave like clones from the original game \u2014 in fact, clones should be one example of these things; the Imbued from <b>World of Darkness: Antagonists</b> would be another. Like Revenants, there should be an option for an \u201cautomaton\u201d to be upgraded to a full-fledged Promethean using an abbreviated version of the Generative Act. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Base Athanors on Refinements rather than Lineages/Humours. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Disquiet and Wasteland should be extrapolations of the mechanics found in <b>Mortal Remains</b>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: (to keep it all in one place)<br /> <br /> \u2022 Revise the \u201cFinal Azoth Roll\u201d as an Extended Action where the goal is to accumulate enough successes to recover your memories and/or to integrate yourself into mortal society, with Exceptional Successes granting you little bonuses that leave you human but leaning more toward the \u201cbest of humanity\u201d end of the spectrum. 15\u201320 successes seems about right for this. <br /> \u2022 Consider reversing the roles of Humanity and Azoth in the New Dawn mechanics: you need enough Azoth to transform yourself innto a human; and you need sufficient Humanity for your resulting life to be a noticeable improvement over your Promethean life: not enough Humanity when you Redeem, and you end up as an amnesiac vagrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-29-2014, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T17:49:40-07:00","id":230731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230629#post230629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I <b>don't</b> want to see is Wasteland and Disquiet tuned down</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire subject is a touchy one that requires a lot of finnicking, but my instincts start here, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T18:34:10-07:00","id":230799,"title":"","content":"Some things i would like to see:<br /> 1. The Promethean books cited thematic elements from the original Pinocchio, the terminator films, and even mentions the Daleks from Dr. Who. But the Promethean mechanics just drive home to point that they want to be frakenstien's monster that makes frankenstein's monster. Let the mechanics actually have something to do with the references in the actual book. In other word &quot;Pinocchio is neat, but he's not frankenstein's monster.&quot;<br /> 2. Pilgrimages that can end in something other then &quot;bang you're human&quot;. Original Robocop seems like a perfect match for a crazy pilgrimage that doesn't end in &quot;Murphy comes back&quot;. That's what i think when i think pilgrimage.<br /> 3. Better Disquiet explanation. Promethean section of Mortal Remains gets the &quot;show don't tell&quot; message across pretty well. Let's see more of that in the new book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T18:42:20-07:00","id":230803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230799#post230799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Pilgrimages that can end in something other then &quot;bang you're human&quot;. Original Robocop seems like a perfect match for a crazy pilgrimage that doesn't end in &quot;Murphy comes back&quot;. That's what i think when i think pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's the <i>entire point of the game</i>.<br /> <br /> Sorry transhumanists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T18:50:35-07:00","id":230807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230803#post230803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that's the <i>entire point of the game</i>.<br /> <br /> Sorry transhumanists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; the transhumanist thing is what <b>Mage</b> is about; <b>Promethean</b> is about humanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T18:55:06-07:00","id":230811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230807#post230807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; the transhumanist thing is what <b>Mage</b> is about; <b>Promethean</b> is about humanism.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a fairly good approximation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T18:56:28-07:00","id":230812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230803#post230803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that's the <i>entire point of the game</i>.<br /> <br /> Sorry transhumanists.</div> </div> </div> </div>i don't mean transhuman i meant not becoming a &quot;one human fits all&quot; redeemed template and actually making it a choice based upon the promethean and not simply &quot;i've completely forgotten i was monster! let's go celebrate by getting me turned into a different kind of monster!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T19:01:23-07:00","id":230816,"title":"","content":"I was pre-empting others with the second part.. The first is mainly what I had to say in response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T19:47:43-07:00","id":230888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230812#post230812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean transhuman i meant not becoming a &quot;one human fits all&quot; redeemed template and actually making it a choice based upon the promethean</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s what Athanors are for. That said, I\u2019d prefer that the \u201cfinal Azoth roll\u201d be recast as an extended action where the newly-Redeemed character struggles over several weeks to regain and integrate his memories of his former life as a Promethean (either directly or through the creation of \u201cmortal memories\u201d that approximate his former experiences); that way, <i>every</i> Redeemed spends some time early on with amnesia, and many (i.e., the ones who are unable to achieve sufficient successes before hitting the limit of how far an extended action can take you) end up as permanent amnesiacs \u2014 as opposed to the current system, where you\u2019re only in danger of permanent amnesia if you Redeem with Azoth 1\u20132 or so, and your amnesia is pretty much guaranteed to clear up in under a month (if you ever suffer any amnesia in the first place) if your final Azoth is much higher than that. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Exceptional Successes during this acclimation process should net you special rewards, whether or not you ever regain your memories. I\u2019ve described elsewhere my thoughts on what a <b>Hunter: the Vigil</b> Second Edition should be like, and it included some optional \u201cheroic mortal\u201d Edges designed to stay within the realm of \u201cbeing human\u201d while at the same time pushing the hunter toward being \u201ccream of the crop\u201d types; I think those same Edges (Boosts to attributes, skills, or advantages; new uses for Willpower; immunities to the likes of Lunacy, the Lie, and/or Disquiet; etc.) could work well as exceptional success \u201cbonuses\u201d for a Redeemed mortal\u2019s acclimation process. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d also consider allowing the acclimation process to do somethung similar to an Unchained patching together a Cover, but without the need to take bits of peoples\u2019 lives from them: when the Redeemed is done, he may not only have memories of a full mortal life (either replacing or in tandem with his Promethean memories); but the friends and neighbors that he remembers may well remember <i>him</i>, too. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230812#post230812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and not simply &quot;i've completely forgotten i was monster! let's go celebrate by getting me turned into a different kind of monster!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, anyone who thinks that \u201cget Embraced\u201d/\u201cAwaken\u201d/\u201cbecome a changeling\u201d/etc. is the logical next step for a Redeemed former-Promethean has pretty much missed the point of <b>Promethean</b>. Which is not to say that there\u2019s no place for such things; but even \u201cPromethean to mortal to mage\u201d should be played as something of a tragedy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T21:06:57-07:00","id":230964,"title":"","content":"Definitely more exploration of the possibilities of The Principle and Its agents.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't know what I'd do with Disquiet and Wasteland, but I'd do something. I know Prometheans are rare, but half the world should be a Wasteland by now.<br /> <br /> More crossover support. I've always thought Prometheans should actually be interested in supernatural groups and species; I'd think a useful of understanding what it is to be human is by seeing how vampires or mages AREN'T human, despite how they might look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T21:08:26-07:00","id":230965,"title":"","content":"Disquiet and Wasteland aren't getting toned down per se, but it's harder to hit the more extreme ends. The goal was to make it possible to have a PtC chronicle that <i>isn't</i> nomadic. <br /> <br /> There are now 10 Refinements. <br /> <br /> There are now 7 Lineages. <br /> <br /> Transmutations work a lot differently, but I really like how they work. <br /> <br /> And the Pilgrimage...well. There's more to it. You can hide in your Pilgrimage for quite a while...but if you're hiding, you're not progressing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T21:17:33-07:00","id":230973,"title":"","content":"Planning on starting with a bang*, are we? I approve.<br /> <br /> *er, bolt of lightning.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Question: Is there more of a &quot;ticking timer&quot; sort of approach to Disquiet and Wasteland mechanics, so to speak?(I want to compare it to Sekhem, but that's not a great parallel)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-17-2014, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T21:35:26-07:00","id":231000,"title":"","content":"Seven and ten, huh? Is the elemental organizing principle still in play for the seven Lineages, or are you using a different organizing principle now? (between the original five Lineages and the Zeka, I\u2019m only coming up with six; so (a) I\u2019ve overlooked one, (b) you\u2019re adding one, or (c) you\u2019re changing them around.) Likewise, I\u2019m coming up with ten Refinements between the six (including Centimani) in the core and the four in <b>Magnum Opus</b>; are those the ten, or are you changing things up? <br /> <br /> Transmutations would pretty much have to work differently; the old way was too dependant on the escalating cost structure. I hope that the new approach keeps the freedom to choose exactly which Transmutations you want instead of having to pick ones you aren\u2019t interested in to get to the ones you want. <br /> <br /> You can \u201chide in the Pilgrimage\u201d? What does that mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T21:42:40-07:00","id":231007,"title":"","content":"The Unfleshed have long been considered a Lineage...somewhere.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't surprise me if it was them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T22:44:09-07:00","id":231046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230965#post230965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Disquiet and Wasteland aren't getting toned down per se, but it's harder to hit the more extreme ends. The goal was to make it possible to have a PtC chronicle that <i>isn't</i> nomadic.</b><br /> <br /> There are now 10 Refinements.<br /> <br /> There are now 7 Lineages.<br /> <br /> Transmutations work a lot differently, but I really like how they work.<br /> <br /> And the Pilgrimage...well. There's more to it. You can hide in your Pilgrimage for quite a while...but if you're hiding, you're not progressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all great, but bolded especially is fantastic news. The core five Lineages plus Zeky and Unfleshed is 7, unless you don't count Unfleshed? As for Refinements, please include Plumbum; I always felt like that should've been in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T22:48:07-07:00","id":231054,"title":"","content":"More support for different modes of play. Nomadic is tops (what sort of Pilgrim never leaves home?), but so many people can't seem to get their head around the concept. Also, tips for how to build a chronicle for transients.<br /> <br /> Better systems for the Pilgrimage and all its hazards, ones that catalyze stories rather than forcing them.<br /> <br /> Thicker, more storied Refinements. <br /> <br /> Deeper ties to the &quot;Stolen Lives&quot; idea, that the body a Created inhabits has had a story all its own, one that might be ongoing.<br /> <br /> Stuff that has been toyed with <i>here</i>, on <i>this </i>forum. You have, like, <i>five </i>fans. Listen to us!<br /> <br /> More Pyros monsters. Weirder fucking Qashmallim encounters. Firestorms too, I guess, since that's the spark.<br /> <br /> A catalog of pre-statted mortals likely to make trouble for the Created: police, social workers, etc., and how they might do so.<br /> <br /> None of that God-Machine talk. The Pyros loves us, its children, and would never give us mortality just to feed us to the Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T23:08:42-07:00","id":231073,"title":"","content":"I don't think a <i>Promethean</i> book is the right place for it, but we'd better get something about the <i>qashmallim</i> in regards to the Machine. Between <i>Magnum Opus</i> calling The Principle &quot;a God-Machine&quot; and the <i>qashmallim</i> being in the <i>Demon </i>core, that has to come to a head at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T23:15:04-07:00","id":231079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=231073#post231073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Magnum Opus</i> calling The Principle &quot;a God-Machine&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's <i>Pandora's Book.</i> There's literally not a single occurrence of so much as the word &quot;machine&quot; in <i>Magnum Opus</i> outside of <i>To the Wastes.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T23:27:38-07:00","id":231092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=231079#post231079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's <i>Pandora's Book.</i> There's literally not a single occurrence of so much as the word &amp;quot;machine&amp;quot; in <i>Magnum Opus</i> outside of <i>To the Wastes.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, apologies. My brain categorized Promethean supplements as &quot;Saturnine Night was the one with the Zeky&quot; and &quot;books that were not Saturnine Night.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T00:13:56-07:00","id":231141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=231054#post231054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You have, like, <i>five </i>fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I object to that, I'm a fan! Six fans!<br /> <br /> Just because I have other interests as well, jeez.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T00:59:32-07:00","id":231179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=231000#post231000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can \u201chide in the Pilgrimage\u201d? What does that mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Insanity is doing the same thing over and over again.<br /> <br /> My guess is you're back tracking in terms of milestones in terms. Given the name of &quot;Firestorm&quot; and the concept that until recently, all the Chronicle books were named off their chief antagonist, I would say the Prommie is attempting to hide from the Divine Fire it's self.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T01:12:34-07:00","id":231187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230799#post230799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Pilgrimages that can end in something other then &quot;bang you're human&quot;. Original Robocop seems like a perfect match for a crazy pilgrimage that doesn't end in &quot;Murphy comes back&quot;. That's what i think when i think pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230803#post230803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that's the <i>entire point of the game</i>.<br /> <br /> Sorry transhumanists.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a conflict I feel here. On the one hand Promethian is a game about self-discovery. On the other hand it explicitly says that any self-discovery that doesn't result in human is wrong.<br /> <br /> Fortuantely it doesn't come up much. Just Grandfather Crow I think; it didn't feel right that a crow had to (edit: might have to) become human even when he didn't want to. An easy solution would be to have a policy of avoiding promethins who have a <u>good</u> reason to want to be something other than human; or to allow you to become regular animals, statues, trees, and various other things that aren't super-human but aren't human either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230888#post230888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, anyone who thinks that \u201cget Embraced\u201d/\u201cAwaken\u201d/\u201cbecome a changeling\u201d/etc. is the logical next step for a Redeemed former-Promethean has pretty much missed the point of <b>Promethean</b>. Which is not to say that there\u2019s no place for such things; but even \u201cPromethean to mortal to mage\u201d should be played as something of a tragedy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly agree with this. The only time I've ever seen a &quot;next step&quot; that I liked was the Reedemed Alchemist in the Waters of Life part of the sample chronicle, and he was very clearly human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T01:12:51-07:00","id":231188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=231000#post231000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can \u201chide in the Pilgrimage\u201d? What does that mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that one fiction piece about Israel Hands hiding in a cave for 60 years? He didn't get back on his Pilgrimage until that one bloody-handed <i>qashmallim</i> made him team up with Sister Stitch.<br /> <br /> *That* is hiding in the Pilgrimage; not making progress, not devolving, just sort of... stalling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T03:46:46-07:00","id":231265,"title":"","content":"*whines* *falls over* *hides in a cave*<br /> wake me up when it's out. i have nothing constructive to add. i want it to be super good. i'm sorry i try to be a constructive forum member but i can't deal with all this antici","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3204-crabbadon","name":"crabbadon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3204_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T04:09:53-07:00","id":231269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crabbadon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=231265#post231265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i can't deal with all this antici</div> </div> </div> </div>...pation?<br /> <br /> I echo the 'more support for different chronicles', the default nomad was limiting and offputting. Linked to that, I'm always championed Wastelands linked to Azoth, and can get on board with Wastelands linked to Pyros use. The idea of Wasteland, Disquiet and other Promethean weaknesses is to make games more interesting, to open up new options, not close them off and force players into a narrow route. I generally echo what Verge and my fellow superfans are saying.<br /> <br /> I want more Pandoran love, though. I adore Pandorans, I really do, but their dormancy (while essential and a bit part of their awesome factor) really limits them and makes the more interesting ones, like the Lady of Chains, seem rather implausible. I want their 'failed' nature to be put forward a little more, and possibly for Centimanni to become more like them the deeper they get involved in Flux. I want ways for them to get Pyros without running into one of the vanishing rare Created - not for all of them, just a few. I want more weird Pandorans, like my idea for dormant Pandorans quarried and used to build a house that comes alive when a Promethean enters. I could be convinced on letting a rare Pandoran start a two-part pilgrimage of its own - Pandoran to Promethean, Promethean to human.<br /> <br /> And I'd really like to see stats and artwork for the <i>Praecipitati,</i><br /> <br /> But above all else, I want the rules and writeup to make Promethean sound incredibly exciting and fun to play for more people. Yes, I want what Promethean has never achieved. MASS APPEAL. Maybe give them more fun lightning-blast powers and shapeshifting or something..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T06:29:09-07:00","id":231402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=231179#post231179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the name of &quot;Firestorm&quot; and the concept that until recently, all the Chronicle books were named off their chief antagonist</div> </div> </div> </div>Story catalyst, not antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T06:51:43-07:00","id":231422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230731#post230731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire subject is a touchy one that requires a lot of finnicking, but my instincts start here, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only argument I can see being made is that Disquiet makes it too difficult for the Created to learn and dwell among humans, thus hindering their Pilgrimmage. Wasteland, too, I suppose, but the mechanics have to be there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230965#post230965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disquiet and Wasteland aren't getting toned down per se, but it's harder to hit the more extreme ends. The goal was to make it possible to have a PtC chronicle that <i>isn't</i> nomadic.<br /> <br /> There are now 10 Refinements.<br /> <br /> There are now <b>7 Lineages</b>.<br /> <br /> Transmutations work a lot differently, but I really like how they work.<br /> <br /> And the Pilgrimage...well. There's more to it. You can hide in your Pilgrimage for quite a while...but if you're hiding, you're not progressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>omgoshomgoshomgosh! Also, I love Transmutations - several tiers but multiple powers at each tier that you pick and choose from","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T11:05:58-07:00","id":231717,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a better system for social gameplay. The Disquiet and Wasteland often got too many complaints to make it easy to enjoy, since loneliness is all too often a familiar topic for people with Depression, like myself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T20:57:31-07:00","id":232366,"title":"","content":"It feels disingenuous to say &quot;my Humanity rules&quot; (even though KR already said the same), but updated Humanity rules. The pilgrimage should be the &quot;Integrity&quot; stat, after all - when you go off it doing terrible things like feeding/making Pandorans, murder, and even Lacuna come easier, and gaining a sense of humanity by pursuing it is big - I modeled that with Breaking Points, but there may be a better way.<br /> <br /> Transmutations that feel like they change you - Pandoran Transmutations in monstrous ways, but even normal ones providing some kind of, you know, alteration to your base matter.<br /> <br /> What the King's Raven said, about Conditions that get resolved. I was never keen on losing neat powers as your Humanity goes up, but I do like the idea of higher Humanity meaning using your powers is a Breaking Point - and much like Demons, I think Prometheans could use some Conditions that continue to come back until something revolutionary (a Milestone, if you will) occurs.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, less Milestones and more player-controlled. Aspirations are great because they give the Storyteller a heads-up about what the players want their characters to do - something similar would be good (I probably made just such a system because I probably feel this way, but I think Milestones were really difficult to use comparatively).<br /> <br /> I'm really into little tweaks. Immunitiy to soul-loss because Prometheans don't have one yet; making it clear that Lacunae is as close as Prometheans can get to soul-loss; greater detail on how Prometheans view and interact with ghosts and spirits, or at least some core-book powers that actually support the Ulgan-as-shaman.<br /> Cleaning up the host of Merits that Prometheans get for-free and updating them is small, but crazy useful. An update to their injury/death mechanics (I like that Aggravted damage from Lethal begins to break down their bodies, but it can be a bit hard to track).<br /> <br /> I suppose I want a lot from it, but then again, it is my favorite nWoD line.<br /> I mean, I love B&amp;S as much as I love Masquerade (which is quite a lot). Promethean is just<br /> Too damn cool, though.<br /> <br /> I want it to be accessible overall, I suppose.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I always thought it should be &quot;Lead and Clay: The Pilgrimage Chronicle,&quot; but that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 08-18-2014, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T10:47:42-07:00","id":233018,"title":"","content":"In the past, my posts on this topic have always leaned towards flights of fancy, because I've never really believed it would happen. Yay to be wrong, and so to try to be a bit more realistic...<br /> <br /> 1. Resist any temptation/pressure to make it all mad science all the time. Sure it's all about obsessions and transgressions, but psychological, mystical, spiritual, and artistic ones should matter just as much.<br /> <br /> 2. Separate Tammuz and Golems. First reason: two of the extant Lineages are based around someone attempting to resurrect a dead loved one, but the tone of grief and loss - despite being a powerful lens to look at Prometheans - is not carried over into how either of them work.<br /> So I'd like to see the Tammuz, with the origin story presented in the first core book; but their Disquiet makes people look for their lost loved ones in the Tammuz and get angry when she doesn't live up to it, their Wasteland evokes emptiness and the grave, and their Torment makes them dwell on their own lossess.<br /> And the Golems - all constructs - made as slaves, and with much the same mechanics presented in the first core book.<br /> Hopefully, this is part of why there are seven instead of five; if not, hopefully Matt can be persuaded to make it eight.<br /> <br /> 3. The Wasteland should make Firestorms easier (unless it already does; I lost my copy of Pandora's Book, so I don't recall).<br /> <br /> 4. A collection of mortal encounters, with notes on how their personalities flavour their responses to Disquiet.<br /> <br /> 5. One chapter should be called the Burning World.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230709#post230709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity should start at 3 and build up from there. One of the Promethean\u2019s Aspirations should be replaced by a Purpose, which works the same way for the most part but represents the \u201cprogramming\u201d the Promethean was created with. The Purpose should also have a compulsory facet to it, which can be overcome using Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, except that &quot;programming&quot; shouldn't necessarily be chosen consciously by the Promethean's creator - instead it should arise out of their obsessions, or those of the demiurge (eg, Frankenstein's Monster so yearns for acceptance in part because Frankenstein was obsessed with the accolades he would receive as a creator of life).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Base Athanors on Refinements rather than Lineages/Humours. </div> </div> </div>Also agreed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:56:09-07:00","id":233102,"title":"","content":"I forgot my biggest one.<br /> <br /> Rename Torment; the reason being is that Torment should - IMO - be the default state of Promethians. The bad frenzy mechanic should be portrayed as something that's desirable yet ultimately self-destructive.<br /> <br /> Take the Golems; created to serve as slaves. Every day in which they are not slaving for a master is Torment. Deep down it feels wrong on a spirtual level, it might literally be wrong on a spitual level (twisting the Divine Fire to create beings who should be slaves on a spiritual level is the ultimate crime of the Golem's demurge). When a Golem gives in, that's not Torment. That's Release from the Torment, and it's also a bad idea for the Golem's long term development.<br /> <br /> <br /> [edit] When I said &quot;bad frenzy mechanic&quot; I mean &quot;morally-bad frenzy&quot; not &quot;bad-mechanic for frenzy&quot;. I believe &quot;oops&quot; is appropraite. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-18-2014, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:23:49-07:00","id":233560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230799#post230799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Pilgrimages that can end in something other then &quot;bang you're human&quot;. Original Robocop seems like a perfect match for a crazy pilgrimage that doesn't end in &quot;Murphy comes back&quot;. That's what i think when i think pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did somebody say my name?<br /> <br /> Super excited about Prommies 2.0! Can't wait for more spoilers!<br /> <br /> I'm actually kind of surprised that Lineages are going to be around for 2nd Ed. Echoing what Dataweaver said, I figured that they'd go away in favor of the Unfleshed/Custom Lineage rules, making each Promethean a more singular anomaly. Are those rules going to be part of 2e, by any chance?<br /> <br /> I'd like a lot more &quot;gray area&quot; with Promethean, particularly with the quashmallim. The Elpidos are the good guys because they help Prometheans, the Lillithim are bad... but I can't think of the concepts of distillation and change in terms of good or evil; they simply are. <br /> <br /> I'd also want a lot of inspiration taken from Fullmetal Alchemist et all. Scar and the Homonculi are excellent examples of what Prometheans can do, as are a few of the other characters who have been altered alchemically.<br /> <br /> And this sounds a little silly, sure, but I definitely want Transmutations where you can control detached body parts from a distance. Think Thing from the Addams Family, or any number of zombie films.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:25:17-07:00","id":233563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=233018#post233018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. One chapter should be called the Burning World.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read The League of Extraordinary Gentlemen: Black Dossier? The Blazing World depicted there is basically how I imagine the Aether looks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T14:44:30-07:00","id":234673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=233560#post233560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually kind of surprised that Lineages are going to be around for 2nd Ed. Echoing what Dataweaver said, I figured that they'd go away in favor of the Unfleshed/Custom Lineage rules, making each Promethean a more singular anomaly. Are those rules going to be part of 2e, by any chance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is this surprising? Lineage is a very apropo idea; for a long time, philosophers were assessed by their lineage of mentors. And, as there is a bodily &quot;passing of the torch&quot; between a Promethean and its offspring, Lineage has a solid basis, and connects the character to the progenitor of the line. It also creates a sense of culture and heritage among a collection of wastrels who cannot safely join or even form a society.<br /> <br /> As for singularity, that's fine and all, but it was said long ago, in a different game, that you have splats like these so new players have something to grab ahold of. Frankenstein, the golem, mummies are all archetypes that are easily seized upon, where DIY Unfleshed-style character creation might simply be bewildering, or, worse, a catalog of optimizeable powers. The same idea drives classes in D&amp;D, or Clans in Vampire. It's not something to be casually tossed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T16:15:00-07:00","id":234753,"title":"","content":"And FWIW, I never suggested doing away with Lineages. What I suggested was more along the lines of treating them as worked examples of a hypothetical Lineage design system, and some changes to the Generative Act that makes literal lineages more of a tendency than an absolute, akin to the way the Zeka may have had as many as eight Progenitors. I\u2019d still want a set of pre-built Lineages to be included for the reasons Verge outlined; just change the feel from \u201cthese seven are all that there are\u201d to \u201cthese are the most common Lineages, but not the only ones\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T16:28:59-07:00","id":234786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=233560#post233560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like a lot more &quot;gray area&quot; with Promethean, particularly with the quashmallim. The Elpidos are the good guys because they help Prometheans, the Lillithim are bad... but I can't think of the concepts of distillation and change in terms of good or evil; they simply are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve always been fond of the story in <b><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Pandora\u2019s Book</span></b> about a Lilithim who frees a Promethean who was being tortured and then sets about punishing his torturers. I\u2019d like more instances like this, where Lilithim are portrayed more like avenging angels and Elpidim sometimes bring <i>false</i> hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T17:07:13-07:00","id":234815,"title":"","content":"I think Promethean would benefit greatly from a &quot;Severed Lines&quot; section, talking about rumored and legendary Prometheans. I'd toss the Zeky and the Unfleshed here, as well as some sort of Fire precursor to the Wretched, and perhaps some Lineages with a stronger link to Chinese and Indian alchemies. Same with Refinements, though I've never been a fan of the alternates (Argentum, in the age of Beast, gains even more ill-gotten legitimacy...).<br /> <br /> Ooh, maybe some sort of treatise on how Lineage carries on into Mortality. Each Demiurge was seeking something specific in their Creations, and each New Dawn is the final perfection of that vision. Refinement clarifies certain aspects of humanity, but the rarity of some and the monstrosity of another means that they are ultimately disposable, as not all need to be followed. Stannum is meant to be abandoned, after all. What do these humours and Transmutations do to the newchanged mortal at the end of the Road?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:22:49-07:00","id":234867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=234815#post234815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Promethean would benefit greatly from a &amp;quot;Severed Lines&amp;quot; section, talking about rumored and legendary Prometheans. I'd toss the Zeky and the Unfleshed here, as well as some sort of Fire precursor to the Wretched, and perhaps some Lineages with a stronger link to Chinese and Indian alchemies. Same with Refinements, though I've never been a fan of the alternates (Argentum, in the age of Beast, gains even more ill-gotten legitimacy...).</div> </div> </div> </div>What: a set of Transmutations that lets you deal with Ephemeral Entities (and other supernatural creatures) is a problem? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=234815#post234815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, maybe some sort of treatise on how Lineage carries on into Mortality. Each Demiurge was seeking something specific in their Creations, and each New Dawn is the final perfection of that vision. Refinement clarifies certain aspects of humanity, but the rarity of some and the monstrosity of another means that they are ultimately disposable, as not all need to be followed. Stannum is meant to be abandoned, after all. What do these humours and Transmutations do to the newchanged mortal at the end of the Road?</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I checked, \u201cwhat you carry over from your Pilgrimage into the New Dawn\u201d is what Athanors are all about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:37:31-07:00","id":234880,"title":"","content":"Change the refinements. They should be something like Demon's cipher, some personal and meaningful and unique, not a prepackaged y-splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1266,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","user":"SirPants","date":". 08-19-2014, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:49:48-07:00","id":234898,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d prefer more \u201cdo it yourself\u201d support across the board (it\u2019s about the Created, after all; there should be room for innovation in creating something); but Athanors in particular should indeed be intensely personal. I don\u2019t have a problem with Refinements representing broad fields of study, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-19-2014, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T04:08:59-07:00","id":235290,"title":"","content":"Matt hasn't given us clearance to say anything yet, but the writing team is well aware of the concerns brought up in this thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:12:33-07:00","id":235524,"title":"","content":"Having struggled with this game, which I absolutely ADORE, I see the following as hacks that I've wanted to implement if possible (and note, some have been covered here already):<br /> <br /> <b>Disquiet and Wasteland as scalable effects</b> would make a nice compromise between the factions saying 'they're too harsh' and 'they're not harsh enough.' By this I mean that any troupe ought to have options for how these effects work in the game, and possibly ideas for how these effects can wax and wane through a chronicle rather than just a one-size-fits-all approach from the core book.<br /> <br /> <b>Decouple Humour from Lineage</b> challenges some of the base assumptions of the game, but I feel that it could work to allow for greater variety. This hack \u2013 the one I've put the most work into, but still not a lot \u2013 keeps each Lineage having a 'preferred' Humour, but it also becomes possible to play a Melancholic Muse or a Sanguine Frankenstein. Mind you, this is likely a moot point with seven Lineages in <b>Promethean</b> 2d edition, but it plays into my third idea...<br /> <br /> <b>Let Humuor affect Refinements</b> in a way that gives Humour much more vitality AND forces a character to really think about the Refinements she pursues. I see Humour as an unchanging Trait, but unlike Lineage, it demands some choice \u2013 on the part of the character's creator rather than the character herself. Anyway, I believe that a Sanguine character would approach each Refinement differently than an Ectoplasmic one might. Again, this could be a moot point in light of the ten Refinements we'll see.<br /> <br /> ...As stated by others, I'm so very much looking forward to whatever comes out in this book. Unlike the 2d editions of other games, I do believe that <b>Promethean</b> deserves a serious overhaul, brilliant as it already is!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T14:20:47-07:00","id":235757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=234867#post234867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What: a set of Transmutations that lets you deal with Ephemeral Entities (and other supernatural creatures) is a problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. You could say this is the &quot;what humanity is not&quot; path, but we have that with Plumbum. This is a whole splat that's about futzing about with other supernaturals. Even in a crossover campaign that's a bit much. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Last I checked, \u201cwhat you carry over from your Pilgrimage into the New Dawn\u201d is what Athanors are all about. </div> </div> </div>That's simply mechanics carryover. It's a cultivated, repeatable, tangible game object, which is cool, but it's not insight into the makeup of the new being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T15:33:51-07:00","id":235788,"title":"","content":"Plumbum isn\u2019t \u201cwhat Humanity is not\u201d any more than Mercurium is: the former delves specifically into Promethean nature; the latter deals with the nature of Pyros. Yes, Argentum is something of a grab-bag; and yes, that grab-bag includes other gamelines should you decide to use them \u2014 that\u2019s inherent in its focus on \u201csupernatural phenomena that <i>aren\u2019t</i> related to Prometheans\u201d. And I phrased it the way I did intentionally: since spirits and ghosts aren\u2019t Pyros-based phenomena, they\u2019re outside the scope of the other Refinements; but they\u2019re <i>exactly</i> the sort of thing that Argentum was made to deal with. You don\u2019t need crossovers to make Argentum useful in a <b>Promethean</b> game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T17:56:00-07:00","id":235974,"title":"","content":"The overly simple version:<br /> <br /> Centimani is about the Monstrous Condition.<br /> Plumbum is about the Promethean Condition.<br /> Stannum is about Torment.<br /> Ferrum is about Humans biologically,as well as the role of warriors within society.<br /> Argentum is about the Supernatural Conditions.<br /> Cuprum is about Nature and man's harmony/disharmony with it.<br /> Mercurius is about Pyros.<br /> Aurum is about Humans sociologically and their relations to each other.<br /> <br /> That's the really, <i>really </i>dumbed down version. To the point I wonder how useful it is.<br /> <br /> (yes, I know I left out Aes and Cobalus)<br /> <br /> EDIT: The point I forgot! All of them are used to inform the human condition directly. They're lens to view humanity though. Centimani is the closest to not doing that, and i<i>t still does it.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-20-2014, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T18:13:29-07:00","id":236006,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting that, as written, Argentum also takes the position that there\u2019s a connection between the supernatural and madness. I wouldn\u2019t mind PtC 2.0 playing that up a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T21:08:30-07:00","id":236158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=234673#post234673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for singularity, that's fine and all, but it was said long ago, in a different game, that you have splats like these so new players have something to grab ahold of. Frankenstein, the golem, mummies are all archetypes that are easily seized upon, where DIY Unfleshed-style character creation might simply be bewildering, or, worse, a catalog of optimizeable powers. The same idea drives classes in D&amp;D, or Clans in Vampire. It's not something to be casually tossed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly understand that point; if absolutely everything's custom from the ground up, the sandbox gets too big and suddenly people aren't necessarily playing by the same rules. I didn't mean &quot;Prometheans don't need an x-axis&quot;, but I thought that the x-axis could be something else that involved more of the Unfleshed and Construct stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=234753#post234753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And FWIW, I never suggested doing away with Lineages. What I suggested was more along the lines of treating them as worked examples of a hypothetical Lineage design system, and some changes to the Generative Act that makes literal lineages more of a tendency than an absolute, akin to the way the Zeka may have had as many as eight Progenitors. I\u2019d still want a set of pre-built Lineages to be included for the reasons Verge outlined; just change the feel from \u201cthese seven are all that there are\u201d to \u201cthese are the most common Lineages, but not the only ones\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>My misinterpretation -- sorry. I like this idea though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T21:22:17-07:00","id":236162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=235524#post235524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Decouple Humour from Lineage</b> challenges some of the base assumptions of the game, but I feel that it could work to allow for greater variety. This hack \u2013 the one I've put the most work into, but still not a lot \u2013 keeps each Lineage having a 'preferred' Humour, but it also becomes possible to play a Melancholic Muse or a Sanguine Frankenstein. Mind you, this is likely a moot point with seven Lineages in <b>Promethean</b> 2d edition, but it plays into my third idea...<br /> <br /> <b>Let Humuor affect Refinements</b> in a way that gives Humour much more vitality AND forces a character to really think about the Refinements she pursues. I see Humour as an unchanging Trait, but unlike Lineage, it demands some choice \u2013 on the part of the character's creator rather than the character herself. Anyway, I believe that a Sanguine character would approach each Refinement differently than an Ectoplasmic one might. Again, this could be a moot point in light of the ten Refinements we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely like the idea of Humours taking a larger role. I kind of think they have more in common with Refinements, too. Perhaps they could be a sort &quot;fluid philosophy&quot; where the Refinement you follow causes that particular substance to surge dominate your body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T22:27:52-07:00","id":236193,"title":"","content":"Mmm, no; not really. The Humours are based off of real-world (outdated) theories about how humours influence one\u2019s temperament \u2014 even today, such things as \u201cENTJ/ISFP/etc.\u201d personality sorters address the same sorts of observed \u201cpersonality types\u201d that the theory of humours was concocted to explain, albeit with different explanations. <br /> <br /> Granted, the aforementioned theory had <i>four</i> Humours rather than <i>seven</i>; still, four of the original five Lineages were clearly designed with the <a href=\"http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_temperaments\" target=\"_blank\">four Temperaments</a> in mind: compare the Frankensteins, Galeteids, Osirans, and Tammuz to the Choleric, Sanguine, Phlegmatic, and Melancholic Temperaments on the linked page, and you\u2019ll notice really strong parallels. The fifth of the original Lineages was based on an explicitly inhuman Humour (Ectoplasm); and the Zeka Humour was defined less in terms of the humour itself and more by the fact that it had been contaminated by radiation. <br /> <br /> These Temperaments are, per the theory, inborn inclinations of one\u2019s personality: one doesn\u2019t <i>choose</i> to be Choleric or Melancholic; one is born with those inclinations, and then either embraces them or fights them. Refinements, OTOH, are fields of study; they represent what you think you need to learn about in order to become more human \u2014 which is why I think that Athanors should be Refinement-based rather than Lineage- or Humour-based, as an Athanor represents what you want to get out of the New Dawn. Lineages or Humours represent where you started; Athanors represent your intended destination; and Refinements represent the route you\u2019re taking to get there. So yes, Humour influences how you express your Refinement; but it does so in the same way that, say, a vampire\u2019s Clan influences how he approaches his Covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T22:47:45-07:00","id":236208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=235788#post235788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plumbum isn\u2019t \u201cwhat Humanity is not\u201d any more than Mercurium is: the former delves specifically into Promethean nature; the latter deals with the nature of Pyros. Yes, Argentum is something of a grab-bag; and yes, that grab-bag includes other gamelines should you decide to use them \u2014 that\u2019s inherent in its focus on \u201csupernatural phenomena that <i>aren\u2019t</i> related to Prometheans\u201d. And I phrased it the way I did intentionally: since spirits and ghosts aren\u2019t Pyros-based phenomena, they\u2019re outside the scope of the other Refinements; but they\u2019re <i>exactly</i> the sort of thing that Argentum was made to deal with. You don\u2019t need crossovers to make Argentum useful in a <b>Promethean</b> game.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm driving at is that the other supernaturals have no direct relevance to the Pilgrimage. Ghosts do, of course, but spirits much less so. While there's plenty of thematic overlap, that's a creative-level connection, untied to the presented assumptions of the Pyros and the Pilgrimage. Mana, Vitae, Plasm, Aether, what-have-you are not components of the mortal soul nor the Pyros, and have been largely opaque to one another, in that the realities of one game aren't universal to them all.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, it's gratuitous. Argentum exists primarily to facilitate crossover chronicles, and while there's nothing wrong with that, it's not much different than Mage adding a Monster Arcanum to smooth over the differences. You also have the issue of whether or not the ST can and should accommodate Spiritus purchases for supernaturals of the sort she would not otherwise include, or give away plot points to forestall a useless power being purchased. If we were just talking ghosts and spirits, there already exist rules for dealing with them without resort to specialized Transmutations. If we were just looking at crossovers, the primary difficulty is Disquiet, which could be addressed holistically with a revamp to those rules. I'm not against Argentum existing, or even Spiritus, but I see the introduction of the various and sundry mysteries that even a single other-splat adds as muddying the waters. Great for a chronicle, but misguided for character mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T23:11:38-07:00","id":236217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=236208#post236208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm driving at is that the other supernaturals have no direct relevance to the Pilgrimage. Ghosts do, of course, but spirits much less so. While there's plenty of thematic overlap, that's a creative-level connection, untied to the presented assumptions of the Pyros and the Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a good reason for spirit stuff: exploring what amounts to the collective unconscious of humanity (the Shadow), isn't exactly unenlightening about the nature of humanity itself. It would not be difficult to misinterpret, of course, but you could say that for any other Refinement, even Aurum.<br /> <br /> That's not an argument for Argentum, though. There's a weird line between <i>Promethean</i> being able to reflect itself back on us players, and Prometheans existing in the World of Darkness. Argentum makes a lot more sense in the latter case than the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T23:53:20-07:00","id":236233,"title":"","content":"One word: spirits. Rules for them are provided in the <b>Promethean</b> core book; they\u2019re very important to the Ulgans; and aside from Spiritus Transmutations and the tools available to everyone, the only tool Prometheans have for dealing with them is the Ulgan Bestowment. If you want to use Argentum without reference to crossovers, you can focus on spirits. Indeed, it\u2019s mentioned that Ulgans are the most likely to pursue this Refinement. As for the Spiritus Transmutations, there are only a handful that <i>aren\u2019t</i> useful when the Mystic focuses his attention on spirits: Mask/Cloak/Sense of [type], and Glimpse of Mortal Memory (that last one only because spirits were never human, and thus have no memories of being human). <br /> <br /> I also hope that the second edition of the World of Darkness core book will include something akin to <b>Mortal Remains</b>\u2019 monster creation rules, with a focus on creating monsters that <i>aren\u2019t</i> covered by other gamelines. If this happens, then Argentum becomes even more viable, since it will drastically increase the scope of non-Pyros supernatural creatures that the Storyteller will easily be able to bring to bear without resorting to crossover. <br /> <br /> There\u2019s also a lot of talk in the Argentum writeup about how mortals who interact with the supernatural tend to come back a bit worse for the wear, mentally; I\u2019d like to see something more done with this, though I\u2019m not quiite sure what. Maybe Disquietus rather than Sensoruim should be associated with Argentum, and tweaked to deal more with supernaturally induced madness in general rather than with the effects of Disquiet in particular? <br /> <br /> Argentum doesn\u2019t need an overhaul; just some refocusing to make its non-crossover uses more prominent, with its crossover uses being more of a side benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T15:54:19-07:00","id":237027,"title":"","content":"Especially given the side-bar in their section, I kinda thought the whole point of Argentum was to over crossover-overload. I understand some Sensorium transmutations fit, but I do like your idea of putting in Disquietism instead","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T09:43:24-07:00","id":237081,"title":"","content":"I just listened to the Gen Con panel and got some new info: seven lineages (original five plus Unfleshed and Extempore), 10 refinements (existing + Refinement of Phosphorous), transmutations take influence from Demon powers and you can take a Condition instead of having your disfigurements show, Prague is one of the city's getting covered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T09:47:59-07:00","id":237087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=237081#post237081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Prague is one of the city's getting covered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it is!<br /> <br /> The Demon powers sounds perfect - the innate, 'free' powers and some that cost Pyros works well for Promethean, IMO, especially with Pyros being (at least under the old rules) slow to charge (unless you get a certain horribly broken Transmutation...)<br /> <br /> No love for zeky, though? Shame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T09:52:08-07:00","id":237091,"title":"","content":"Zeky are one of my favorites, but I can see why they wouldn't include the walking cancer spreaders in a Promethean that seems to be more focused on accessability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T09:58:11-07:00","id":237098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=237081#post237081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just listened to the Gen Con panel and got some new info: seven lineages (original five plus Unfleshed and Extempore)</div> </div> </div> </div> I wonder how they're going to handle like Unfleshed and Extempore - they're not lineages; rather a term applied to a large number of unrelated linages.<br /> <br /> The Unfleshed even came with lineage design mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T13:53:23-07:00","id":237292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=237091#post237091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zeky are one of my favorites, but I can see why they wouldn't include the walking cancer spreaders in a Promethean that seems to be more focused on accessability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, but they're a fun sci-fi part of the game and if we're getting Unfleshed support, I'd like some Zeka. But as long as they're still a setting element I'll be happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T14:13:24-07:00","id":237325,"title":"","content":"I think we overlooked something far more important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=237081#post237081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10 refinements (existing + Refinement of Phosphorous),</div> </div> </div> </div> There are already 10 refinements. Did Matt misspeak, not count the Hundred Handed, or is something happening to the Freaks?<br /> <br /> Admitedly, I'd like it if the Hundred Handed were explicitly not a refinement - but what you get when you abandon the pilgrimage.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T14:20:14-07:00","id":237355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=237081#post237081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just listened to the Gen Con panel and got some new info:</div> </div> </div> </div>Help a brother out with a link? Much obliged!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T15:33:56-07:00","id":237466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=237355#post237355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Help a brother out with a link? Much obliged!</div> </div> </div> </div> It's an episdode of Geeks Out After Dark?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T20:28:25-07:00","id":237661,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised to see the Extempore, though there's an implication there that I like -- that Lineages may end up being much more free-form, with room to customize. Certainly, the Extempore need a <i>lot</i> of customization if they work anything like how they were presented in <b>Magnum Opus</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T20:45:32-07:00","id":237690,"title":"","content":"For the Unfleshed, I very much like an offhand comment that I remember hearing about one of the bits of fiction in <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b>: that one of the characters was &quot;an Unfleshed Galeteid&quot;. I <i>really</i> would rather <i>Unfleshed</i> and <i>Construct</i> be &quot;lenses&quot; that can be applied to Lineages, modifying the way they work to represent variants of the Promethean who aren't made of flesh and blood, with Lineages being more fundamentally about things like temperament and purpose than construction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T21:09:54-07:00","id":237742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=237690#post237690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Unfleshed, I very much like an offhand comment that I remember hearing about one of the bits of fiction in <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b>: that one of the characters was &quot;an Unfleshed Galeteid&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of which, do we know if Wood's on the writing team for Firestorm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T21:14:47-07:00","id":237745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=237742#post237742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, do we know if Wood's on the writing team for Firestorm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dear gods among men, I hope so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T07:41:18-07:00","id":238183,"title":"","content":"A completely unhelpful request:<br /> <br /> At the moment Promethean has a reputation as pretty much as the greatest game no one plays. For some reason Promethean is great to read, think about, and potentially ST for but not actually <i>play</i>. I'd like that fixed.<br /> <br /> As for the whole humanist thing. Its really hard to pull off in a way thats evocative for players. Its also ind of hard to handle as an ST. What happens when one player finishes their pilgrimage, but no one else does? Is it basically character death? Likewise, if you're gradually dialing up the tension and conflict in a story you reach a point where becoming human doesn't make the uber and horrifying issues you are facing <i>go away</i>, it just breaks your own kneecaps.<br /> <br /> I get that its the point of the game. As an ST I like that focus. As a player, I can understand being frustrated by it. How to handle this needs to be spelled out very clearly, possibly in the ST section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T13:29:58-07:00","id":238467,"title":"","content":"<b>Two Thoughts</b>:<br /> <br /> &lt;&gt; This has been stated before, but worth reiterating: <u>more variety in the possible ways to play the game</u>. As it is, Promethean 1.0 was geared rather heavily towards a specific style of gameplay (nomadic, antisocial, geared towards becoming human), and the mechanics (Wasteland, Disquiet, and the Pilgrimage) made it rather difficult to play anything else without chopping entire parts of the game out. Basically, I want to be able to run Prometheans as being able to do more stuff. I want it to be possible to have a social-focused Promethean who impersonates a human long-term, Prometheans who stay in a city for the duration of a game, Prometheans who have goals other than becoming human. Relatedly, support for Prometheans in a crossover game (seriously, Spiritus was the best crossover power set of any game, follow up on this!)<br /> <br /> &lt;&gt; Tone down the philosophy and provide a simpler hook. Promethean has a strong reputation, mentioned above, as 'the greatest game no one plays', and I think a part of that is because 'you are an unwanted abomination that's wandering the world trying to become human' is a more difficult sell than 'you're a wizard screwing around with reality' or 'you're a vampire playing politics with other vampires'. It's erudite, it's esoteric, it's quite beautiful... but it does not make it easy to convince players to try it. Right now Promethean is sort of the game that appeals to Lit Majors and no one else. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T13:53:29-07:00","id":238472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=238467#post238467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &lt;&gt; Tone down the philosophy and provide a simpler hook. Promethean has a strong reputation, mentioned above, as 'the greatest game no one plays', and I think a part of that is because 'you are an unwanted abomination that's wandering the world trying to become human' is a more difficult sell than 'you're a wizard screwing around with reality' or 'you're a vampire playing politics with other vampires'. It's erudite, it's esoteric, it's quite beautiful... but it does not make it easy to convince players to try it. Right now Promethean is sort of the game that appeals to Lit Majors and no one else.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>[Insert sound of alarm blaring]<br /> <br /> NO! NO! NO! NO! NO!<br /> Sorry, but anything short of a verbal exclamation fails to adequately express how strongly I disagree with this point. Prometheans unique selling point is the rather outlandish philosophy, and taking that away in the name of appealing to a wider audience is perhaps a good marketing decision, but its not the kind of decisions that we as the consumers should ask for. Its like telling Hollywood to make more stupid low-brow Micheal Bay-esque movies instead of another Watchmen/Sin City. You're telling telling them to dumb-down the game in an effort to appeal to the lowest common denominator, and I cannot for the life of me understand why, nor do I agree with any arguement that might convievably be put forth in the defence of the point.<br /> I know I am comming off terribly hostile and I am genuinly sorry for that. I dont mean to offend you, I just stand in very very strong disagreement to what you wrote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T14:27:00-07:00","id":238529,"title":"","content":"As a Wraith fan, I have intense sympathy for everyone who loves Promethean fir the themes that make it &quot;unplayable.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T20:24:36-07:00","id":238824,"title":"","content":"I think this is one of those times when people aren't asking for what they really want. The issue with Promethean isn't that it has a lot of high brow philisophical undertones, or that it approaches the question of what it means to be human. Do people really want <i>less</i> depth to their game? Eh. Maybe, but I'd wager no.<br /> <br /> The issue, I feel is that Promethean forgets the medium in which that philosophy is presented. Pen and paper games are an interactive media meant to be played by joining the thoughts and ideas of people in a guided conversation where mechanics govern the resolution of ideas. I can think of <i>no better</i> context to wrestle with the question of &quot;what does it mean to be human?&quot; than in a game whose nuts and bolts are literally made of the people who play it. Yet, Promethean 1E <i>feels</i> like its bothered and held back by being a game when really, being a fun game is the best advantage it has over just being a book.<br /> <br /> I don't want the philosophy to go away. I want the developers at every point to say, &quot;How can being a great game inform the rumination and execution of this philosophical struggle?&quot; and &quot;How can we make this struggle accessible and fun for the average player?&quot; I feel that saying that a game must be &quot;unplayable&quot; or &quot;unfun&quot; to express the concept of being humanity is a particularly bad brand of cynicism and irony that doesn't make for a good business model (or philosophical debate, for that matter). Any enjoyment Promethean can provide by being a great collection of philosophical ideas pales in comparison to the amount of joy it can bring by being a great collection of philosophical journeys to be shared by the group.<br /> <br /> I get it.<br /> You don't want to tone down the philosophy.<br /> We want that philosophy to be more accessible and more satisfying.<br /> <br /> When your content is literally &quot;people&quot; implicitly denying access to people actually undermines your own philosophical pursuits. Thankfully, these ideas are not actually mutually exclusive, and I trust the devs to deliver a great philosophical dialogue that is also fun and accessible.<br /> <br /> tl;dr. I want to have my cake and eat it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T21:27:57-07:00","id":238836,"title":"","content":"Disquiet and Wastelands are the major mechanical enforcers of Promethean's themes and also the mechanics that make it &quot;unplayable.&quot; Change them to satisfy those people and the game's themes suffer. It's like folks who complain about the myriad things that make Wraith &quot;unfun;&quot; the things those rules enforce are what make the game such a gem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T21:36:49-07:00","id":238841,"title":"","content":"People who say the game is unplayable, or unfun, because of Disquiet being a constant obstacle are missing the point. Disquiet is the tension between the Created and the Born. I never hear anyone complain that Vampire is unfun because of the Masquerade busting their balls, or the constant need to feed getting in the way of being playable. Granted, Promethean Curses are unwieldy, tedious, and distracting, but, hey, Paradox can be, too. A good ST will break the rules to get the game she wants, and that is true of any RPG out there.<br /> <br /> People ought to keep in mind that Promethean is about small victories, not small defeats. Vampire is about small defeats mounting up, forcing characters further and further from their humanity. Promethean is about walking softly and finding something worthy in the worst of your tormentors. That does take a pretty big change in perspective, but if a person <i>won't</i> even attempt that, well, I doubt they're in this hobby.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Wraith fan, I have intense sympathy for everyone who loves Promethean fir the themes that make it &quot;unplayable.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, watch how strident I get when Wr20 kicks out. Now <i>that </i>game is damn near unplayable, and will get every penny I can afford, is how good it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T21:57:46-07:00","id":238849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=238836#post238836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disquiet and Wastelands are the major mechanical enforcers of Promethean's themes and also the mechanics that make it &quot;unplayable.&quot; Change them to satisfy those people and the game's themes suffer. It's like folks who complain about the myriad things that make Wraith &quot;unfun;&quot; the things those rules enforce are what make the game such a gem.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's been identified as a problem, then do something new/interesting/different or handle it in a better way. It's not &quot;do it this way or nuke it.&quot; Its &quot;find something that works. If the past helps, use it. If it doesn't, go in a new direction.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T22:15:45-07:00","id":238857,"title":"","content":"I'll start by saying that I have never actually played Promethean nor really had the time to properly read through it. Despite this the idea of playing the Creature from Frankenstein is just too enticing, too inviting to ignore. It's the line I have long contemplated on buying physical copies of even before the GMC which was what made nWoD mechanics into something I can tolerate, that is to say finally I can play nWoD games without converting them to cWoD rules. So naturally I postponed, again, Promethean on my shopping list and am glad I did since it does get it's own Chronicle book which is awesome.<br /> <br /> Now to the actual meat of my post.<br /> <br /> While I do understand that Prometheans idea is about becoming human it is not what Frankenstein, or the Creature, was really about. The Creature wanted to be human so that he could have friends, not be feared and to not look as horrid as it did, it was never about literally becoming human it was more about companionship for the Creature, and about crossing lines that should not be crossed for Victor himself, than about becoming something else. It was also pretty clear that such a thing would not really be possible for it to achieve, companionship perhaps someday but not any sort of change towards being human, from the Creatures point of view it's much more about trying to accept that which it is than about trying to become something else. This leads me to wandering why exactly is Prometheans theme about becoming human instead of trying to come to accept that which one is. The story about the Creature Frankenstein created should not be about it changing to be something else it should be about it coming to terms with what it is.<br /> <br /> As for the Pinocchio reference that story is about becoming something else altogether but it is that from the very beginning, also he is not a creation of folly from a man lost in his hubris but a labor of love from one who never wished for the actual doll to live but was longing for a child of his own. Pinocchio's life did not come from his creator but as a gift from another being that breathed life unto him with the express purpose of changing him into a real boy after certain conditions had been met, it's a totally different themed story than that of Victor and the Creature. Which is why I do not understand why the Creature must give up it's own themes to follow those of Pinocchio, if both stories must be told within the same game why not just make both themes achievable. Why should the become human be the end all of what stories you can tell with Promethean? Why should there be only one possible end game there? Why is changing one self preferable to accepting one self?<br /> <br /> As a final note I must say I like the idea behind Disquiet and Wasteland and would not want them to change as I just love the idea that a Prometheans prolonged residency somewhere could slowly turn that quiet little city into Silent Hill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T23:08:22-07:00","id":238901,"title":"","content":"Promethean is a game where both can happen. They aren't mutually exclusive themes. The Creature wants to be accepted, but is rejected at every turn by everyone, and turns to vengeance. Pinocchio wants to be a real boy. Neither, I might point out, is about accepting one's self, and neither is Promethean. This is the story of the perfect human made to fulfill an impossible ideal, only to be tainted by its artifice. This is the Creature and its children, yes, but it's also Galatea made real to love Pygmalion, only to crush him in her arms. This is the Golem, maddened in its slavery and affront to God, rampaging through Prague. This is the Mummy, raised from the dead to reign over a kingdom lost to time. This is the story of all of these monsters, alive through blasphemous rituals, seeking to undo their original sin, and to forge a soul on the altar of ordeal.<br /> <br /> Prometheans are driven by forces internal and external to seek Mortality. Succor and rest are denied them as a result of their condition. Angels hound and guide them. The very experience of humanity changes them, bringing Pyros and Vitriol. They can resist, or turn from the path, but their lack of souls torment them as much as their lack of acceptance, and if they fail to be reborn with a soul, they will die without a soul, and everything they ever were dies forgotten with them. That's not easy for any of them to simply accept, not when a better way surrounds and tantalizes them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T00:36:23-07:00","id":238932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=238849#post238849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that's been identified as a problem, then do something new/interesting/different or handle it in a better way. It's not &quot;do it this way or nuke it.&quot; Its &quot;find something that works. If the past helps, use it. If it doesn't, go in a new direction.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>They are. It's post 20 of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T10:27:10-07:00","id":239311,"title":"","content":"I must agree with why Disquiet and Wasteland are the way they are, as Promethean I see as... a really frustrating struggle to try and get a goal that will frequently seem impossible. Additionally, its a plight that can be extremely relatable, whether its being rejected solely for being a foreigner, or for being different in some other manner than society will accept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T13:19:46-07:00","id":239521,"title":"","content":"*shrug* I'm not particularly offended, Krobeles, though I think SoulGambit has grasped my intent better. <br /> <br /> Sort of... putting it as a choice between philosophy and Lowest Common Denominator pandering is a false binary. It's not like Promethean is the only White Wolf game that has philosophical brooding in it. Look at Vampire, look at Changeling. They have profoundly philosophical elements integrated into the game and into the system (look at <i>Clanbook: Mekhet</i> for an example), but they also have better, shall we say, 'hooks' to draw people in, and they do so in a way that doesn't limit play versatility as starkly as Promethean does.<br /> <br /> So, I'll take a step back. Not necessarily 'tone down' the philosophy, but integrate it better, make it less obtrusive, and come up with a better way of selling it. Better?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T17:52:16-07:00","id":239732,"title":"","content":"Yeah, better.<br /> <br /> I think we can agree that Promethean needs to be more playable and provide a little more appeal beyond the festival of depression it currently is. &quot;Tone down the philosophy&quot; is just really, really the wrong way to frame that, though; there's no meaningful game design decision that statement leads to. Especially since what you're really asking for is <i>more</i> philosophy, not less. The Spring Court in addition to the Winter Court, to draw a metaphor.<br /> <br /> It's probably worth asking what kinds of gameplay you want to be possible in Promethean. I get that you want more, but more of what?<br /> <br /> I personally have trouble seeing how Promethean could be played in a throng; it feels aimed towards a two-person high-trust ST-player game. You can see that in the y-splat, for instance: Refinements are intensely personal, as opposed to the organizational structure of pretty much every other y-splat. It would be nice to have better social support, but I don't know how to achieve that or what it'd look like.<br /> <br /> I'd like to keep the &quot;every character is trying to become human&quot; angle, but I'd be open to having a perspective that regarded &quot;human&quot; as something as constructed as the Prometheans themselves are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T18:01:20-07:00","id":239741,"title":"","content":"I can't believe this hasn't been brought up already: I want demiurges and alchemists to have a much larger impact, preferably as potential antagonists. Each Promethean is effectively a walking talking Philosopher's Stone, and thus they must have a metric ton of uses for alchemists and not just as study. I want there to be secret societies that require a Wretched's liver as their bile is extra toxic, or military wings that use Promethean limbs to make super soldiers (a la chimerae in Fullmetal Alchemist).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T18:03:43-07:00","id":239746,"title":"","content":"On the minor end of things, I'd like to see a little more of the spiritual trappings of alchemy show up, if only because it makes for a nice bridging point (and contrast) between the Ulgans and the Ophidians and helps to illustrate a little more clearly why the line has generally presented the Ulgans as dealing with spirits over ghosts.<br /> <br /> Besides which, Paracelsian elementals are neat but rather outside the headspace of the qashmallim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T22:15:19-07:00","id":239925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=239741#post239741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't believe this hasn't been brought up already: I want demiurges and alchemists to have a much larger impact, preferably as potential antagonists. Each Promethean is effectively a walking talking Philosopher's Stone, and thus they must have a metric ton of uses for alchemists and not just as study. I want there to be secret societies that require a Wretched's liver as their bile is extra toxic, or military wings that use Promethean limbs to make super soldiers (a la chimerae in Fullmetal Alchemist).</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. Maybe an appendix with &quot;true alchemists&quot; alongside clones and what-not, with some playable Merits, like B&amp;S's mortals appendix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T23:39:54-07:00","id":239965,"title":"","content":"Actually, since prometheans are the embodiment of alchemy rather than the source of it, there ought to be stuff about nonpromethean alchemy, perhaps even as natural phenomena: like lakes with healing properties, forests that don't burn, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Not saying that an alchemist shouldn't be able to use prometheans for their personal use, but since pyros is a natural force they shouldn't have to.<br /> <br /> Another thing I'd like them to include is higher technology, they have transgenic clones and three law compliant robots already, they ought to go ahead and open that pandora's box and show what kind of high tech secrets are hiding in the world of darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T23:44:58-07:00","id":239967,"title":"","content":"Doesn't Promethean generally portray Pyros as being <i>unnatural</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T23:49:38-07:00","id":239970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=239741#post239741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't believe this hasn't been brought up already: I want demiurges and alchemists to have a much larger impact, preferably as potential antagonists. Each Promethean is effectively a walking talking Philosopher's Stone, and thus they must have a metric ton of uses for alchemists and not just as study. I want there to be secret societies that require a Wretched's liver as their bile is extra toxic, or military wings that use Promethean limbs to make super soldiers (a la chimerae in Fullmetal Alchemist).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thirded.<br /> <br /> I want secret societies of gentlemen alchemists, eager to milk Prometheans for precious Vitriol. I want Demurges mad with inspiration creating ever more alien abominations. I want <b>deliberate</b> mortal antagonists, who persecute and pursue Prometheans for reasons other than disquiet. Antagonists who starkly mirror to the Promethean's own pilgrimage with their selfish quest to transcend humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T23:50:49-07:00","id":239971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=239732#post239732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably worth asking what kinds of gameplay you want to be possible in Promethean. I get that you want more, but more of what?<br /> <br /> I personally have trouble seeing how Promethean could be played in a throng; it feels aimed towards a two-person high-trust ST-player game. You can see that in the y-splat, for instance: Refinements are intensely personal, as opposed to the organizational structure of pretty much every other y-splat. It would be nice to have better social support, but I don't know how to achieve that or what it'd look like.<br /> <br /> I'd like to keep the &quot;every character is trying to become human&quot; angle, but I'd be open to having a perspective that regarded &quot;human&quot; as something as constructed as the Prometheans themselves are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read with charity as it's early where I am and I haven't examined this idea as thoroughly as I would like.<br /> <br /> The key things are...<br /> 1) I want to be able to play a stationary game. Whether a large city (a lost Promethean among the faceless crowds of London or New York seems rather appropriate) or a small town (Stephen King was onto something in that thats a wonderful horror setting).<br /> 2) I want to be able to play long-term social interactions. Given the rarity of Prometheans, an all-Promethean society seems... improbable. In that case, it would be nice to develop the possibility of a Promethean forging some kind of place for themselves in either human society or that of other supernaturals. The main element is just that it should be more doable to develop NPCs and relationships over a long period of time.<br /> 3) The possibility of alternative motives. Perhaps a Promethean wants to be <i>accepted</i> in human society, but not necessarily become human themselves (I mean, objectively speaking, super-powers, insane durability, and very long life are desirable things to keep, and not even for selfish reasons -- think of a Promethean policeman who wants to serve his community). Or perhaps a Promethean wants vengeance on their creator, and the game plays out as a kind of long-standing 'nemesis' arc. Or perhaps a Promethean actually has a beneficial, positive relationship with their demiurge.<br /> <br /> So, a few possible concepts, drawn out from that (I'm sure you can finagle most of these in the current system, but it's tricky):<br /> --A Promethean who makes it his life's goal to hunt down his creator, to kill them, or make them suffer, or prevent them from ever hurting anyone again. Conversely, one who feels the same way about a misbegotten creation.<br /> --A Promethean created for a specific purpose, who actually basically agrees with that purpose. For instance, the Robocop approach -- a Promethean is created to be the perfect defender of law and order in a small town.<br /> --A Promethean who has decided to infiltrate and dominate society. Think Stepford Wives.<br /> --A Promethean who tries to create a life for itself in a cold and uncaring urban conglomeration, who finds the closest thing he can get to companionship either from humans ignorant of his nature, or from other supernaturals who know all too well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T00:07:39-07:00","id":239976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=239971#post239971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a few possible concepts, drawn out from that (I'm sure you can finagle most of these in the current system, but it's tricky):<br /> --A Promethean created for a specific purpose, who actually basically agrees with that purpose. For instance, the Robocop approach -- a Promethean is created to be the perfect defender of law and order in a small town.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the sake of pointed RTFM: Yes, I imagine it's extremely difficult to make <i>the Promethean who's the corebook's example of character creation.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-25-2014, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T00:07:56-07:00","id":239977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=239967#post239967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't Promethean generally portray Pyros as being <i>unnatural</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div> If pyros is unnatural than how can a natural process create a promethean, ala the extempore?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T00:10:58-07:00","id":239981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=239977#post239977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If pyros is unnatural than how can a natural process create a promethean, ala the extempore?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Pyros is explicitly both perfectly natural and utterly unnatural - if nothing else, it's specifically almost never found in a concentrated and usable form outside the context of &quot;a Promethean catalyzes the idea-energy-substance of the Fire from their experiences.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T01:54:43-07:00","id":240038,"title":"","content":"I shouldn't write while on painkillers, let alone on the divine alien nature of the Pyros.<br /> <br /> The Pyros is the Divine Fire, stolen from the heavens, but that's not where it began. Its light drew the titans out of the Chaos, its heat churned the waters and infected certain triglyceride bubbles with life, and its power awed the first minds to behold it. But it was always there, since the dawn of time, and some worry, from long before that. It is the Prime Mover in a universe that wishes to sleep forever, that wakes it from its slumber, thrashing with light and movement. It is the outsider, the intruder, but without its invasion, there would be nothing here to invade.<br /> <br /> There would be stirred from the mud those who learned how to harness it. They thought themselves great, watching the fire serve them, and put themselves above the animals. And the Pyros saw this, and it was good. Gods and men would believe that they had tamed fire, when the fire had only made them wilder than nature. Nature, meanwhile, was a savage and jealous creature, forever tormented by the driving, feeding light, and would gnash and flee whenever the Pyros drew to close. When the Pyros finally took on the shape of men and touched its dead fingers to the ground, it screamed in the agony of the burnt, and every creature under its wing quailed and withered for miles.<br /> <br /> This is what is meant by unnatural. The natural world cannot be without the forces of evolution and destruction, but the Pyros is a catalyst for creation that had to exist before Creation itself. <br /> <br /> Eh, one theory. Painkillers!<br /> <br /> Alchemists as antagonists: wanting Prometheans for parts is neat, but shouldn't be encoded in rules. First, those rules provide meta-clues as to what that crazy murderer, &quot;the Black Alchemist&quot;, is up to, as you now have this shopping list. Second, Prometheans are the Lead in this narrative, not the Philosopher's Stone. They don't offer a lot of insight to &quot;legitimate&quot; alchemy, as they're unrefined piles of dirt, figuratively speaking. They are walking, talking corpses with an affinity for electricity, so maybe there's truth to Homonculi stories. Third, they're interesting subjects for study, and simply observing a Promethean for any length of time is going to Disquiet them, delicious organs or not. An alchemist might realize he's the only one who knows how to deal with the &quot;threat&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T05:12:53-07:00","id":240159,"title":"","content":"I point out that while there's no rules for them; the sample chronicle had a very cool Alchemist NPC who helps the players. I would definitely like more of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T10:23:41-07:00","id":240369,"title":"","content":"+1 for more on Alchemists / Demiurges. As allies, enemies, and everything in between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T15:53:01-07:00","id":240846,"title":"","content":"How mad would folks be about an Orphean lineage replacing the Ulgan? The whole spirits thing has never fit well to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T16:00:35-07:00","id":240852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=240159#post240159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I point out that while there's no rules for them; the sample chronicle had a very cool Alchemist NPC who helps the players. I would definitely like more of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Calogero is indeed very cool -- in fact, I like that whole adventure. I thought the formula for the aqua vitae was a great primer on what alchemy could be; a sort of metaphorical science. Sir Isaac Newton apparently thought that ancient myths were cyphers for alchemical formulae. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Net_(substance\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Net_(substance</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T16:04:35-07:00","id":240869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=240846#post240846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How mad would folks be about an Orphean lineage replacing the Ulgan? The whole spirits thing has never fit well to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Platinum mad.<br /> <br /> We have an entire other gameline amply better suited to the Orphic mysteries and the Nepri remain the better candidates for death-related motifs in Promethean (Strange Alchemies underlines this thoroughly in the text even if &quot;mythologically associated with an Egyptian god of the dead, has two Bestowments dealing with death and corpses, has the most lethal Wasteland effect, and has a signature character whose driving goal is mapping the river of death&quot; wasn't sufficient support already). Spirits have a fair bit of historical alchemical association that the lands of the dead lack, and the corebook points out quite nicely that spirits make for good encounters when going to the Wastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T21:04:52-07:00","id":241034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=239971#post239971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, points 1 and 2 are things that we not only agree on, but have explicit developer intent on achieving anyways, so excepting ideas for actually <i>doing</i> it, it seems pointless to discuss those. Onto, therefore, point 3.<br /> <br /> I think it's worth making a Mage: the Awakening comparison here.<br /> <br /> In Mage, many people concluded that the purpose of every Mage is ultimately to Ascend. This isn't too surprising; the corebook actually says so. But it's not actually true: a lot of Mages have other things to do, like playing their political games and furthering their research and otherwise being human.<br /> <br /> It's much the same with Promethean. I broke out my book to poke through it and I notice one thing in particular: the corebook claims that Prometheans who refuse to go on the Pilgrimage still end up inching closer to Mortality. (Refusing the Dawn, p72) The difference is that &quot;otherwise being human&quot; is the very thing your Promethean supposedly isn't interested in.<br /> <br /> Promethean shares a lot with the superpowered genre. They're largely indistinguishable when not using powers; there is an us-and-them alienation; they tend to just want to have a normal life. You can make a lot of very poignant comparisons between Prometheans and the X-Men teenage themes, not least of which is the frequent desire of mutants to have their mutations purged, their powers nullified, and their lives normal. The two major differences are that X-Men tended to have had a human childhood, so they're perfectly aware of what being normal is like, and they are not under the burden of forces like Torment, Disquiet, and Wasteland.<br /> <br /> That makes it a lot easier to do things like form teams or hide amongst normals. Which leads me, inexorably, to my actual point:<br /> <br /> I think that if points 1 and 2 are addressed, if it starts to make sense to form a local crime-fighting group, for instance, you'll find that point 3 will be sufficiently addressed as a result. Figuring out how to do that without losing what makes Promethean unique is Matt's headache. And maybe Ben Quo's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T21:38:27-07:00","id":241068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=241034#post241034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's much the same with Promethean. I broke out my book to poke through it and I notice one thing in particular: the corebook claims that Prometheans who refuse to go on the Pilgrimage still end up inching closer to Mortality. (Refusing the Dawn, p72) The difference is that &quot;otherwise being human&quot; is the very thing your Promethean supposedly isn't interested in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contrariwise, being near the end of my readthrough of <i>Strange Alchemies</i>, a worthwhile excerpt from the chapter full of essays:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>When did the Promethean first learn about the Pilgrimage?</b> Some Prometheans hear about the Great Work from the moment they are able to understand the concept, or even before. Others hear about it only as they are about to undertake their independence from their creators. Still others only hear their creator talk of it occasionally, or to other people, and they are never given any context for what it means. Some hear absolutely nothing about the Pilgrimage from their creators, and have to discover its existence from other Prometheans. The circumstances under which the Promethean hears of it, and from whom he hears it, can set the tone for his Pilgrimage. Those who hear of it from a cruel creator may walk it with hesitation, while others may consider the Pilgrimage the thing that took their beloved creators from them.<br /> <br /> Other Prometheans simply find themselves on the Pilgrimage. For some, they\u2019ve somehow always known that their goal was to be come human; it simply took someone else putting it into words for them. Others seek to be near humans, to emulate them, but do not understand why they do these things. <b>The Pilgrimage is an innate part of the Promethean existence \u2014 the Divine Fire is transformative, and rare is the Promethean who is simply content as he is. Prometheans are all driven by the desire for change, to become something else, and most of them find their role models in humanity.</b> </div> </div> </div>And another one from the chapter fiction:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I had thought he\u2019d leave after the fight in the motel room. The way he looked when he hurt me made me think maybe it was best if he did. But he\u2019d stayed. Said he\u2019d learned something there, not about fighting or Transmutations or the like. But when I forgave him, when I said I\u2019d understood, he\u2019d gotten all wide-eyed and you could see it come on inside like a light there in the darkness.<br /> <br /> How could I explain it to him, when I didn\u2019t quite understand it myself? We didn\u2019t keep going just because there were no other options. That wasn\u2019t enough to keep trying, to keep striving. But it was those moments, like the one he\u2019d had in the motel room, when things become clear, if only for a little while. <b>Those times when we get a glimpse of what it is we could be, or when we see in the humans what they could be if they let themselves.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why we do it. That\u2019s why we keep going. Something just keeps us following that little spark of Hope.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T00:06:52-07:00","id":241147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=239970#post239970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thirded.<br /> <br /> I want secret societies of gentlemen alchemists, eager to milk Prometheans for precious Vitriol. I want Demurges mad with inspiration creating ever more alien abominations. I want <b>deliberate</b> mortal antagonists, who persecute and pursue Prometheans for reasons other than disquiet. Antagonists who starkly mirror to the Promethean's own pilgrimage with their selfish quest to transcend humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>4th'd<br /> <br /> And even though Zekies might not be one of the Core lineages, I think keeping them around in 'boogy-man' territory, (ala VII), works out well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T08:16:57-07:00","id":241367,"title":"","content":"Since there seems to be disagreement regarding Disquiet and Wasteland severity, might I suggest including both ends of the scale? A Promethean with Humanity 1 and Azoth 10 might be the stereotypical walking-chaos Zeka, while a Promethean with Humanity 10 and Azoth 1 might be essentially a clone - Created, but only distinguishable from Mortality under close examination.<br /> <br /> That way you can let the players choose how nomadic and antisocial they want to be as part of character creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=238824#post238824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is one of those times when people aren't asking for what they really want. The issue with Promethean isn't that it has a lot of high brow philisophical undertones, or that it approaches the question of what it means to be human. Do people really want <i>less</i> depth to their game? Eh. Maybe, but I'd wager no.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere's a difference between depth and complexity. People aren't saying they want the game to be even more shallow and superficial; they're saying they want it to be simpler and more direct. It's a question of refining elements to better put across the themes of the game, rather than making it into a puzzle.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, does anyone know what Transmutations are supposed to be? From a philosophical/alchemical perspective, they seem to undermine the game's themes ... surely they should be <i>dangerous</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 08-26-2014, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T09:17:40-07:00","id":241402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=241367#post241367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Azathoth</div> </div> </div> </div>Azoth. It's an old term for the fabled universal solvent and agent of transformation in alchemy, not the Nuclear Chaos of Lovecraft's Mythos.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Incidentally, does anyone know what Transmutations are supposed to be? From a philosophical/alchemical perspective, they seem to undermine the game's themes ... surely they should be <i>dangerous</i>? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Promethean: the Created Core Rulebook, p47-48, &quot;Transmutations&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Pyros is a catalyst for change, and it cares not if this change violates natural laws such as the conservation of mass and energy. Under the influence of Pyros, anything can be transmuted into something else entirely. In theory, at least. In practice, such alchemical operations are more difficult, requiring training and mastery of the principles involved, along with hard-won experience. In addition, learning how to manipulate the Pyros to achieve one class of effects doesn\u2019t guarantee that it will behave the same way when you want it to achieve another range of effects. It is indeed mercurial, and like a crackling flame, it sends out tongues of fire in every direction.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">[\u2026]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Each Refinement lends itself to the practice of certain classes of Transmutations, the name Prometheans gives to the amazing powers the Pyros gives them to effect change in their bodies, minds or the world itself. The Promethean transmutes a part of his physical or mental substance into something else.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Most Transmutations are only temporary until the base matter of a Promethean\u2019s being reasserts itself. During the time a Transmutation is in effect, however, impossible things can occur.<br /> <br /> [\u2026]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Without these boons, Prometheans would be hard pressed to complete their Pilgrimages. Life is hard enough for them. Without special means, they would not likely survive for long. With the world itself turned against them, the powers of the Pyros are their only firm allies.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T10:49:44-07:00","id":241481,"title":"","content":"Looking over things, something that seems ripe for simplification and refinement - heh, refinement - is folding Azothic Radiance, Wasteland, and Disquiet into one Disquiet Radius.<br /> <br /> They're canonically supposed to be the same effect - nature rejects that which was Created apart from the natural order, as Azoth leaks out and contaminates the world - but they lack unified mechanics, and seem to have drifted apart in terms of terminology over time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=241402#post241402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Azoth. It's an old term for the fabled universal solvent and agent of transformation in alchemy, not the Nuclear Chaos of Lovecraft's Mythos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops. Good catch.<br /> <br /> I'm ... not really sure I follow those quotes. Sure, the Divine Fire is vague enough it could be harnessed to produce semi-useful effects.<br /> <br /> What are they <i>for? </i>What role do they play thematically? How do they help direct play?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>Without these boons, Prometheans would be hard pressed to complete their Pilgrimages. Life is hard enough for them. Without special means, they would not likely survive for long. With the world itself turned against them, the powers of the Pyros are their only firm allies.</i></span> </div> </div> </div>They ... help Prometheans fight the dangers inherent in being PCs? That's it? They're an objective benefit compared to humanity, the universe saying &quot;you seem nice, have some superpowers for your hard work&quot;?<br /> <br /> Well, there's your problem. Transmutations need to say something about the Promethean condition. They should, in a word, be <i>unnatural</i> - even, dare I say it, horrific?<br /> <br /> (If I'm wildly misreading those quotes, or I'm forgetting about better ones - I need to re-read the Transmutations - please, someone yell at me for my hubris.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 08-26-2014, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T15:56:31-07:00","id":241778,"title":"","content":"I want a big theme in this new edition to be <b>discovery</b>. A lot of discussion has centered around how Mummy does a great job of keeping players and characters in the dark about large parts of the world they live in, even on a mechanical level -- like how Mummy characters don't really &quot;learn&quot; Affinities as much as they come into them, despite most of their acquisitions being conscious choices by the player. (For the record I'm not advocating that as how Transmutations should go, it was just an example.)<br /> <br /> Prometheans similarly have to stumble through the dark, just as man did before the advent of Prometheus' Gift. So I'd like for there to be no One True Way to make it to the New Dawn; or even One True New Dawn.<br /> <br /> I'd like there to be no One True Way to even <i>make</i> a Promethean. Sure having Victor Frankenstein's notes would <i>help</i>, but he definitely got it <i>wrong</i> in certain regards and now <i>you see that</i>. You can do <i>better, </i>or <i>more beautiful</i>, or whatever subjective way you choose to judge <i>your</i> magnum opus.<br /> <br /> Having the player learn things along with their character, whether that character's &quot;fresh off the slab&quot; or has been journeying through the Saturnine Night for centuries, is a really engaging style of play. By not nailing everything down to a formula (or even having formulae that just <i>don't work as promised</i>), the mystique deepens.<br /> <br /> For the record I'm not advocating for a meta-plot either, but damn do I love meta-plot <i>hooks</i>. You may recall that the God-Machine came from just a few mentions of the concept in a couple of books scattered throughout the WoD lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T19:30:15-07:00","id":241917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=241481#post241481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm ... not really sure I follow those quotes. Sure, the Divine Fire is vague enough it could be harnessed to produce semi-useful effects.<br /> <br /> What are they <i>for?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Demonstrating the various expressions through which the Fire is the principles of anything-can-happen and this-too-shall-pass (Brine, Promethean Core p158), particulars of which may be studied for Prometheans to learn more about their bodies and pseudosouls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What role do they play thematically? </div> </div> </div>&quot;Getting closer to completing a transition into a different type of being increases the intensity with which Nature conspires against you - it is to your advantage to turn the engine of raw potential that drives you to more nuanced uses.&quot; You have to <i>pursue</i> these powers to learn them, for all that the Refinements incentivize certain tenors of activity by spontaneous development.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do they help direct play? </div> </div> </div>Define terms, please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They ... help Prometheans fight the dangers inherent in being PCs? That's it? They're an objective benefit compared to humanity, <b>the universe saying &quot;you seem nice, have some superpowers for your hard work&quot;?</b><br /> <br /> <b>Well, there's your problem. </b>Transmutations need to say something about the Promethean condition. They should, in a word, be <i>unnatural</i> - even, dare I say it, horrific?<br /> <br /> (If I'm wildly misreading those quotes, or I'm forgetting about better ones - I need to re-read the Transmutations - please, someone yell at me for my hubris.) </div> </div> </div>If you don't actually want an answer you can just not ask, dude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-26-2014, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T19:50:47-07:00","id":241923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=241778#post241778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like there to be no One True Way to even <i>make</i> a Promethean. Sure having Victor Frankenstein's notes would <i>help</i>, but he definitely got it <i>wrong</i> in certain regards and now <i>you see that</i>. You can do <i>better, </i>or <i>more beautiful</i>, or whatever subjective way you choose to judge <i>your</i> magnum opus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. It actually brings to mind Howard Bloom's ideas on the nature of (literary) genius: that it's agonistic, where the up-and-comer looks at the past, looks at the Epitome of That Bygone Era, and judges it to be lacking, so they do it <i>better</i>. They fix the errors.<br /> <br /> I actually wonder if it'd be worthwhile to poke at the metaphor of writing literature more: a Promethean's journey is figuring out how to write the Book of Life, and they manage chapters and characters and wonderful turns of dialogue, but then it doesn't quite fit together, the themes are incoherent, it just doesn't gel, so they have to try again and rearrange and reconfigure until it's..., well..., a magnum opus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=241778#post241778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having the player learn things along with their character, whether that character's &quot;fresh off the slab&quot; or has been journeying through the Saturnine Night for centuries, is a really engaging style of play. By not nailing everything down to a formula (or even having formulae that just <i>don't work as promised</i>), the mystique deepens.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also like this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T01:04:15-07:00","id":242079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=241923#post241923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually wonder if it'd be worthwhile to poke at the metaphor of writing literature more: a Promethean's journey is figuring out how to write the Book of Life, and they manage chapters and characters and wonderful turns of dialogue, but then it doesn't quite fit together, the themes are incoherent, it just doesn't gel, so they have to try again and rearrange and reconfigure until it's..., well..., a magnum opus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had previously always thought that each Promethean is their own magnum opus, but I like this as well. If they can create a thing of great beauty, maybe they can live through that thing. And maybe that's how a new Promethean is made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T04:54:04-07:00","id":242161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=241778#post241778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like there to be no One True Way to even <i>make</i> a Promethean. Sure having Victor Frankenstein's notes would <i>help</i>, but he definitely got it <i>wrong</i> in certain regards and now <i>you see that</i>. You can do <i>better, </i>or <i>more beautiful</i>, or whatever subjective way you choose to judge <i>your</i> magnum opus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say his notes are useful for how to assemble various bodies into one (it's skilled work!), but if you take them seriously - if you think you can make this work because he did - you're making it <i>less</i> likely you'll succeed, since a big part of the Demiurge making a Promethean is that it involves a transcendental obsession, not a rational choice, and becomes harder/impossible oncy you know it can be done. Making Prometheans isn't a science that can be replicated. It's a profane miracle. At least under the old rules.<br /> <br /> The literary metaphor of Errol's is great, a worth alternative to the journey theme. Fun to have some in-game Prometheans use it, I'd say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T07:20:13-07:00","id":242232,"title":"","content":"For a segue, and this is something I'm considering, not something I have an answer to.<br /> <br /> While each Promethean is working towards being Human, does actually reaching that point add to the game? If it does, what? Is the whole becoming human thing better handled as a Golcanda style send-off for a character, with no real rules that say &quot;you must become redeemed after going this far, or deliberately shun the themes of the game so you never get there?&quot; If that isn't the best way to handle it, how do Prometheans remain relevant after becoming humans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T09:57:00-07:00","id":242305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242232#post242232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While each Promethean is working towards being Human, does actually reaching that point add to the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion is &quot;No.&quot; This is one of those videogame endings; a Promethean might hit Human at the end of a chronicle, with maybe an epilogue scene or two to wrap certain things up, but after that, the game is done. More than anything else, in Promethean, <i>winning matters</i>.<br /> <br /> It's completely different from, say, a Mage forging his Golden Road and becoming an Archmaster*; in the Mage's case, the structural themes of play continue to matter, just on a wider scale. In Promethean, innocence is achieved. It doesn't quite work with the WoD theme as a whole in that now you're a mortal in a somewhat crapsack world, but ignoring the wider milieu, it's like a fallen angel regaining their place in heaven. It's a <i>good death</i>, but it's a death. Not in the biological sense, but the metaphysical: you are no more. There is no Promethean tormented by the tragedy of his existence anymore.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't even like the term Redeemed. Redeemed implies that you were being punished for something. New Dawn works fine.<br /> <br /> * I need to read Demon: the Descent at some point and decide whether or not the Cipher and Hell are useful as comparisons here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T11:28:02-07:00","id":242349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242305#post242305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't even like the term Redeemed. Redeemed implies that you were being punished for something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a rather fixated way of reading a term that also has a transactional connotation to it in a game where the entire driving process is &quot;<i>earn</i> your Mortality&quot; and the foremost bit of established occult shenanigans the line gives focus to has, in another gameline, been compared to <i>making a trade at a metaphorical marketplace using the innate over-concept of &quot;worth&quot; to change skill into beauty into wealth into permanence</i>.<br /> <br /> Did you get swept up in the metaphorical connotations of the line's conflating Mortality with <i>Gold</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T11:30:29-07:00","id":242352,"title":"","content":"You know, I really like the idea that Humanity should start at 3. Making a point of buying Humanity, trying to be like a human when you don't need to, but want to.<br /> <br /> This guy attacked intending to kill you. You fought and subdued him. Now he deserves to die, you won't be affected by that. But a human would. A human wouldn't kill this guy in cold blood. And you want to be a human, even if you think this guy will be trouble next time. So you let him go, even when it doesn't make sense, but you have to make sense of this. A human would.<br /> <br /> The only problem I see is that it could be easy to reach Humanity 0. But as the focus of the game would be gaining Humanity, this might be off-set (though I don't remember if there's anything worse that happens at Humanity 0).<br /> <br /> Also, it goes without saying, I hope they keep Humanity as the morality trait. The only motive I see for then to changing it is to do it differently from Vampire, and I really like this dichotomy it has with Vampire. Humanity in Vampire represents a Human turning into a Monster. Humanity in Promethean represents a Monster turning into a Human. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T11:34:50-07:00","id":242353,"title":"","content":"The Onyx Path Movie thread reminded me:<br /> <br /> Opening, closing, and chapter fiction that is as good as the original stuff. I swear to God, the people who loved Promethean must have started with the fiction, and those who don't must have skipped it. The fiction in that book is, I think, some of the best the World of Darkness has ever had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-28-2014, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T11:57:27-07:00","id":242370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242353#post242353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Onyx Path Movie thread reminded me:<br /> <br /> Opening, closing, and chapter fiction that is as good as the original stuff. I swear to God, the people who loved Promethean must have started with the fiction, and those who don't must have skipped it. The fiction in that book is, I think, some of the best the World of Darkness have ever had.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this in turn reminds me of a thing that I did a lot in the pre-previews part of the runup to Idigam: beating the RTFM Drum in the presence of people talking about adding things that are already in the game or taking out things that weren't in it.<br /> <br /> <b>Read the books, people. All the way through. There is important shit in there.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T12:43:27-07:00","id":242440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242349#post242349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a rather fixated way of reading a term that also has a transactional connotation to it in a game where the entire driving process is &quot;<i>earn</i> your Mortality&quot; and the foremost bit of established occult shenanigans the line gives focus to has, in another gameline, been compared to <i>making a trade at a metaphorical marketplace using the innate over-concept of &quot;worth&quot; to change skill into beauty into wealth into permanence</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see: obviously Prometheans are actually coupon books. Everything becomes clear now. /s<br /> <br /> Debt, outside of the context of a society, is a punishment. That's why fines are levied for minor offenses; paying your fine is redemption for, say, the crime of littering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242349#post242349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you get swept up in the metaphorical connotations of the line's conflating Mortality with <i>Gold</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems more like <i>your</i> mistake, with your fixation on interpreting redemption in terms of money, not mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T12:58:13-07:00","id":242488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242440#post242440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see: obviously Prometheans are actually coupon books. Everything becomes clear now. /s</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny story: one of the more mundane types of pilgrimage is going to particular places and getting stamps or other marks that show that you went to those places; among those with an interest in a given kind of place, having such proof of experience is accorded a good deal of worth despite the marks just being lines and colors on paper that say &quot;the bearer of this symbol was at this place.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Debt, outside of the context of a society, is a punishment. That's why fines are levied for minor offenses; paying your fine is redemption for, say, the crime of littering. </div> </div> </div>And winning a lottery is redemption of a ticket you were in the right place and time to get.<br /> <br /> <i>Redemption gives you a <b>new soul.</b></i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That seems more like <i>your</i> mistake, with your fixation on interpreting redemption in terms of money, not mine. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Gold is a thing that possesses connotations of value, worth, permanence, and other things directly related to its role as a currency&quot; is a counterpoint I was making to your apparent preference for ignoring those in favor of &quot;gold is beautiful and symbolic of the sun&quot; that preferring &quot;the New Dawn&quot; suggests.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really do to try and turn around my use of &quot;fixated&quot; when the examples I'm giving are specifically in contrast to what I perceived as a narrowness in your interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T14:16:11-07:00","id":242534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242370#post242370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Read the books, people. All the way through. There is important shit in there.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Books? There's <i>books </i>for this stuff?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T15:15:40-07:00","id":242601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242534#post242534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Books? There's <i>books </i>for this stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure man. There are several. I mean, just look at all the threads going on in this forum. You could write entire lexicons about this. A shame nobody has, though.<br /> Would be real neat. I think with all this stuff on the forums, there would be enough material for atleast a source book and then like 4 supplement book. You could come up with all these kind of neat names for them too, like Magnum Opus, Strange Alchemies, Saturnine Nights and even something outlandish like Pandoras Box (who even knows who Pandora was anyway?). A shame this feat is yet to be accomplished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T15:30:27-07:00","id":242611,"title":"","content":"but seriously though guys<br /> <br /> I had already decided to reread the entire line like a month before we got word of Firestorm because <s>I am a lunatic</s> I happened to be up to that point in my reread-all-the-gamelines list at the time.<br /> <br /> The fact that we now have a second edition <i>confirmed</i> is a <i>fantastic</i> excuse to refamiliarize yourselves with the actual content of Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T18:04:33-07:00","id":242714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242352#post242352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I really like the idea that Humanity should start at 3. Making a point of buying Humanity, trying to be like a human when you don't need to, but want to.<br /> <br /> This guy attacked intending to kill you. You fought and subdued him. Now he deserves to die, you won't be affected by that. But a human would. A human wouldn't kill this guy in cold blood. And you want to be a human, even if you think this guy will be trouble next time. So you let him go, even when it doesn't make sense, but you have to make sense of this. A human would.<br /> <br /> The only problem I see is that it could be easy to reach Humanity 0. But as the focus of the game would be gaining Humanity, this might be off-set (though I don't remember if there's anything worse that happens at Humanity 0).<br /> <br /> Also, it goes without saying, I hope they keep Humanity as the morality trait. The only motive I see for then to changing it is to do it differently from Vampire, and I really like this dichotomy it has with Vampire. Humanity in Vampire represents a Human turning into a Monster. Humanity in Promethean represents a Monster turning into a Human. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am right with you there -- but hey, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">I'm biased.</a> Keep in mind that you have to really, REALLY try to get to Humanity 0 though.<br /> <br /> Speaking of -- and returning to the mortal alchemists -- what if there were people who were trying to <i>give up</i> their humanity by replacing themselves with Promethean parts in a sort of inverse Pilgrimage? Like the robot people in Galaxy Express 999, or Alpha from Men in Black (the show). They want to be more than human, so they replace more and more of themselves with monster parts and lose themselves in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T18:13:48-07:00","id":242721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242611#post242611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but seriously though guys<br /> <br /> I had already decided to reread the entire line like a month before we got word of Firestorm because <s>I am a lunatic</s> I happened to be up to that point in my reread-all-the-gamelines list at the time.<br /> <br /> The fact that we now have a second edition <i>confirmed</i> is a <i>fantastic</i> excuse to refamiliarize yourselves with the actual content of Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conversely, and I say this as someone who <i>has</i> RTFM<sup>*</sup>, the issue at hand is how the <b>PtC 2e</b> core book should be handled; so asking for something that has been addressed in one of 1e\u2019s supplements is legit. <br /> <br /> I like the notion of cyborgs (<i>not</i> Unfleshed, but humans with non-human parts grafted on) as potential antagonists \u2014 but I find myself asking how they\u2019d differ from <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s Cheiron Group\u2026<br /> <hr /><br /> * If there\u2019s any gameline where I\u2019m likely to be able to quote an obscure reference from a rarely-read supplement by memory, <b>Promethean</b> is it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-27-2014, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T18:22:19-07:00","id":242724,"title":"","content":"Humanity as morality stat works. <br /> <br /> Throwing something random on the pile: so does Humanity (or similar) as a Powerstat. Would address some on-screen issues, if the devs decide to make it Good End, but End for the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T19:40:07-07:00","id":242796,"title":"","content":"Actually, Humanity is <i>already</i> \u201cGood End, but End\u201d as written \u2014 perhaps a bit <i>too much</i> so, as it makes the end-game awkward as Redeemed former throngmates almost inevitably get driven away by Disquiet. <br /> <br /> There are already a handful of ways that a Redeemed mortal is subtly different from an ordinary mortal (e.g., he keeps any superhuman attributes he had as a Promethean; and if his corpse is used for the Generative Act, <i>he comes back as a Promethean</i> \u2014 though I wouldn\u2019t mind seeing that difference disappear); I\u2019d like to add one more: if the Redeemed was a member of a Branded Throng when he achieved Mortality, he\u2019s automatically immune to any Disquiet caused by his former throngmates. If the throng <i>didn\u2019t</i> forge an Alchemical Pact before he Redeemed, too bad; likewise, if he meets a Promethean who isn\u2019t part of his former throng, he\u2019s subject to the effects of Disquiet. But his former traveling companions? He can choose to stick around and help them finish off their Pilgrimages if he wants to, without risk of being turned against them. Strictly as a way to facilitate a gaming group playing out the final stages of a throng achieving Mortality without the players having to drop out of the game as they Redeem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T20:06:07-07:00","id":242804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242721#post242721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, and I say this as someone who <i>has</i> RTFM<sup>*</sup>, the issue at hand is how the <b>PtC 2e</b> core book should be handled; so asking for something that has been addressed in one of 1e\u2019s supplements is legit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, most certainly - my other main drum-beating back in earlier IC/WtF2e what-do-you-want-to-see discussion, for any who missed it, was &quot;consolidate, consolidate, consolidate.&quot; It would do nicely to see the five 1e Core Lineages have their writeups refined (and streamlined to suit the addition of two more Lineages to the section) to account for bits like the first chapter of Strange Alchemies - the Frankenstein Rumors sidebars in that book is one of my favorite such sections, for instance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242796#post242796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are already a handful of ways that a Redeemed mortal is subtly different from an ordinary mortal (e.g., he keeps any superhuman attributes he had as a Promethean; and if his corpse is used for the Generative Act, <i>he comes back as a Promethean</i> \u2014 though I wouldn\u2019t mind seeing that difference disappear)</div> </div> </div> </div>Disappearance need not be a thing, considering the only differences are 1) the Generative Act is less likely to succeed, and 2) the resulting Promethean might <i>eventually <b>maybe</b></i> remember the prior two stages of their existence.<br /> <br /> I will agree that the matter of what the player of a Promethean who Redeems their Azoth ought to do for the rest of the game if the process doesn't go just right would be quite welcome, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T20:54:37-07:00","id":242819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242721#post242721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the notion of cyborgs (<i>not</i> Unfleshed, but humans with non-human parts grafted on) as potential antagonists \u2014 but I find myself asking how they\u2019d differ from <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s Cheiron Group\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Cheiron employees aren't really &quot;cyborgs,&quot; though. More like &quot;fleshborgs.&quot; A full Robocop cyborg would be different, and cool.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T21:04:57-07:00","id":242821,"title":"","content":"They\u2019re cyborgs if the parts they graft on come from the Unfleshed or an equivalent; they\u2019re \u201cflesh-borgs\u201d if the parts come from a Promethean. How is that different from what Metamurpho suggested?<br /> <br /> Thematically though, it\u2019s a fascinating idea: to a Promethean, a mortal who is trying to \u201ctranscend\u201d the human condition would register as a contradiction, if the Promethean can grasp the concept at all. Ordinary humans are everything a Promethean aspires to be; why would someone who was born with that willingly <i>throw it away</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-28-2014, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T23:24:55-07:00","id":242861,"title":"","content":"You know, thinking on it, things really do start to fall together if you have Humanity be the Promethean's Powerstat instead of their morality stat. Then you can use Disquiet (Serenity?) as their Morality stat. Probably make the Powerstat only increasing through a rewritten Vitriol or similar &quot;XP, but only to raise limited number of traits&quot; mechanics. Assuming I'm remembering Vitriol right, its been a while.<br /> <br /> Humanity as Powerstat rewards players for going on the pilgrimage in a real, tangible way. Its an ascension of power, which will settle better in people's minds. Powerstat 10 is also unambiguously so far off that you don't have to worry about it in the normal course of play, similar to how no one really worries about Changelings becoming True Fae in most of their games. So you have a lot more buy in on the whole becoming human angle from more casual people who might not be interested in all the philosophy ever for its own sake.<br /> <br /> More importantly, your Morality stat can now handle Disquiet. Move it from &quot;This roll happens vs everyone you meet&quot; to on Disquiet Break rolls, you get Disquiet-esque conditions that say people hate you. Resolve when Y interesting thing happens. Can even make the Dramatic Failure option what triggers Wasteland. The key to pulling this together is what you make the break conditions be. Demon-esque break conditions for using certain powers and doing things like &quot;extended social contact&quot; are entirely appropriate.<br /> <br /> This creates a lot more hinges you can fine-tune to get the feel of Promethean just right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T23:35:44-07:00","id":242865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242861#post242861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, thinking on it, things really do start to fall together if you have Humanity be the Promethean's Powerstat instead of their morality stat.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes powerful Prometheans <i>less</i> susceptible to Torment and stalling rather than more. Promethean power is a measurement of the strength of their <i>potential for change</i>, not their potential for humanity in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T23:38:07-07:00","id":242866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242488#post242488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny story: one of the more mundane types of pilgrimage is going to particular places and getting stamps or other marks that show that you went to those places; among those with an interest in a given kind of place, having such proof of experience is accorded a good deal of worth despite the marks just being lines and colors on paper that say &quot;the bearer of this symbol was at this place.&quot;<br /> <br /> And winning a lottery is redemption of a ticket you were in the right place and time to get.<br /> <br /> <i>Redemption gives you a <b>new soul.</b></i><br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Gold is a thing that possesses connotations of value, worth, permanence, and other things directly related to its role as a currency&quot; is a counterpoint I was making to your apparent preference for ignoring those in favor of &quot;gold is beautiful and symbolic of the sun&quot; that preferring &quot;the New Dawn&quot; suggests.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really do to try and turn around my use of &quot;fixated&quot; when the examples I'm giving are specifically in contrast to what I perceived as a narrowness in your interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say thank you for writing a response where you're not entirely being an asshole, and acknowledge that you are correct. Sometimes I forget that you're someone with whom I want a minimum of interaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T23:58:36-07:00","id":242875,"title":"","content":"Satchel is good peeps.<br /> <br /> Course, given how involved he stays with threads like these, I also sympathize when he decides to play harsh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T01:15:43-07:00","id":242901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242861#post242861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, thinking on it, things really do start to fall together if you have Humanity be the Promethean's Powerstat instead of their morality stat. Then you can use Disquiet (Serenity?) as their Morality stat. Probably make the Powerstat only increasing through a rewritten Vitriol or similar &quot;XP, but only to raise limited number of traits&quot; mechanics. Assuming I'm remembering Vitriol right, its been a while.<br /> <br /> Humanity as Powerstat rewards players for going on the pilgrimage in a real, tangible way. Its an ascension of power, which will settle better in people's minds. Powerstat 10 is also unambiguously so far off that you don't have to worry about it in the normal course of play, similar to how no one really worries about Changelings becoming True Fae in most of their games. So you have a lot more buy in on the whole becoming human angle from more casual people who might not be interested in all the philosophy ever for its own sake.<br /> <br /> More importantly, your Morality stat can now handle Disquiet. Move it from &quot;This roll happens vs everyone you meet&quot; to on Disquiet Break rolls, you get Disquiet-esque conditions that say people hate you. Resolve when Y interesting thing happens. Can even make the Dramatic Failure option what triggers Wasteland. The key to pulling this together is what you make the break conditions be. Demon-esque break conditions for using certain powers and doing things like &quot;extended social contact&quot; are entirely appropriate.<br /> <br /> This creates a lot more hinges you can fine-tune to get the feel of Promethean just right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. That ... actually works, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> I assume this would invert the &quot;usual&quot; benefits/drawbacks of raising one's powerstat, insofar as there are such things? That is, you lose access to superhuman Attributes as your Humanity increases, but also get rid of some social penalties and possibly power-consumption issues?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242353#post242353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opening, closing, and chapter fiction that is as good as the original stuff. I swear to God, the people who loved Promethean must have started with the fiction, and those who don't must have skipped it. The fiction in that book is, I think, some of the best the World of Darkness has ever had.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm rereading that fiction now, and let me just say hells yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 08-28-2014, 04:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T01:17:37-07:00","id":242902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242875#post242875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satchel is good peeps.<br /> <br /> Course, given how involved he stays with threads like these, I also sympathize when he decides to play harsh.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as I remember he's like Wikipedia, it's fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T04:37:52-07:00","id":242981,"title":"","content":"I dislike the Humanity as powerstat idea - you're essentially removing powerful, low Humanity antagonists. You can still do a lot with Humanity - use it with Azoth to determine Disquiet and other effects, give more incentives for raising it - but as a flat powerstat it doesn't work well. <br /> <br /> Also, if we're talking fiction, I want more Verney. Also more Oleg, but he got his story in the Horror Recognition Guide so I reckon he's about done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T04:59:01-07:00","id":243007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242981#post242981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike the Humanity as powerstat idea - you're essentially removing powerful, low Humanity antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you, though?<br /> <br /> It's possible to be a formidable antagonist with a low powerstat. I mean, it's a question of Attributes and Transmutations and so on, surely? <hr /><br /> <br /> Ooh, here's an idea (largely unrelated to the above.) What if the limiting factor on Transmutations was not raw power, but control? That is, the roll is not to successfully <i>produce</i> the effect, but to stop it killing everyone in a ten-yard radius.<br /> <br /> That would work better with the themes, as well as the idea that Transmutations are based around studying the Divine Fire in preparation for the New Dawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":".  phrasing 08-28-2014, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T05:51:45-07:00","id":243033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=243007#post243007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you, though?<br /> <br /> It's possible to be a formidable antagonist with a low powerstat. I mean, it's a question of Attributes and Transmutations and so on, surely? <hr /><br /> <br /> Ooh, here's an idea (largely unrelated to the above.) What if the limiting factor on Transmutations was not raw power, but control? That is, the roll is not to successfully <i>produce</i> the effect, but to stop it killing everyone in a ten-yard radius.<br /> <br /> That would work better with the whole &quot;pilgrimage&quot; thing, as well as the idea that Transmutations are based around studying the Divine Fire in preparation for the New Dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very true, but Azoth is (under current rules) used for a lot of Transmutation dicepools. And if we look at B&amp;S, BP's been made to have more benefits than increasing the attribute cap (which actually does limit antagonists under this system, though admittedly not by much), which would almost certainly follow for Azoth under the new rules. Admittedly, a lot of vampire stuff flat out doesn't convert - the Predatory Aura, physical bonuses when Frenzying (well, maybe this one), improved Kindred senses... but since powerstat has also doubled as Supernatural Resistance Trait it's also making your low Humanity antagonist vulnerable to all kinds of supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> You also lose the very different and very interesting combos of high Azoth and low Humanity, the potentially amazing low Azoth high Humanity, the trickier high both and low both... If Disquiet end s up married to Azoth and modulated by Humanity those combos become mechanically interesting too. In any case, I can't see them doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T08:36:31-07:00","id":243160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=243033#post243033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very true, but Azoth is (under current rules) used for a lot of Transmutation dicepools. And if we look at B&amp;S, BP's been made to have more benefits than increasing the attribute cap (which actually does limit antagonists under this system, though admittedly not by much), which would almost certainly follow for Azoth under the new rules. Admittedly, a lot of vampire stuff flat out doesn't convert - the Predatory Aura, physical bonuses when Frenzying (well, maybe this one), improved Kindred senses...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yeah, I was assuming the benefits/costs were inverted as I described above.<br /> <br /> So high Humanity starts to (say) restrict superhuman Attributes, or reduce a Promethean's resistance to damage in a fashion analogous to Kindred Senses (oh, that needs fixing, incidentally, it doesn't work now) at high levels; while you might run into (say) social penalties or increased Pyros consumption at lower levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> since powerstat has also doubled as Supernatural Resistance Trait it's also making your low Humanity antagonist vulnerable to all kinds of supernatural powers. </div> </div> </div>I suppose so. But - in my (admittedly limited) experience? - defensive superpowers are usually the most important defense at high levels, with Supernatural Tolerance being more of a perk.<br /> <br /> Still, it's a good point ... hmm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You also lose the very different and very interesting combos of high Azoth and low Humanity, the potentially amazing low Azoth high Humanity, the trickier high both and low both... </div> </div> </div>Do you, though? I still think that the <i>impact</i> of high or low Azoth is almost entirely mediated by the fact that high-Azoth characters tend to be simply <i>more powerful,</i> being built with more XP.<br /> <br /> You can still pull off those combos: but now, it's &quot;high Transmutations low Humanity, the potentially amazing low Transmutations high Humanity, and the trickier high both and low both.&quot; Indeed, there is now a bit of a <i>tradeoff</i> between the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T10:15:36-07:00","id":243254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=243160#post243160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose so. But - in my (admittedly limited) experience? - defensive superpowers are usually the most important defense at high levels, with Supernatural Tolerance being more of a perk.<br /> <br /> Still, it's a good point ... hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supternatural Tolerance penalises nearly every mind-controlling power across the gamelines, as well as a few other ones. I don't like the idea of the powerful low Humanity Promethean being easily puppeteered (though one can make interesting arguments re: their lacking soul) since a player with access to the right power can make them sit up and beg. Even if this is played down for Promethean, crossovers happen and the nWoD rules have always been written to allow them.<br /> <br /> And how will Humanity interact with Pyros? Will lower Humanity allow you to store more, like high Azoth? That also affects the Transmutations-as-power. I think you're putting far too much on Humanity and I don't think it needs this - the powerstat system is simple and works.<br /> <br /> To further explain what I mean by the Azoth/Humanity pairups... I like that, with Azothic Radiance the way it is, Prometheans can <i>feel</i> a high Azoth Promethean coming. There's some of the instinctive, Vampire-like, bigger-fish sensing. I like the fact that high Azoth is a problem for high Humanity-Prometheans, who face nastier Disquiet and Wastelands despite being so close to Humanity, so they'll want to bleed it off even though doing so weakens them. Equally, I like that the further gone or outright monstrous Prometheans are less inclined to care and might live in their Wastelands (until it gets too bad even for them) like horrific Fisher Kings, Tsar Bomba style.<br /> <br /> Azoth covers a lot, and I don't think we can translate it all into Humanity without overburdening it and making a weird power disparity (that's what Beast: The Primordial is going to do, for one thing, but Beast will have it swinging within a given session, Promethean wouldn't). Even if we have low Humanity as the powerful end, with more Pyros and stronger Wasteland effects, it's still taking away the idea that a Promethean who is trying and evolving as a person still struggles with the Promethean condition and the kindling fire inside them.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, Promethean needs some clever rules and to throw out some traditional ideas and I love people throwing theirs out on here, but I just don't think the powerstat is one of them. If nothing else, it's going to make future supplements harder to write, mechanically incompatabile with past ones and make any crossovers a nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T11:38:06-07:00","id":243304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=238467#post238467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;&gt; Promethean has a strong reputation, mentioned above, as 'the greatest game no one plays', and I think a part of that is because 'you are an unwanted abomination that's wandering the world trying to become human' is a more difficult sell than 'you're a wizard screwing around with reality' or 'you're a vampire playing politics with other vampires'. It's erudite, it's esoteric, it's quite beautiful... but it does not make it easy to convince players to try it. <b>Right now Promethean is sort of the game that appeals to Lit Majors and no one else.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>As a Lit Major: nah, it's pretty unplayable to us, too.<br /> <br /> Hoping that changes, though, because it's great fun to read.<br /> <br /> Edit: I disagree that &quot;toning down the philosophy&quot; is the way to go about that, though. I just think there are mechanical ways to encourage the sorts of themes and stories that promethean is made to tell that don't amount to &quot;the game near-literally beats you in the face unless you play it exactly this way at all times&quot;. That doesn't necessarily entail a philosophical change at all, so much as somewhat less hamfisted mechanics. Say what you want about how disquiet and wasteland reinforce the themes (because they do!), they just do it in a really inelegant, clumsy, and frustrating way.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your character is frustrated, so you should be frustrated too&quot; is a really bad design principle for a <i>game</i>, because 9 times out of 10 the player will say &quot;Okay, then as someone who does this in their spare time for fun, I guess I'd rather be playing someone less frustrated&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 08-28-2014, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T16:08:23-07:00","id":243475,"title":"","content":"Re: Humanity (renamed?) as Powerstat / Disquiet (renamed?) as Morality.<br /> <br /> You would obviously have to adjust Humanity, Torment, Disquiet and Azoth to accomodate that change. I am talking about basically renaming Azoth Humanity and making it tie heavily into the Pilgrimage, not shoehorning a Morality Trait into a Powerstat because why. I am suggesting this because I feel the key to making the philisophical elements of Promthean accessible is to make taking the Pilgrimage <i>feel</i> good and invite people to participate it with rewards.<br /> <br /> A lot of Promethean's accessibility issues is that everything related to its deep and meaningful philosophy is focused around constantly punishing the player. Disquiet punishes the player. Humanity is an XP sink that doesn't really add much. Etc etc etc. Need your carrots too. Really, Satchel's pointing out that it makes delaying the journey harder just highlights my point. If your game has a design goal of &quot;let the players ignore the major themes of the game&quot; then <i>something</i> is wrong.<br /> <br /> As for the thematic of &quot;potential for change&quot; etc etc etc. Watch. *waves hands* And suddenly, its fixed. Joys of writing a new edition is that you can change things. In this particular case you wouldn't even need to change that much. Just correlate ability to catalyze a human soul with the potential for change and bam, done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 08-28-2014, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T16:29:50-07:00","id":243481,"title":"","content":"Re: Low Humanity Antagonists<br /> <br /> How many elders do you throw at your players, really? I know most of my antagonists tend to range in the Powerstat 1-3 range, with 5 being the outliers and 6+ being &quot;Oh my God Why.&quot; Usually the 6+ Powerstat is used in foreshadowing and the real reason they are bad juju is because of the uber quantity of powers and size of their dicepools that implies. Supernatural Tolorance is a thing, but that can be taken care of with a merit.<br /> <br /> I mean hell, if you really want Monstrous Power at odds with Humanity. Get a 5-dot or 4-dot merit (purchasable with normal EXP, so pilgrimage not a requirement). Make it count your Humanity as +1 higher for some purposes. Make it purchasable multiple times but interfere with the pilgrimage and probably link it with the pandarans or something. Power now, but its not going to help your pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And how will Humanity interact with Pyros? Will lower Humanity allow you to store more, like high Azoth? That also affects the Transmutations-as-power. I think you're putting far too much on Humanity and I don't think it needs this - the powerstat system is simple and works. </div> </div> </div>Wut. Why would you have a powerstat that reduces your power? It'd react with Pyros like any other powerstat interacts with the fuel stat. Humanity in this context = Ability to Catalyze a Human Soul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To further explain what I mean by the Azoth/Humanity pairups... I like that, with Azothic Radiance the way it is, Prometheans can <i>feel</i> a high Azoth Promethean coming. There's some of the instinctive, Vampire-like, bigger-fish sensing. </div> </div> </div>That was removed from Vampire for a reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like the fact that high Azoth is a problem for high Humanity-Prometheans, who face nastier Disquiet and Wastelands despite being so close to Humanity, so they'll want to bleed it off even though doing so weakens them. Equally, I like that the further gone or outright monstrous Prometheans are less inclined to care and might live in their Wastelands (until it gets too bad even for them) like horrific Fisher Kings, Tsar Bomba style. </div> </div> </div>Azoth being a problem for high humanity Prometheans is part of the problem. Progressing Mechanically should almost never be at odds with Progressing Narratively. If you do that, then you get all the problems Promethean currently has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T16:55:22-07:00","id":243489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=243254#post243254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supternatural Tolerance penalises nearly every mind-controlling power across the gamelines, as well as a few other ones. I don't like the idea of the powerful low Humanity Promethean being easily puppeteered (though one can make interesting arguments re: their lacking soul) since a player with access to the right power can make them sit up and beg. Even if this is played down for Promethean, crossovers happen and the nWoD rules have always been written to allow them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this sounds like a really interesting plot hook, myself. The big bad brainwashes an old, powerful Promethean who recently spent time in the Wastes to cool his Azoth, and the players must find a way to break the spell. Not saying it should be the norm, of course, but food for thought. <hr /><br /> What do you guys want to see in terms of Virtue and Vice? I would like to see them evolve into something else, like B&amp;S did with your Mask and Dirge.<br /> <br /> I think one of them should be replaced by something relating to the <b>reason</b> the Promethean was created, perhaps called Impetus. Unlike basically anyone else, Prometheans have a baked in raison d'etre that I think should make an impact on the character. If they were created as a companion, maybe they restore Willpower when they comfort someone, or maybe if they were made to be a soldier they regain Willpower when winning a fight. Thus Prometheans can find solace in the reason they were made -- but is that truly a way forward on the Pilgrimage? What they were made for could get in the way of what they want to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","user":"Metamurpho","date":". 10-15-2014, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T19:16:34-07:00","id":243543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=243475#post243475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the thematic of &quot;potential for change&quot; etc etc etc. Watch. *waves hands* And suddenly, its fixed. Joys of writing a new edition is that you can change things. In this particular case you wouldn't even need to change that much. Just correlate ability to catalyze a human soul with the potential for change and bam, done.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem then becomes <i>that is unspeakably lazy and ill-fitting and &quot;they can just make it work tho&quot; is the most useless thing to assume in conversations like this.</i><br /> <br /> The point of the second editions is to <i>refine the concepts that the first editions developed across the initial run and in the intervening years. </i>In the game as currently written, being powerful makes it more likely that <i>your transformation will be one of the exceptional rarities</i> if it should succeed, in addition to making you more likely to birth numerous or powerful monsters from your failures to create progeny or your extended captivity by such monsters.<br /> <br /> It is very important that &quot;humanlike character&quot; and &quot;character with minimal inadvertent supernatural impact on their surroundings&quot; not be inherently part of the same end of the scale - Azoth getting higher is called out as a marker of progress on the Pilgrimage in no small part because <i>it makes things harder for the character by attracting all manner of terrible things</i>.<br /> <br /> Decoupling the Disquieting aura from how supernaturally powerful a Promethean is doesn't thematically gel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T20:29:53-07:00","id":243582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=243481#post243481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Low Humanity Antagonists<br /> <br /> That was removed from Vampire for a reason.<br /> <br /> Azoth being a problem for high humanity Prometheans is part of the problem. Progressing Mechanically should almost never be at odds with Progressing Narratively. If you do that, then you get all the problems Promethean currently has.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that it was removed from Vampire in the new edition, doesn't the negate the fact that it happened, and that the writers (and I assume, multitudes of players) found it to be an enjoyable gameplay element for at time. We shouldn't scoff at old ideas, simply for being old. I dont feel like Promethean needs the thematic weight of feeling a &quot;Big Fish comming&quot;, but I found it thematically apropriate in Vampire.<br /> DISCLAIMER: I never played Vampire, but I could imagine that the entire predatory aura thing, might become a grind in-game. Despite its perhaps lacking gameplay weight, I still found it thematically pleasing.<br /> <br /> To suggest that a high Azoth score becomming a problem, is in themtic conflict with its Pilgrimage nearing its end, is missing out on the nature of Azoth. Azoth was never a gauge of the Prometheans experience with interacting with Humanity, nor his understanding thereof. Azoth is rather a gauge of his inner stores of refined Pyros, his inner fire that keeps him animate. It is this inner fire and his unnatural animation, that causes mortals to fall victim to Disquiet, and which flares out to scour the world around him, coursing the Wasteland. A Promethean can potentially (although not likely) have 10 Azoth, and be no closer to finding Humanity than the day he first opened his eyes.<br /> A Promethean with high Humanity and high Azoth will still be at odds with Humanity, because although his understanding of the Human condition has improved tremendously over the cause of his Pilgrimage, our understanding of him have not improved by as much as a hairs thickness. We're still scared and hateful towards the zombie-man who just spend the greater part of two centuries traveling the world studying and admireing us, even as his understanding soon will allow to become one of us.<br /> If high Humanity could cancel out the effects of Azoth, what that mechanic effectively says is; &quot;Your knowledge and understanding of the Human condition alone, is enough to quell the unnatural fear and aversion they feel for you&quot;. There would be little need for a true Magnum Opus, because the Promethean would allready be able to reap the majority of the rewards of this project, solely by virtue of increasing his Humanity.<br /> As it stands currently, Humanity does play a big part in the Prometheans abillity to become Human, although Azoth still burns. It'll burn - and by proxy invoke Disquiet - untill the moment that the transformative fire undoes the Prometheans unlife, and turns it into true life. Its a constant, likely ever increasing, reminder of all the Promethean has to gain from his Pilgrimage and all that he is trying to escape. If you allowed that feeling to be subverted by merely raising your Humanity, you'd slay one of the cornerstones of Promethean as it stands.<br /> If you feel like this cornerstone is detrimental to Promethean as it stands, I cant fault you for it. Thats a matter of taste. However, I dont personally believe that it is detrimental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T22:10:02-07:00","id":243638,"title":"","content":"I could see an argument for inverting the roles of Azoth and Humanity in the New Dawn: you need a high Azoth in order to have the necessary transformative power to become human (i.e., base the Crucible roll off of Azoth instead of Humanity); but without a high Humanity, you\u2019ll end up as a homeless amnesiac whose life is little better than a Promethean\u2019s. <i>With</i> a high Humanity, you retain your memories, find a place in human society, and possibly even end up representing the best that humanity has to offer. See my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230709#post230709\">earlier post</a> for how I\u2019d revise the \u201cfinal Azoth roll\u201d; but substitute \u201cHumanity\u201d for \u201cAzoth\u201d as the basis for the extended roll\u2019s pool. <br /> <br /> But I see no benefit from reversing their roles (even partially) anywhere else. Until a developer says that he\u2019s considering using Humanity as a power stat, that\u2019s my last word on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-29-2014, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T06:36:23-07:00","id":243848,"title":"","content":"I've more/less beaten the frankenstinian horse as much as is useful for this discussion.<br /> <br /> Regardless of how it is handled. The take away is that progressing needs to feel good and be rewarded in a mechanical sense, regardless of how that is accomplished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T06:46:56-07:00","id":243853,"title":"","content":"True enough. Fortunately, it already is: we already have Milestones, the completion of which grant Vitriol awards which can be used to improve Humanity, among other things. If Matt decides to start Humanity low and give it an upper trajectory, much like Memory in <b>Mummy</b>, it wouldn\u2019t hurt to have at least some of these Milestones grant whole Experiences worth of Vitriol or even dots of Humanity; but that\u2019s something that will come out in playtest. <br /> <br /> One thing I\u2019d like to see would be for Milestones to become more Condition-like, granting Beats of Vitriol whenever the Promethean makes substantial progress toward resolving a given Milestone and then granting more Vitriol upon actually resolving it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T06:49:46-07:00","id":243855,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I can't help but wonder now about Prometheans and the social construct of &quot;race&quot;. I mean, on one hand Disquiet is Disquiet regardless of the politics surrounding a Promethean's skin; but on the other hand there's something to be said for the potential intersection of the Promethean experience and... say... how black children are perceived differently than white children (<a href=\"http://www.apa.org/news/press/releases/2014/03/black-boys-older.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.apa.org/news/press/releas...oys-older.aspx</a>) or perception of how pain is experienced (<a href=\"http://www.plosone.org/article/info%3Adoi%2F10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0048546\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.plosone.org/article/info%...l.pone.0048546</a>). And those are just the issues of psychological perception, to say nothing of over discrimination in arrest/conviction/sentencing rates for the same crimes, or the hireability of people with identical qualifications.<br /> <br /> It makes me wonder how a Promethean after the New Dawn is prone to view their own treatment based on race - whether they're desensitized to it having experienced so much worse as a Promethean, or more likely to be outraged at still being &quot;Othered&quot; despite everything they went through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T06:57:50-07:00","id":243860,"title":"","content":"My biggest disappointment with Promethean (which I mostly love, mind you) back in the day was the scarcity of Demiurges. I had initially thought the game would feature a combination of human obsessives and Promethean reproduction; just kind of an ongoing phenomenon where occasionally someone became so obsessed they touched the Divine and sparked flawed life out of stolen corpses.<br /> <br /> So I want to see demiurges being something that just sometimes happens, not a &quot;once in a century&quot; sort of deal, such that any old Promethean might have been made by another Promethean or by a human. <br /> <br /> I would like to see lineages based on the Tulpa and Talos myths (group demiurges acting through meditation for the former and corpses-with-clockwork-parts for the latter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T07:59:17-07:00","id":243932,"title":"","content":"I dunno, I'm kinda fond of the once in a millennium stroke of genius. It was a nice touch, atmospherically, that helped the sense of isolation and distance and drift. I also like what it suggest about Demiurges to begin with, which some people seem to forget in all their love of mad science-Demiurges are <i>completely fucked up in the head.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T08:10:25-07:00","id":243973,"title":"","content":"While there\u2019s something to that, I don\u2019t like the fact that once-in-a-millenium demiurges means that <i>I don\u2019t get to play</i> the creation of a demiurge. The only \u201cparent/child\u201d-type relationship the game currently gives any support for is Promethean/Promethean \u2014 save only for the \u201cdemiurge\u201d stuff in <b>Saturnine Night</b>, which implicitly violates the notion of rarer-than-hen\u2019s-teeth demiurges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T08:31:33-07:00","id":243986,"title":"","content":"I...don't buy the <i>I don't get to play the creation of the Progenitor</i> argument.<br /> <br /> Like, nothing stops you from playing a Demiurge. Just because only a handful of people do it doesn't mean you can't play out your own story.<br /> <br /> Saturnine Night didn't violate the notion of rarer-than-hen's-teeth, beyond implying that within the last century some more people have been successful than before(which was kind of needed in order to make the Zeka and Unfleshed work), because they are still rare-it's just that where opportunity was limited before, now there's more room for the chance.<br /> <br /> Not to advocate a shit ton of of Demiurges,because I think they should be rare, less than 20 in the whole of history to now if I have to slap a number on it, but I think the big thing Saturnine Night did was show that opportunity was denied to a lot of people up until the last century with the technological boom. I think there were...well, not a lot of people, but a proportional number of people(to waht we see in modern day) who <i>could have</i> <i>been</i> Demiurges have always existed throughout the ages, it's just that the depths of alchemy/mad science are hard to work for most, and most just didn't even have a chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T10:45:51-07:00","id":244171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=243855#post243855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes me wonder how a Promethean after the New Dawn is prone to view their own treatment based on race - whether they're desensitized to it having experienced so much worse as a Promethean, or more likely to be outraged at still being &quot;Othered&quot; despite everything they went through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obligatory \u201cvaries by individual Redeemed\u201d disclaimer.<br /> <br /> To me the interesting way of looking at this question is not \u201cwhy would Redeemed agree with my values\u201d but \u201cwhy would they not.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I could easily imagine a Mimic who systematically learns about different races and consciously chooses a race without paying attention to their own skin colour (which may be rock, marble or patchwork). The New Dawn turns them into whichever race they selected.<br /> <br /> While this Promethian would obviously know that (Michael Jackson aside) people generally can't choose their skin colour. It would be interesting to speculate on what they might think of race in general.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another possibility, one I'm particularly fond of, is a Mimic (Mimics are good for this topic) who comes to the conclusion that the way people treat others is an inevitable side effect of in-group bonding; and thus accepts buying into the system as the price of being accepted by somebody \u2013 a massive improvement over the Promethian reality of being accepted by nobody.<br /> <br /> I like this one because it really captures the idea of a Promethian becoming human \u2013 rather than superhuman \u2013 while leaving clear room for further development in the next stage of the pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just a little brain-spew. All I think I can say is generally applicable is that Redeemed will probably learn the basics race, well in/out group dynamics in general, during their time as Promethians and that I find looking for the Redeemed's unique viewpoint is more interesting than trying to say which regular human viewpoint they'd agree with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T19:11:53-07:00","id":245129,"title":"","content":"Hey, I just wanted to say, I read through Chapter One today (Refinements &amp; Lineages), and I'm liking what I'm seeing. The biggest changes you'll see, so far (apart from that whole &quot;we added a new Refinement&quot; thing), is that the Tammuz focus more on language and being word-bound, because the whole &quot;artificial person&quot; thing that resonates with golems is really bound up with the Unfleshed. <br /> <br /> Going to be playtesting soon. Might want to watch for the AP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T19:35:28-07:00","id":245141,"title":"","content":"Tease!<br /> <br /> If I can make a request, if not for core book, then as a suggestion for within another, is having Alchemists be a minor template to the Prometheans. They both parrallel and directly oppose the idea of Prometheans - while the latter wants to become more human, the former wants to become less. It gives a whole 'humanism vs. transhumanism' angle to play which I would find delicious!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T00:33:14-07:00","id":245215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=245129#post245129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I just wanted to say, I read through Chapter One today (Refinements &amp; Lineages), and I'm liking what I'm seeing. The biggest changes you'll see, so far (apart from that whole &quot;we added a new Refinement&quot; thing), is that the Tammuz focus more on language and being word-bound, because the whole &quot;artificial person&quot; thing that resonates with golems is really bound up with the Unfleshed.<br /> <br /> Going to be playtesting soon. Might want to watch for the AP.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. If you look at the origional legend of Rabbi Loew - the Golem wasn't really defined by slavery, in fact he had to be treated with respect and rested every Sabbath. Meanwhile the focus on language and words ties in nicely with both the emet and kabbala. Provided golems are typically made out of clay and not corpses I'm happy with this change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T06:50:26-07:00","id":246119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=245141#post245141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tease!<br /> <br /> If I can make a request, if not for core book, then as a suggestion for within another, is having Alchemists be a minor template to the Prometheans. They both parrallel and directly oppose the idea of Prometheans - while the latter wants to become more human, the former wants to become less. It gives a whole 'humanism vs. transhumanism' angle to play which I would find delicious!</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemists are actually included...as antagonists. We very deliberately decided against a minor template for Prometheans, because I wanted to emphasize how alone they are. (For a game with a more &quot;the gang's all here&quot; kind of approach, <b>Beast</b> is coming soon.) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T09:21:00-07:00","id":246187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=243860#post243860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see lineages based on the Tulpa and Talos myths (group demiurges acting through meditation for the former and corpses-with-clockwork-parts for the latter).</div> </div> </div> </div> Considering we're getting Unfleshed as a core Lineage now, I think you're getting your wish on at least one of those. (You might be able to argue group-meditation Tulpas are a kind of Extempore, and thus you've gotten both those wishes, but that's pushing things.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=243254#post243254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supternatural Tolerance penalises nearly every mind-controlling power across the gamelines, as well as a few other ones. I don't like the idea of the powerful low Humanity Promethean being easily puppeteered (though one can make interesting arguments re: their lacking soul) since a player with access to the right power can make them sit up and beg. Even if this is played down for Promethean, crossovers happen and the nWoD rules have always been written to allow them.<br /> <br /> And how will Humanity interact with Pyros? Will lower Humanity allow you to store more, like high Azoth? That also affects the Transmutations-as-power. I think you're putting far too much on Humanity and I don't think it needs this - the powerstat system is simple and works.<br /> <br /> To further explain what I mean by the Azoth/Humanity pairups... I like that, with Azothic Radiance the way it is, Prometheans can <i>feel</i> a high Azoth Promethean coming. There's some of the instinctive, Vampire-like, bigger-fish sensing. I like the fact that high Azoth is a problem for high Humanity-Prometheans, who face nastier Disquiet and Wastelands despite being so close to Humanity, so they'll want to bleed it off even though doing so weakens them. Equally, I like that the further gone or outright monstrous Prometheans are less inclined to care and might live in their Wastelands (until it gets too bad even for them) like horrific Fisher Kings, Tsar Bomba style.<br /> <br /> Azoth covers a lot, and I don't think we can translate it all into Humanity without overburdening it and making a weird power disparity (that's what Beast: The Primordial is going to do, for one thing, but Beast will have it swinging within a given session, Promethean wouldn't). Even if we have low Humanity as the powerful end, with more Pyros and stronger Wasteland effects, it's still taking away the idea that a Promethean who is trying and evolving as a person still struggles with the Promethean condition and the kindling fire inside them.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, Promethean needs some clever rules and to throw out some traditional ideas and I love people throwing theirs out on here, but I just don't think the powerstat is one of them. If nothing else, it's going to make future supplements harder to write, mechanically incompatabile with past ones and make any crossovers a nightmare.</div> </div> </div> </div>... hmm. Yeah, I think you're right on this one. (We still need some way to make IC progress on the Pilgrimage equal, not oppose, OOC progress with XP ... but I guess maybe this isn't it.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=243489#post243489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys want to see in terms of Virtue and Vice? I would like to see them evolve into something else, like B&amp;S did with your Mask and Dirge.<br /> <br /> I think one of them should be replaced by something relating to the <b>reason</b> the Promethean was created, perhaps called Impetus. Unlike basically anyone else, Prometheans have a baked in raison d'etre that I think should make an impact on the character. If they were created as a companion, maybe they restore Willpower when they comfort someone, or maybe if they were made to be a soldier they regain Willpower when winning a fight. This Prometheans can find solace in the reason they were made -- but is that truly a way forward on the Pilgrimage? What they were made for could get in the way of what they want to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>... huh. Giving each Promethean a unique Torment that replaces Virtue or Vice?<br /> <br /> It's so crazy it might just work.<br /> <br /> (Off the top of my head, I'd suggest Origin, make it the Vice-replacement; and have Destination - an personal image of their New Dawn - as the Virtue-replacement.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=243638#post243638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see an argument for inverting the roles of Azoth and Humanity in the New Dawn: you need a high Azoth in order to have the necessary transformative power to become human (i.e., base the Crucible roll off of Azoth instead of Humanity); but without a high Humanity, you\u2019ll end up as a homeless amnesiac whose life is little better than a Promethean\u2019s. <i>With</i> a high Humanity, you retain your memories, find a place in human society, and possibly even end up representing the best that humanity has to offer. See my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=230709#post230709\">earlier post</a> for how I\u2019d revise the \u201cfinal Azoth roll\u201d; but substitute \u201cHumanity\u201d for \u201cAzoth\u201d as the basis for the extended roll\u2019s pool.<br /> <br /> But I see no benefit from reversing their roles (even partially) anywhere else. Until a developer says that he\u2019s considering using Humanity as a power stat, that\u2019s my last word on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Ah</i>, I like this.<br /> <br /> You could simply declare that one's Azoth has to reach 10 before the fires are hot enough to refine the dross of a Promethean into gold. Then, as you say, have an extended Crucible roll to determine how much of the Promethean comes through the process intact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T10:18:45-07:00","id":246208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246187#post246187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Considering we're getting Unfleshed as a core Lineage now, I think you're getting your wish on at least one of those. (You might be able to argue group-meditation Tulpas are a kind of Extempore, and thus you've gotten both those wishes, but that's pushing things.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Tulpas are dream-born Created. Nothing particularly special about them besides their origin and the way they interact with dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T10:29:15-07:00","id":246212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246119#post246119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemists are actually included...as antagonists. We very deliberately decided against a minor template for Prometheans, because I wanted to emphasize how alone they are. (For a game with a more &quot;the gang's all here&quot; kind of approach, <b>Beast</b> is coming soon.) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So how would you include Calogero in the Firestorm Chronicles?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T10:48:15-07:00","id":246234,"title":"","content":"Again, don\u2019t forget the Milestones: if they\u2019re being kept, progress on your Pilgrimage can be measured in terms of how many Milestones are left to complete. Admittedly, since the Storyteller is the only one who <i>knows</i> what Milestones you have yet to complete, it\u2019s not a measurement that the player is aware of. Sure, he knows how many Milestones he has completed already; but he doesn\u2019t know how many are left. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not comfortable with a hard-and-fast rule such as \u201conce you reach Azoth 10, you can become a mortal\u201d. All I was suggesting was to replace Humanity with Azoth in the Crucible roll \u2014 and I\u2019d amend that with a penalty for each Milestone you\u2019ve yet to reach \u2014 <i>not</i> any sort of absolute criteria that <i>must</i> be met. You may attempt the Crucible roll any time you like, subject to Storyteller veto if he thinks you\u2019re nowhere close to ready. High Azoth and completed Milestones are indicators that you\u2019re <i>probably</i> ready; but it should be theoretically possible to Redeem with as little as a single dot of Azoth. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d be half-inclined to make the Crucible roll be the one roll in the game that can be reduced <i>below</i> a Chance Die. If the dice penalties would reduce the dice pool below zero, you cannot succeed: either the Storyteller tells you this flat out, or he lets you roll a single die anyway \u2014 but a 10 <i>doesn\u2019t</i> count as a success, and you have to roll higher than the amount the penalties exceeded the dice pool in order to avoid a botch (e.g., if your dice pool was reduced to -3, the \u201dbotch threshold\u201d is 3, not 1). And a botch on the Crucible roll should be a <i>really</i> bad thing, ranging from losing a dot of Humanity to gaining a new Milestone to having your Milestones be <i>reset</i>, forcing you to restart your Pilgrimage from scratch. You do <i>not</i> attempt the Crucible until you\u2019re ready.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T11:30:12-07:00","id":246255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246234#post246234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not comfortable with a hard-and-fast rule such as \u201conce you reach Azoth 10, you can become a mortal\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I meant that as &quot;you have to reach Azoth 10 in order to TRY and become mortal&quot;. You shouldn't <i>have</i> to (that would eliminate Azoth 10 from play in practice), and personally I would allow characters to fail the extended Humanity roll completely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246208#post246208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tulpas are dream-born Created. Nothing particularly special about them besides their origin and the way they interact with dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to the idea of a &quot;tupa&quot; - in the legendary sense - being born out of group meditation. Which I think I could see as an origin for an Extempore-Lineage character in the new edition, although we haven't been given many details on how they've changed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246234#post246234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, don\u2019t forget the Milestones: if they\u2019re being kept, progress on your Pilgrimage can be measured in terms of how many Milestones are left to complete. Admittedly, since the Storyteller is the only one who <i>knows</i> what Milestones you have yet to complete, it\u2019s not a measurement that the player is aware of. Sure, he knows how many Milestones he has completed already; but he doesn\u2019t know how many are left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.<br /> <br /> Did anyone else think Aspirations and Mage 2.0's Obsessions were a natural idea for Milestones in the new edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T11:49:04-07:00","id":246265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246255#post246255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I meant that as &quot;you have to reach Azoth 10 in order to TRY and become mortal&quot;. You shouldn't <i>have</i> to (that would eliminate Azoth 10 from play in practice), and personally I would allow characters to fail the extended Humanity roll completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>First: I\u2019m against requiring Azoth 10 in order to be able to Redeem: both Azoth and Humanity should <i>help</i> with different aspects of the New Dawn; but neither should be required to be 10. <br /> <br /> Second: the new GMC Extended Action rules always allow for the possibility of failure, since you can never keep rolling indefinitely. Set the required successes at 15, and someone with Humanity 7 will have roughly even odds of reaching the threshold before running out of rolls. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246255#post246255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.<br /> <br /> Did anyone else think Aspirations and Mage 2.0's Obsessions were a natural idea for Milestones in the new edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>I considered it; but I think that Conditions would be a better model \u2014 like the Agenda Conditions in <b>Demon</b>, but unique to each Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-01-2014, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T12:52:02-07:00","id":246331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246119#post246119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemists are actually included...as antagonists. We very deliberately decided against a minor template for Prometheans, because I wanted to emphasize how alone they are. (For a game with a more &quot;the gang's all here&quot; kind of approach, <b>Beast</b> is coming soon.) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is nice to hear. I understand that Prometheans are alone and I agree with that approach, but I do want to see the 'magic of the Promethean universe' explored, and I think presenting alchemists in a bigger light will help with that.<br /> <br /> Vampire was also bland to me until Wicked Dead and B&amp;S because they really expanded the 'magic of the Vampire universe.' Promethean has a lot if you know where to look (mostly Pandora's Book, IIRC) but I just want to see to expanded and given more of a spotlight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T01:30:08-07:00","id":246703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246187#post246187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... huh. Giving each Promethean a unique Torment that replaces Virtue or Vice?<br /> <br /> It's so crazy it might just work.<br /> <br /> (Off the top of my head, I'd suggest Origin, make it the Vice-replacement; and have Destination - an personal image of their New Dawn - as the Virtue-replacement.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Origin, Catalyst, Impetus -- I think they all work, and glad you dig the idea. And while I understand wanting the flip side of this to be involved too, I would worry that Destination would &quot;lock in&quot; what you want to be. I think Prometheans change their minds a lot about what the want out of the New Dawn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246234#post246234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, don\u2019t forget the Milestones: if they\u2019re being kept, progress on your Pilgrimage can be measured in terms of how many Milestones are left to complete. Admittedly, since the Storyteller is the only one who <i>knows</i> what Milestones you have yet to complete, it\u2019s not a measurement that the player is aware of. Sure, he knows how many Milestones he has completed already; but he doesn\u2019t know how many are left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget about the size of said Milestones, too -- per the core, they're supposed to vary in Vitriol reward.<br /> <br /> And you know what would be awesome? Milestones/Burdens expressed as Conditions. Sometimes they'd be secret, sometimes the player would know about them... fun stuff to figure out. Not all of them, of course, but I think Conditions will fit very nicely into Promethean 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246234#post246234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not comfortable with a hard-and-fast rule such as \u201conce you reach Azoth 10, you can become a mortal\u201d. All I was suggesting was to replace Humanity with Azoth in the Crucible roll \u2014 and I\u2019d amend that with a penalty for each Milestone you\u2019ve yet to reach \u2014 <i>not</i> any sort of absolute criteria that <i>must</i> be met. You may attempt the Crucible roll any time you like, subject to Storyteller veto if he thinks you\u2019re nowhere close to ready. High Azoth and completed Milestones are indicators that you\u2019re <i>probably</i> ready; but it should be theoretically possible to Redeem with as little as a single dot of Azoth.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d be half-inclined to make the Crucible roll be the one roll in the game that can be reduced <i>below</i> a Chance Die. If the dice penalties would reduce the dice pool below zero, you cannot succeed: either the Storyteller tells you this flat out, or he lets you roll a single die anyway \u2014 but a 10 <i>doesn\u2019t</i> count as a success, and you have to roll higher than the amount the penalties exceeded the dice pool in order to avoid a botch (e.g., if your dice pool was reduced to -3, the \u201dbotch threshold\u201d is 3, not 1). And a botch on the Crucible roll should be a <i>really</i> bad thing, ranging from losing a dot of Humanity to gaining a new Milestone to having your Milestones be <i>reset</i>, forcing you to restart your Pilgrimage from scratch. You do <i>not</i> attempt the Crucible until you\u2019re ready.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally hate the Crucible roll. Something so monumental to a character and based off mostly plot elements shouldn't be reduced to something that can be mathematically gamed. Sure it's easy enough to excise, but it always rubbed me wrong that there was a most efficient and mathematically sound way to spend your XP to meet the &quot;win condition&quot;. Much more mystery in this department, please!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T02:53:48-07:00","id":246727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246265#post246265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First: I\u2019m against requiring Azoth 10 in order to be able to Redeem: both Azoth and Humanity should <i>help</i> with different aspects of the New Dawn; but neither should be required to be 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T05:56:42-07:00","id":246766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246703#post246703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Origin, Catalyst, Impetus -- I think they all work, and glad you dig the idea. And while I understand wanting the flip side of this to be involved too, I would worry that Destination would &amp;quot;lock in&amp;quot; what you want to be. I think Prometheans change their minds a lot about what the want out of the New Dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides, we already have <i>two</i> mechanisms for \u201cwhat do you want to become?\u201d: Milestones, and the Athanor. <br /> <br /> Go back to the definitions of Virtue and Vice as given in GMC: <br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">\u2022 A character's Virtue should be something that gives her a great sense of self-actualization, but which she is often tempted to ignore. It's her higher calling, the personality trait that would be at the fore all the time if she didn't live in the World of Darkness. It should be both difficult to act upon and make her feel good when she does make the effort.<br /> \u2022 A character's Vice, on the other hand, is a source of short-term comfort and a distraction from the world. Vice should be the easy way out, the sand he buries his head in, like a bully lashing out to avoid his own fear or an alcoholic drinking to forget.</span></div>Now let\u2019s take that \u201cOrigin\u201d idea and apply it to both, thinking of a newly-created Promethean as an organic machine that has yet to achieve any agency. The equivalent of \u201cVirtue\u201d for such a creation would be its <i>Purpose</i>: the role that its creator made it to fill. Filling that role is a higher calling, a means of self-actualization; and fulfilling one\u2019s Purpose serves as a powerful source of positive reinforcement. <br /> <br /> Conversely, the equivalent of \u201cVice\u201d is a reflection of the fact that any time you create something as elaborate and complex as a Promethean, it\u2019s bound to develop unanticipated behaviors: the <i>Quirk</i> represents some aspect of the Promethean\u2019s personality which was <i>not</i> chosen for it by its creator: if this Quirk interferes with the Promethean\u2019s Purpose, it\u2019s typically viewed as a bug or a glitch, and is the sort of thing the creator might spend time and effort trying to purge from his creation. (\u201cQuirk\u201d may not be the best name for it; but hopefully I\u2019ve successfully communicated the idea I\u2019m thinking of.)<br /> <br /> Note also the advice that GMC gives for changing Virtue and Vice. IMHO, Prometheans (being \u201cworks in progress\u201d and conduits for the agent of change known as \u201cPyros\u201d) should have more opportunities to change their Virtue/Vice equivalents: say, every time a Promethean resolves a Milestone, it can change its Purpose and/or Quirk to reflect the revelation that the fulfilled Milestone represents. Which brings me to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246703#post246703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget about the size of said Milestones, too -- per the core, they're supposed to vary in Vitriol reward.<br /> <br /> And you know what would be awesome? Milestones/Burdens expressed as Conditions. Sometimes they'd be secret, sometimes the player would know about them... fun stuff to figure out. Not all of them, of course, but I think Conditions will fit very nicely into Promethean 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, the reason for the varying sizes of Milestones was to allow more momentous milestones to grant better rewards. But with a Milestones-as-Conditions mechanic, that distinction can be phrased as \u201cthe harder you have to work for it, the more you get out of it\u201d \u2014 and that, in turn, can be addressed by having the more \u201cmomentous\u201d Milestones grant more Vitriol Beats leading up to the resolution of the Milestone: as a Persistent Condition, it grants Beats (of Vitriol) whenever the Promethean makes significant progress toward resolving the Milestone. There might not be a need to distinguish between different intensities of Milestones \u2014 or there might be. <br /> <br /> The other thing that I like about the \u201cMilestone as Condition\u201d approach is that the notion of a Burden becomes a natural extension of it: a Burden is merely a Milestone that inflicts some sort of penalty or downside on the Promethean while he\u2019s working to resolve it \u2014 which would give even more opportunities to earn Vitriol, as you\u2019d generate a Beat whenever the Burden complicates matters, not just when you make progress toward resolving it. (For the record, I like the notion of Burdens because they would provide another way besides Disquiet and Wasteland to illustrate the faulty nature of a Promethean \u2014 in this case, through its incompleteness. It would also provide a possible Bane-like mechanic: if you lose a point of Humanity and want to avoid losing more in a similar situation, take on a Burden that reflects the Breaking Point that you want immunity from. Unlike Banes, Burdens would reward you for playing them up, and you\u2019d eventually want to resolve them before attempting the New Dawn: even if the developers decide not to apply penalties to the Crucible roll for unresolved Milestones, Burdens should apply such a penalty. Which brings me to: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246703#post246703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally hate the Crucible roll. Something so monumental to a character and based off mostly plot elements shouldn't be reduced to something that can be mathematically gamed. Sure it's easy enough to excise, but it always rubbed me wrong that there was a most efficient and mathematically sound way to spend your XP to meet the &quot;win condition&quot;. Much more mystery in this department, please!</div> </div> </div> </div>I get where you\u2019re coming from; but I don\u2019t agree: \u201cmathematically gaming\u201d the Crucible roll is about the same in my mind as \u201cmathematically gaming\u201d social influence. I <i>do</i> think more mystery is called for; but I tend to think that it is best introduced by including \u201chidden factors\u201d that the player isn\u2019t privvy to in the Crucible roll (which is why I suggest penalizing the roll for unresolved Milestones) rather than by doing away with the roll entirely, which would force the decision of whether or not the Crucible succeeds entirely into the realm of Storyteller fiat. <br /> <br /> Mind you, I\u2019m OK with both approaches getting coverage in <b>Promethean 2e</b>; but I <i>don\u2019t</i> want to see the Crucible roll option dumped completely because some gaming groups would prefer to handle it sans game mechanics. Which brings me to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246265#post246265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First: I\u2019m against requiring Azoth 10 in order to be able to Redeem: both Azoth and Humanity should <i>help</i> with different aspects of the New Dawn; but neither should be required to be 10.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246727#post246727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradoxically, for a reason very similar to the one just voiced by Metamurpho for doing away with the Crucible roll altogether: the Crucible should become available when story concerns indicate that it makes sense for it to become available, <i>not</i> when a rigid checklist of prerequisites are satisfied. There should be more Storyteller and Player freedom in deciding when it\u2019s appropriate to attempt the Crucible than would be the case if it only became an option upon maximizing one of your character traits. Really, if I had to select one absolute condition that <i>must</i> be met before the Crucible can be attempted, it would be having no Milestones left to resolve, not Azoth 10 or Humanity 10; and even \u201cno Milestones left\u201d strikes me as a needlessly harsh restriction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T12:26:47-07:00","id":247035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246119#post246119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alchemists are actually included...as antagonists. We very deliberately decided against a minor template for Prometheans, because I wanted to emphasize how alone they are. (For a game with a more &quot;the gang's all here&quot; kind of approach, <b>Beast</b> is coming soon.) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Works for me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T13:20:53-07:00","id":247095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246766#post246766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, the equivalent of \u201cVice\u201d is a reflection of the fact that any time you create something as elaborate and complex as a Promethean, it\u2019s bound to develop unanticipated behaviors: the <i>Quirk</i> represents some aspect of the Promethean\u2019s personality which was <i>not</i> chosen for it by its creator: if this Quirk interferes with the Promethean\u2019s Purpose, it\u2019s typically viewed as a bug or a glitch, and is the sort of thing the creator might spend time and effort trying to purge from his creation. (\u201cQuirk\u201d may not be the best name for it; but hopefully I\u2019ve successfully communicated the idea I\u2019m thinking of.)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Fault&quot;, perhaps? I like it, better than my idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Paradoxically, for a reason very similar to the one just voiced by Metamurpho for doing away with the Crucible roll altogether: the Crucible should become available when story concerns indicate that it makes sense for it to become available, <i>not</i> when a rigid checklist of prerequisites are satisfied. There should be more Storyteller and Player freedom in deciding when it\u2019s appropriate to attempt the Crucible than would be the case if it only became an option upon maximizing one of your character traits. Really, if I had to select one absolute condition that <i>must</i> be met before the Crucible can be attempted, it would be having no Milestones left to resolve, not Azoth 10 or Humanity 10; and even \u201cno Milestones left\u201d strikes me as a needlessly harsh restriction. </div> </div> </div>Ah, I think I see. I'm picturing the player going &quot;OK, I'm about ready for the New Dawn&quot;; whereas you're imagining it as the ST deciding when a character is &quot;ready&quot;.<br /> <br /> Does that seem accurate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T19:27:09-07:00","id":247333,"title":"","content":"Not really. Sure, the nature of Milestones as written pretty much requires the Storyteller to have a hand in deciding whether or not the Promethean is ready to Redeem; but the core issue is that Milestones are far more important for judging progress of the Pilgrimage (and thus readiness for the Crucible) than Azoth or Humanity are. It is, after all, why they\u2019re called <i>Milestones</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T20:05:08-07:00","id":247389,"title":"","content":"This in turn reminds me: given that Argentum seems to be planned for inclusion in the 2e corebook, it would be nice to see the various non-milestone supernatural-exploration Vitriol-generation methods get a little more play than barely-any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T20:29:17-07:00","id":247402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=246766#post246766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go back to the definitions of Virtue and Vice as given in GMC:<br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">\u2022 A character's Virtue should be something that gives her a great sense of self-actualization, but which she is often tempted to ignore. It's her higher calling, the personality trait that would be at the fore all the time if she didn't live in the World of Darkness. It should be both difficult to act upon and make her feel good when she does make the effort.<br /> \u2022 A character's Vice, on the other hand, is a source of short-term comfort and a distraction from the world. Vice should be the easy way out, the sand he buries his head in, like a bully lashing out to avoid his own fear or an alcoholic drinking to forget.</span></div>Now let\u2019s take that \u201cOrigin\u201d idea and apply it to both, thinking of a newly-created Promethean as an organic machine that has yet to achieve any agency. The equivalent of \u201cVirtue\u201d for such a creation would be its <i>Purpose</i>: the role that its creator made it to fill. Filling that role is a higher calling, a means of self-actualization; and fulfilling one\u2019s Purpose serves as a powerful source of positive reinforcement.<br /> <br /> Conversely, the equivalent of \u201cVice\u201d is a reflection of the fact that any time you create something as elaborate and complex as a Promethean, it\u2019s bound to develop unanticipated behaviors: the <i>Quirk</i> represents some aspect of the Promethean\u2019s personality which was <i>not</i> chosen for it by its creator: if this Quirk interferes with the Promethean\u2019s Purpose, it\u2019s typically viewed as a bug or a glitch, and is the sort of thing the creator might spend time and effort trying to purge from his creation. (\u201cQuirk\u201d may not be the best name for it; but hopefully I\u2019ve successfully communicated the idea I\u2019m thinking of.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the concept, but I would argue that the two elements should be flipped: it is the original purpose that the Promethean comforts himself with, while the 'fault' of self-determination, the growing beyond original intentions, is the difficult path the Promethean must follow to achieve her New Dawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T04:10:57-07:00","id":247724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>StSword:</b> Another thing I'd like them to include is higher technology, they have transgenic clones and three law compliant robots already, they ought to go ahead and open that pandora's box and show what kind of high tech secrets are hiding in the world of darkness. </div> </div> </div>It shouldn't go the route of all mad science all the time, though. Mysticism and initiation, strange rituals, and uncanny artworks are all equally mad transgressions (eg, I'd class the original Picture of Dorian Grey as more of a Promethean event than a Mage or changeling one, despite Dorian benefiting from something like an anti-Disquiet). <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>atamajakki:</b> How mad would folks be about an Orphean lineage replacing the Ulgan? The whole spirits thing has never fit well to me. </div> </div> </div>I used to favour a ghostly lineage, but these days, I'd rather adjust the Orisians to cover that more fully. If it was up to me, I <i>would</i> like to see the Ulgan replaced, but with something rooted in the Delphic and similar Oracles: retaining the theme of twisted initiation making you a literal new being, and the mood of seeing things others don't; but eshewing spirit worlds in favour of visions and dreams (yes, the Greeks did connect oracles with the Underworld sometimes, but not in an especially &quot;ghostly&quot; way). But nothing that drastic is going to happen. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dataweaver:</b> They\u2019re cyborgs if the parts they graft on come from the Unfleshed or an equivalent; they\u2019re \u201cflesh-borgs\u201d if the parts come from a Promethean. </div> </div> </div>At least one of the thaumotech grafts clearly comes from a <i>Pandoran</i>. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Eremite:</b> Supternatural Tolerance penalises nearly every mind-controlling power across the gamelines, as well as a few other ones. I don't like the idea of the powerful low Humanity Promethean being easily puppeteered (though one can make interesting arguments re: their lacking soul) since a player with access to the right power can make them sit up and beg. </div> </div> </div>Rather than lack of a soul, consider lack of identity. High Humanity protects from mind control because by that point, the Promethean knows herself more completely than almost any other creature; and she doesn't <i>just</i> know who she is, she's also <i>won</i> who she is to a level that few non-Prometheans will ever comprehend. And so, no one can take that identity from her. I don't favour Humanity as a power stat, but I might have talked myself into favouring it taking over from the actual power stat when it comes to mind control. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>blackhatmatt</b> The biggest changes you'll see, so far (apart from that whole &quot;we added a new Refinement&quot; thing), is that the Tammuz focus more on language and being word-bound, because the whole &quot;artificial person&quot; thing that resonates with golems is really bound up with the Unfleshed. </div> </div> </div>Cool. Can I ask - what I mentioned earlier about having two Lineages with an origin story about the attempt to resurrect a loved one, but neither of them going on to particularly figure grief or loss into how they work - is grief or loss getting incorporated in any way, be it to the Tammuz or Osirians or one of the new ones? Because I do think it's a powerful vehicle for Disquiet and Torment. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alchemists are actually included...as antagonists. We very deliberately decided against a minor template for Prometheans, because I wanted to emphasize how alone they are. </div> </div> </div>Makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T14:12:01-07:00","id":248136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=247724#post247724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Rather than lack of a soul, consider lack of identity. High Humanity protects from mind control because by that point, the Promethean knows herself more completely than almost any other creature; and she doesn't <i>just</i> know who she is, she's also <i>won</i> who she is to a level that few non-Prometheans will ever comprehend. And so, no one can take that identity from her. I don't favour Humanity as a power stat, but I might have talked myself into favouring it taking over from the actual power stat when it comes to mind control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing - I like this, it's really cool, and for your Golems, Galateids and Unfleshed especially it's an excellent system where high Humanity ones who overcome their innate need to serve and be a tool, not a person, can resist supernatural powers that control and compel...<br /> <br /> ...But from a game balance perspective, it makes every Promethean who is failing to become human - or walking the Hundred-Handed Path towards inhumanity - less mechanically threatening, especially if Prometheans get any mind-controlling powers in the new build. I really do hate to choose mechanics and balance over theme, for Promethean especially, but if you've ever seen a game of vampire struggle under the pressure of Dominate and Majesty (the struggle is stopping the power trumping everything but not making everything so resistant/immune that the power becomes useless) then you'll hopefully see where I'm trying to come from.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T15:45:05-07:00","id":248175,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s not even a \u201cbalance over theme\u201d thing, as the current setup of Azoth-and-Pyros + Humanity-as-Integrity-substitute is thematically very solid as is. Changing it around has the potential to introduce a whole host of unintended consequences, only a few of which have been outlined. And the main motive for proposing the switch-up in the first place (i.e., having a trait that measures the progress of the Pilgrimage) is largely a non-issue, as the game already has a means of tracking such progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T07:25:33-07:00","id":248822,"title":"","content":"Humanity isn't the Integrity analog anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T07:33:17-07:00","id":248829,"title":"","content":"That was unexpected. So what <i>is</i> the Integrity analog?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T09:49:58-07:00","id":248922,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the requests for Simalcrum were heard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T17:03:50-07:00","id":249293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=248822#post248822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity isn't the Integrity analog anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glee! Will it, or another stat, still be used as a sort of Pilgrimage-gauge then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T19:33:31-07:00","id":249393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=249293#post249293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glee! Will it, or another stat, still be used as a sort of Pilgrimage-gauge then?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep. <br /> <br /> Lest you all think I'm being uncharacteristically coy about this, you're right. I am planning on doing some open dev stuff, I'm just waiting on a couple of first drafts to roll in (and wrapping up some other writing I need to get done, like, this week), and then I'll tell you all about some of the fun changes we're making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T19:43:19-07:00","id":249397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=249393#post249393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yep. <br /> <br /> Lest you all think I'm being uncharacteristically coy about this, you're right. I am planning on doing some open dev stuff, I'm just waiting on a couple of first drafts to roll in (and wrapping up some other writing I need to get done, like, this week), and then I'll tell you all about some of the fun changes we're making.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fantastic .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T22:56:54-07:00","id":249574,"title":"","content":"We definitely seem to be looking at some radical changes than we've seen in Blood &amp; Smoke.<br /> <br /> I'm skeered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T12:45:42-07:00","id":251660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=249393#post249393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lest you all think I'm being uncharacteristically coy about this, you're right. I am planning on doing some open dev stuff, I'm just waiting on a couple of first drafts to roll in (and wrapping up some other writing I need to get done, like, this week), and then I'll tell you all about some of the fun changes we're making.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems wise to me! Very much looking forward to more spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T01:48:30-07:00","id":252117,"title":"","content":"<i>Notice:</i> <i>I\u2019m mostly <b>Mage</b> ST and have read corebook only, so if make silly assumptions on gameline, just tell me.</i><br /> <br /> We see that <b>Promethean</b> 1e is not fun enough for most possible players to like it. Let\u2019s look then on it\u2019s base premise and see what can be done with that, just like it was shown in <b>Mage Chronicle Guide</b>.<br /> <br /> <i>Prometheans are lonely creatures, because they are few in the world and they own existence make Disquiet in people and Wasteland in whole nature. Almost all of them seek to become humans after alchemical processes inside their once mortal body. But they don\u2019t have recollection to life of previous host that gave them their body. They make great journeys, because they are hunted by humans driven by Disquiet and they own, mocked creations \u2013 Pandorans.</i><br /> <br /> So here are my proposition to make game more fun to play by changing those things a bit.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><i>Prometheans are lonely creatures, because they are few in the world</i></li> </ol><b>Parliament of Created:</b> One of major problems from RPG game design with <b>PtC</b> 1e is that there are only very small population of Prometheans in the world. You just can\u2019t make local political, world political or comic scale games. I would propose to make in <b>PtC</b> 2e corebook Tiers of Play guidelines, with at least small support for Tiers 2 ( local ) and Tiers 3 ( global games ). Those \u201cmodes\u201d of play should be as much visable, as typical Pligrimage mode of 1e.<br /> <br /> <b>Throng is good for you:</b> There should be some mechanics and fluff hints that by working in throngs, Created are more human like, beside Generative Acts \u2013 maybe some Pyros discount on Transmutations? Something to be felt on each game session. Idea is that other player characters are \u2013 maybe not needed \u2013 but very good for your own.<br /> <br /> <b>More of us, more the fun: </b>Refinements maybe are personal take on Pilgrimage of Created, but there should be obvious mechanics that working in tandem with other practitioners you can achieve your goals quicker. Basically, it should be rather easily to make \u201calchemical guild\u201d of your Refinement in the city if there are enough practitioners of it \u2013 this way we cold get quasi-Order or Covenant local structure for more political oriented games.<br /> <br /> <b>Titles, titles and titles:</b> To make possible political games, there need to be positions to strive to, plot for or even kill for inside they community. I\u2019m not saying game need title level of<b> Changling</b>, or even <b>Mage</b>, but one position per Refinement for big \u201cguilds\u201d should make at least in-setting possible for more intrigue advanced game.<br /> <br /> <i>2. (\u2026)they own existence make Disquiet in people and Wasteland in whole nature.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Weakening Disquiet and Wasteland</b>: Those mechanics are very interesting and fitting for Created, but are large turn off from players. \u201cWhat, I can\u2019t have any real relationship with people on around me, and I will make my local in to living hell in time of weeks? Bye bye, local game.\u201d Some middle ground for those harsh mechanics should be found for 2e.<br /> <br /> <i>3. Almost all of them seek to become humans</i><br /> <br /> <b>Many end goals: </b>This is my second biggest issue with 1e and I think it\u2019s one of many possible players. Quest to become human is very noble, but many people thinking \u201cI\u2019am artificial man\u201d think \u201cwow, it can be awesome to become MORE than human\u201d. And contrary to developers main line, I think that idea of some Created not wanting to become mortals in the end is <b>much strongly</b> highlighting the Humanity of those that end mortal, than when almost all of them want to become one. It\u2019s like in <b>Mage</b> \u2013 Hubris is best shown when you confront characters that fall for it, with those that become Wise.<br /> <br /> So idea is basically this \u2013 there are many New Dawns. One of them is to become human. Other is to become in reality uberPandoran ( it\u2019s mine Centimanii character idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). And there is rest, like Created that want to become RoboCop-like entity ( Ferrum guys, mostly ). And many, many others take on Final Goal. Yeah, most of players will probably will lean to proper Humanity. But cool NPCs and players character are made with diversion from norm. And New Dawn is exactly what is heart of Promethean character.<br /> <br /> As to mechanics, I think that something like connection of your Refinement and Athanor should point to this. Even more second than the first. If Refinement point you HOW you want to make to end of journey, your Athanor should point to WHAT you strive.<br /> <br /> For our RoboCop guy it would be Refinement of Steel ( be honing his physical and warrior code ) and Athanor of Perfection ( for ending as inhuman perfect being ). This model would open game for much, much, much more possible gameplay concepts.<br /> <br /> <i>4. (\u2026)alchemical processes inside their once mortal body.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Flesh and Unflesh equal: </b>I very like idea in 1e that Unfleshed were members of normal Linages, only made from \u201csacred materials\u201d than human bodies. It lead to very interesting characters, like the Pygmalion Acanthus mage in mine LARP that made Galateid being from perfect statue he was obsessed with ( mage player is also great fan of Promethean ). Once more \u2013 opening game for more basic options will only serve it good. And contrasting Unfleshed Galateid that so much want to become mortal with Fleshed one that want to forsake it in road to become inhuman being would nicely support themes of game, don\u2019t you think? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>5. But they don\u2019t have recollection to life of previous host that gave them their body.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sometimes they remember:</b> I know Created are new beings based on bodies of previous lives, and generally shouldn\u2019t have memoires of body they inhabit. But nice would be diversion from norm on this from time to time, maybe with Merit, but something more than your muscle memory. What would do character that is practicing Aurum if she will get flashbacks that her body was serial killer? Will it take as proper road for New Dawn? Or Ulgan, that is now inhuman being made from spirits get\u2019s vision of his previous life as happy husband with wife and two children \u2013 would he envious them?<br /> <br /> <i>6. They make great journeys</i><br /> <br /> <b>Settle for once: </b>Creating WoD chronicle minisetting \u2013 with proper locations, bunch of NPCs and subplots \u2013 it\u2019s tedious job, that repay in long term, when after couple of session game flows on it\u2019s own. But running Pilgrimage chronicle, with new, little settings every few session when Created are shunted from they locations \u2013 it\u2019s tedious to extreme, and only most dedicated Storytellers will go with them. ( This is one of reasons why I\u2019m not running the game, right now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> It is needed that short chronicle ( up to 20 game session ) should be possible to be run in one location. Yes, Prometheans will have reasons to travel often, and many games will still be Pilgrimages. But there need to be more settled style possible to play, especially for political games.<br /> <br /> <i>7. (...) hunted by humans driven by Disquiet and they own, mocked creations \u2013 Pandorans</i><br /> <br /> <b>More human antagonists: </b>Inhuman enemies of Created are fine and good. But mortal antagonists should not only by raging mob from Disquiet. Alchemists and Hunters are especially groups that should be putted in this light. They are mortals that \u201cknows\u201d what Prometheans really are and they fight with them not only because they ha Disfigurements.<br /> <br /> It's just my ideas, but I think this would open game for many, many, many new players. What do you think - especially developers - on those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-08-2014, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T05:46:18-07:00","id":252203,"title":"","content":"<b>@wyrdhamster: </b>I almost exclusively agree with your point about having different end-goals. To open the game up for political plays, means making it so that there are more of The Created. Making it so that there are more of The Created, means that you take away the aspect of lonelyness. Thats one of the major cornerstones of Promethean being taken away right there. It would be the equivalent to taking the mages need for secrecy and shadow-play or the vampires political intrigue.<br /> Promethean dont need the political play. Most other game lines has that in one fashion or another. There is no need to shoe-horn something into Promethean that wont add anything to the core thematic.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't characterize Promethean as a &quot;fun&quot; system. But thats fine. Not everything needs to be &quot;fun&quot;. As long as it is interesting and provides an enjoyable experience for the people involved, thats enough for me and I feel that Promethean delivers in spades on the &quot;interesting and enjoyable&quot; part.<br /> <br /> But yes, a few suggestions for different end-goals seems like something that would add to the system. Especially because some Prometheans dont know their creator, and then who is to tell them of the possibillity of The New Dawn? Other Prometheans? What if they never encounter any? Or the ones they encounter never got told of The New Dawn either?<br /> I also rather liked your idea of &quot;Sometimes they remember&quot;. I think that would open up for some decent gameplay with the previous relatives and aquintances of the body. Even though this was mentioned throughout Promethean 1E throughout the books, the storyhooks were shatter-shot and dropped into the books with inconsistency, so it was hard to look at it and really answer to the question &quot;How often is this?&quot;. WIthout a merit or flaw to repressent it, it made it slide into a nebulous space even more so.<br /> Personally, I flavored Residual Memory - if applied to mental or social skills - in this fashion, but that more of a houserule than anything else, I think.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T06:15:54-07:00","id":252236,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>Krobeles</b>, the nWoD games are toolboxes, they don't need to be &quot;one way or another&quot;. Tiers is old guidelines made in part of most games 1e by later half of they lifespan. I totally don't say there shouldn't be Pilgrimage chronicle &quot;mode&quot; for <b>PtC</b>. Or even it should't be default. Rather, let there be more open to other possibilities. Tiers could easily show up only in Storyteller sections and maybe showing possibility of &quot;Guilds&quot; in Refinement section. That would be enough to let more &quot;ambitious&quot; Storyteller to run with the game.<br /> <br /> Alternative is to stick with all 3 players of Promethean you have in Europe... ( Yes, it is sarcasm. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T06:56:00-07:00","id":252260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252236#post252236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Krobeles</b>, the nWoD games are toolboxes, they don't need to be &quot;one way or another&quot;. Tiers is old guidelines made in part of most games 1e by later half of they lifespan. I totally don't say there shouldn't be Pilgrimage chronicle &quot;mode&quot; for <b>PtC</b>. Or even it should't be default. Rather, let there be more open to other possibilities. Tiers could easily show up only in Storyteller sections and maybe showing possibility of &quot;Guilds&quot; in Refinement section. That would be enough to let more &quot;ambitious&quot; Storyteller to run with the game.<br /> <br /> Alternative is to stick with all 3 players of Promethean you have in Europe... ( Yes, it is sarcasm. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>True. They are toolboxes, but in order to be able to work with this toolbox, you need to bring the right tools and know what job you want to accomplish. You cant bring a chainsaw if you want to build a shed, and you wanna fill your box with Iphones filled with social media apps if you intend setting up a new shelve in your kitchen. Some things also exclude each other. If you bring the saw for the brances, you wont have enough space for hammer to beat in the nails.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is; that yes. Its a toolbox. But if you include the tool for political games, you hamstring the tools for lonely Pilgrimage play, because one is relying on a weak Disquiet and Wasteland, while the other is relying on a strong one. They are in direct conflict with each other, and you cant have both. Unless you include something that basically says; &quot;Alright, look. Here some rules if you want A and heres another set of mostly unrelated rules, for if you want B&quot;, I dont think you meaningfully have both. And doing that dimminishes both, I find.<br /> Its like hosting a party. Ideally, you'd want to include everyone and everything, but you dont wanna hang the band-banner from the last Diecide concert if you're gonna invite your Christian friend, and you dont wanna invite your buddy from the KKK if you intend to bring your black friend. Some things are just in too large contrast to each other, for them to mesh well, and outside of segregating the rules in the manner I mentioned before, I cant see it working out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T08:13:55-07:00","id":252330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252117#post252117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Notice:</i> <i>I\u2019m mostly <b>Mage</b> ST and have read corebook only, so if make silly assumptions on gameline, just tell me.</i><br /> <br /> We see that <b>Promethean</b> 1e is not fun enough for most possible players to like it. Let\u2019s look then on it\u2019s base premise and see what can be done with that, just like it was shown in <b>Mage Chronicle Guide</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things before we begin: first, <b>Mage Chronicler\u2019s Guide</b> is a book of options for a Storyteller who wishes to divert from the baseline setting; you\u2019ll note that very little of its contents are making it into FWC. And what <i>is</i> making it in isn\u2019t radically changing the core premises of the setting; at most, it\u2019s providing a different spin on what was already there. FWC is working with what\u2019s already there, emphasizing some elements more than they used to be emphasized and downplaying others, but not introducing wholly new elements or excising anything from the game: refine and elaborate, not wholesale alteration. <br /> <br /> Second, I don\u2019t agree with your implication that <b>Promethean</b> needs a complete overhaul to be a successful game. Sure, it could use some tweaking here and there; but there\u2019s no reason to completely rebuild it from scratch. <br /> <br /> With that in mind, I\u2019m going to be approaching your post from two perspectives: a hypothetical <b>Promethean Chronicler\u2019s Guide</b> that takes its cues from the <b>Mage Chronicler\u2019s Guide</b>, and the upcoming <b>Promethean 2e</b>, which I expect will be more akin to <b>Mage 2e</b>: a refinement of 1e, aimed at bringing forth its core themes more effectively. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252117#post252117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here are my proposition to make game more fun to play by changing those things a bit.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><i>Prometheans are lonely creatures, because they are few in the world</i></li> </ol><b>Parliament of Created:</b> One of major problems from RPG game design with <b>PtC</b> 1e is that there are only very small population of Prometheans in the world. You just can\u2019t make local political, world political or comic scale games. I would propose to make in <b>PtC</b> 2e corebook Tiers of Play guidelines, with at least small support for Tiers 2 ( local ) and Tiers 3 ( global games ). Those \u201cmodes\u201d of play should be as much visable, as typical Pligrimage mode of 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>A grand idea for a PCG; but <i>not</i> for 2e core. Mind you, I don\u2019t object to Prometheans being a bit more common that 1e portrayed them; but the notion of a Promethean equivalent of a \u201cPrince of the City\u201d just doesn\u2019t feel like <b>Promethean</b> to me. In this regard, <b>Promethean</b> is more akin to <b>Werewolf</b> than to <b>Vampire</b> or <b>Mage</b>: the Throng or Pack is about as organized as they get. <br /> <br /> With that in mind, I\u2019m skipping over further suggestions related to the notion of \u201cPromethean politics\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252117#post252117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Throng is good for you:</b> There should be some mechanics and fluff hints that by working in throngs, Created are more human like, beside Generative Acts \u2013 maybe some Pyros discount on Transmutations? Something to be felt on each game session. Idea is that other player characters are \u2013 maybe not needed \u2013 but very good for your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e includes something in it called an Alchemical Pact a.k.a. a Branded Throng, which adds supernatural properties to a Throng of Prometheans. I can see 2e revising said benefits; but the core idea is that establishing an Alchemical Pact and conducting your Pilgrimage in tandem with other Prometheans <i>is</i> good for you. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252117#post252117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>2. (\u2026)they own existence make Disquiet in people and Wasteland in whole nature.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Weakening Disquiet and Wasteland</b>: Those mechanics are very interesting and fitting for Created, but are large turn off from players. \u201cWhat, I can\u2019t have any real relationship with people on around me, and I will make my local in to living hell in time of weeks? Bye bye, local game.\u201d Some middle ground for those harsh mechanics should be found for 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bottom line: I hear that something along these lines is being considered for 2e: at the very least, Wasteland needs a more active trigger to kick into effect than the mere prolonged presence of a Promethean, and its more severe stages tend to recede on their own. OTOH, Disquiet looks like it\u2019s going to remain in full force. I wouldn\u2019t even be surprised if it intensifies, maybe getting tied into the Integrity mechanics the way <b>Mage 2e</b> is tying Quiescence into Integrity. Removing Disquiet from Prometheans is like removing the nocturnal nature of vampires. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252117#post252117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>3. Almost all of them seek to become humans</i><br /> <br /> <b>Many end goals: </b>This is my second biggest issue with 1e and I think it\u2019s one of many possible players. Quest to become human is very noble, but many people thinking \u201cI\u2019am artificial man\u201d think \u201cwow, it can be awesome to become MORE than human\u201d. And contrary to developers main line, I think that idea of some Created not wanting to become mortals in the end is <b>much strongly</b> highlighting the Humanity of those that end mortal, than when almost all of them want to become one. It\u2019s like in <b>Mage</b> \u2013 Hubris is best shown when you confront characters that fall for it, with those that become Wise.<br /> <br /> So idea is basically this \u2013 there are many New Dawns. One of them is to become human. Other is to become in reality uberPandoran ( it\u2019s mine Centimanii character idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). And there is rest, like Created that want to become RoboCop-like entity ( Ferrum guys, mostly ). And many, many others take on Final Goal. Yeah, most of players will probably will lean to proper Humanity. But cool NPCs and players character are made with diversion from norm. And New Dawn is exactly what is heart of Promethean character.<br /> <br /> As to mechanics, I think that something like connection of your Refinement and Athanor should point to this. Even more second than the first. If Refinement point you HOW you want to make to end of journey, your Athanor should point to WHAT you strive.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is based on a fundamental misunderstanding of what the New Dawn is. It\u2019s not the Promethean\u2019s goal; it\u2019s the [i]Principle\u2019s[/b] goal for the Promethean. And yes, there <i>are</i> Prometheans who don\u2019t seek to become human, just as there are vampires who choose not to feed on humans. In both cases, they\u2019re resisting the urgings that come with being what they are. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252117#post252117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For our RoboCop guy it would be Refinement of Steel ( be honing his physical and warrior code ) and Athanor of Perfection ( for ending as inhuman perfect being ). This model would open game for much, much, much more possible gameplay concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026and would completely undermine the game\u2019s themes. In the Robocop universe, there was no means for Robocop to literally become human again; but the impression that you get from watching his development is that if he <i>were</i> to be offered a way to become fully human again \u2014 say, by means of advanced biotech providing him with fully human replacement parts instead of the mechanical parts he got \u2014 he\u2019d leap at the chance. The \u201chappy ending\u201d that he ended up with was as close as the metaphysics of the setting would allow him to come to fully reclaiming his humanity. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252117#post252117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>4. (\u2026)alchemical processes inside their once mortal body.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Flesh and Unflesh equal: </b>I very like idea in 1e that Unfleshed were members of normal Linages, only made from \u201csacred materials\u201d than human bodies. It lead to very interesting characters, like the Pygmalion Acanthus mage in mine LARP that made Galateid being from perfect statue he was obsessed with ( mage player is also great fan of Promethean ). Once more \u2013 opening game for more basic options will only serve it good. And contrasting Unfleshed Galateid that so much want to become mortal with Fleshed one that want to forsake it in road to become inhuman being would nicely support themes of game, don\u2019t you think? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to agree with this; but it appears that the developers don\u2019t. That said, we <i>will</i> be getting Unfleshed in the core book. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252117#post252117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>5. But they don\u2019t have recollection to life of previous host that gave them their body.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sometimes they remember:</b> I know Created are new beings based on bodies of previous lives, and generally shouldn\u2019t have memoires of body they inhabit. But nice would be diversion from norm on this from time to time, maybe with Merit, but something more than your muscle memory. What would do character that is practicing Aurum if she will get flashbacks that her body was serial killer? Will it take as proper road for New Dawn? Or Ulgan, that is now inhuman being made from spirits get\u2019s vision of his previous life as happy husband with wife and two children \u2013 would he envious them?</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s a Merit for this in the core book. Note, though, that the former occupant of the body is <i>still</i> someone else: you may be able to tap into their memories from time to time; but they\u2019re <i>someone else\u2019s memories</i>, not your own: especially in a world that has ghosts in it, \u201cRobocop\u201d will never become Alex Murphy. OTOH, \u201cRobocop\u201d might easily find himself being haunted by the ghost of Alex Murphy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252117#post252117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>6. They make great journeys</i><br /> <br /> <b>Settle for once: </b>Creating WoD chronicle minisetting \u2013 with proper locations, bunch of NPCs and subplots \u2013 it\u2019s tedious job, that repay in long term, when after couple of session game flows on it\u2019s own. But running Pilgrimage chronicle, with new, little settings every few session when Created are shunted from they locations \u2013 it\u2019s tedious to extreme, and only most dedicated Storytellers will go with them. ( This is one of reasons why I\u2019m not running the game, right now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div> the changes to Wastelands are being made with making non-nomadic chronicles more feasible. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252117#post252117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>7. (...) hunted by humans driven by Disquiet and they own, mocked creations \u2013 Pandorans</i><br /> <br /> <b>More human antagonists: </b>Inhuman enemies of Created are fine and good. But mortal antagonists should not only by raging mob from Disquiet. Alchemists and Hunters are especially groups that should be putted in this light. They are mortals that \u201cknows\u201d what Prometheans really are and they fight with them not only because they have Disfigurements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemists will indeed exist as antagonists; and I won\u2019t be a bit surprised to see the occasional <b>Hunter</b> reference \u2014 though I hasten to add that Disquiet comes from understanding what a Promethean is at least as often as from <i>not</i> understanding what it is. That some need no prodding to hunt Prometheans doesn\u2019t mean that Disquiet won\u2019t come along and reinforce that tendency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T10:41:40-07:00","id":252474,"title":"","content":"With talk of the 2e 'Predatory Aura' mechanics for a variety of splats, I remember people talking about how Disquiet kind of fits that bill for Promethean. Reading through some of the core again, though (it's been a long, long time since I've run it - it was the first WoD game I ever ran!), there's something called the Measure.<br /> <br /> It's what the Created sense when they meet another of their kind. I think that might fit the bill better. It was always a vague kind of thing in 1e and I liked that, but maybe it could get more talk in 2e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T12:49:50-07:00","id":252589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252330#post252330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, I don\u2019t agree with your implication that <b>Promethean</b> needs a complete overhaul to be a successful game. Sure, it could use some tweaking here and there; but there\u2019s no reason to completely rebuild it from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't implaying this. Mostly, I made things to <b>build on what is now </b>in <b>PtC 1e</b>. There should be default Pilgrimage mode, but add some elements and you could also make a quasi-political game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252330#post252330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A grand idea for a PCG; but <i>not</i> for 2e core. Mind you, I don\u2019t object to Prometheans being a bit more common that 1e portrayed them; but the notion of a Promethean equivalent of a \u201cPrince of the City\u201d just doesn\u2019t feel like <b>Promethean</b> to me. In this regard, <b>Promethean</b> is more akin to <b>Werewolf</b> than to <b>Vampire</b> or <b>Mage</b>: the Throng or Pack is about as organized as they get.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't envison this &quot;more political&quot; as a &quot;Prince of the City&quot; - more, Created race on their Magnum Opus and stealing secrects of New Dawn. Like &quot;Ferrum Guild is very close to unlock secrets of Alchemicus, we can't let them achive this! Their alchemy will be ours!&quot; - something like this. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252330#post252330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Removing Disquiet from Prometheans is like removing the nocturnal nature of vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once more, I wasn't implying this. I was thinking more in terms that Disquiet should be more <br /> thing to tune in the game itself - some ST will make it harsh, others making it rather low.<br /> <br /> And just nitpick, but in <b>Blood &amp; Smoke</b> young vampires <b>can</b> be rather active by day. So we have somehow precedent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T14:47:04-07:00","id":252674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252589#post252589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't envison this &quot;more political&quot; as a &quot;Prince of the City&quot; - more, Created race on their Magnum Opus and stealing secrects of New Dawn. Like &quot;Ferrum Guild is very close to unlock secrets of Alchemicus, we can't let them achive this! Their alchemy will be ours!&quot; - something like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid you've entirely lost me here.<br /> Why? What more can one group of Prometheans possibly gain from stealing from another, that they couldn't gain from merely asking them kindly to share their secrets? Unless one group is Hundred Handed, there is literally no reason why they couldn't work together.<br /> Even if there were introduced more Magnum Opus options, I fail to see why The Created couldn't work together. On average, a Promethean simply isn't human enough to habor feelings of xenophobia and selfish greed that might compel a Mage to steal another Mages secrets for himself. A Promethean might steal from another in order to try and gain that level of human understanding (I need to be more selfish, because Humans are inherently selfish), but a group of Prometheans who genuinely feel on a gut deep level the selfish need to steal and exclude, are human enough that they will likely think of other things than stealing Alchemical secrets.<br /> <br /> What you're suggesting isn't an inherently boring, I think. However to implement it in a Promethean corebook of any kind, is in direct opposition to a big part of what even makes Promethean. I can totally see it in some alternate setting shard, but not as a core thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T18:30:09-07:00","id":252834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252474#post252474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With talk of the 2e 'Predatory Aura' mechanics for a variety of splats, I remember people talking about how Disquiet kind of fits that bill for Promethean. Reading through some of the core again, though (it's been a long, long time since I've run it - it was the first WoD game I ever ran!), there's something called the Measure.<br /> <br /> It's what the Created sense when they meet another of their kind. I think that might fit the bill better. It was always a vague kind of thing in 1e and I liked that, but maybe it could get more talk in 2e</div> </div> </div> </div>The trouble is that the Measure is essentially the Created reading each other's Azoth.<br /> <br /> The Predatory Aura and Nimbuses both work on beings other than their own owner's category, and the mortal response to Azoth is Disquiet, which is likewise responsible for the Wasteland effect.<br /> <br /> People talk about Disquiet as a candidate because it's a function of Azoth that affects more than just your first impressions with some of the rarest sapient monsters in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T22:38:39-07:00","id":253032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252674#post252674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid you've entirely lost me here.<br /> Why? What more can one group of Prometheans possibly gain from stealing from another, that they couldn't gain from merely asking them kindly to share their secrets? Unless one group is Hundred Handed, there is literally no reason why they couldn't work together.<br /> Even if there were introduced more Magnum Opus options, I fail to see why The Created couldn't work together. On average, a Promethean simply isn't human enough to habor feelings of xenophobia and selfish greed that might compel a Mage to steal another Mages secrets for himself. A Promethean might steal from another in order to try and gain that level of human understanding (I need to be more selfish, because Humans are inherently selfish), but a group of Prometheans who genuinely feel on a gut deep level the selfish need to steal and exclude, are human enough that they will likely think of other things than stealing Alchemical secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowledge, techniques, transmutations, safer generative acts, the identities of known Redeemed, the whereabouts of known alchemists and Pandoran lairs: it only takes one Promethean-Throng-Guild hiding something to make others want to chase it. Every Promethean's existence is a matter of assembling rare knowledge and &quot;magic&quot; in order to achieve a higher state, which makes them as prone to covetousness as any willworker. Ophidians can summon conflagrations from the Pyros, and even the craziest of them recognize that it's not a gift to be shared cavalierly, though a Fury might violently beg to differ. Prometheans are jealous, in their nature and in their inspirations, which makes them every bit as fractious as mortals. There's no virtue in the Promethean condition that makes them somehow better creatures then humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T23:20:41-07:00","id":253064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=253032#post253032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Knowledge, techniques, transmutations, safer generative acts, the identities of known Redeemed, the whereabouts of known alchemists and Pandoran lairs: it only takes one Promethean-Throng-Guild hiding something to make others want to chase it. Every Promethean's existence is a matter of assembling rare knowledge and &quot;magic&quot; in order to achieve a higher state, which makes them as prone to covetousness as any willworker. Ophidians can summon conflagrations from the Pyros, and even the craziest of them recognize that it's not a gift to be shared cavalierly, though a Fury might violently beg to differ. Prometheans are jealous, in their nature and in their inspirations, which makes them every bit as fractious as mortals. There's no virtue in the Promethean condition that makes them somehow better creatures then humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but why cant the Prometheans just ask the other throng kindly to tell them? Why would the throng hide the knowledge in the first place? Most of them leave Firebrand for the express purpose of freely sharing knowledge with as many Prometheans as they possibly can, so why hide it away? Prometheans aren't better in any fashion than humans, but thats precisely why they aren't prone (on average, anyway) to such selfish actions as this. They dont have genuine emotions or wants, they have false and simulated wants and emotions.<br /> To think &quot;I dont want this person to have this knowledge, because I dont like him!&quot; or &quot;I want to steal this knowledge because I want it, and that person is a cunt so I wont bother asking!&quot; is a very human way of thinking, one I dont think that Prometheans are really capable of, without having advanced far on their pilgrimage.<br /> I supose you could easily have a Promethean who found Stannum or Cobalus rather early in his pilgrimage, and therefor understood such emotions, but thats the exception rather than the norm.<br /> <br /> Most of the &quot;secrets&quot; that Prometheans have, are philosophical in nature anyway, and a philosophical understand can hardly be stolen. What does a Promethean hope to gain by hamstringing his fellow kin by holding back infomation about Pandoran locations, Alchemists, safer generative acts or Redeemed? It is possible for a single Promethean - or even a single throng - to have come to some conclusion that would justify this (Perhaps they wish to study how their malignant actions effects other people - for good and ill - and they feel that by being dicks to other Prometheans they are causing less karmic imbalance?) but again. Thats an isolated instance.<br /> I could understand if a Promethean had created some kind of philosophers stone or other simmilarily powerful alchemical relic, that a Promethean may want to steal it, in the hopes that it alone can transmute him into a real human, but again, thats the exception rather than the norm.<br /> <br /> I cant see this being a thing on any large scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T00:50:51-07:00","id":253143,"title":"","content":"I don't think hoarding of secrets is very big in Promethean. There's many concepts in it that oppose the idea: Pilgrim signs, Pilgrim locations, the Shepherd and Pilgrim merits, and the Scrutiny bestowment, and throng-branding as well - all of these are mechanics which foster communal generosity among the Created. They're really all trying to help each other out.<br /> <br /> I don't think clandestine societies of political backstabbing works either. Even if 2e does help Prometheans be a little less mobile from Wasteland there's still not going to be more than a dozen in a given city. I mean...their Y-splats aren't really even groups of societies so much as schools of philosophy. Like someone above said, it's the throng/pack that matters most (throng-branding), which again just means that they care about community more than other splats. It's just that their communities aren't very big.<br /> <br /> Like Matt said above, Prometheans are alone. They only have each other. That means they need to stick together. Vampires, Mages, Mummies, and Demons all have choices to screw each other over. Beasts might just love being around everybody. Prometheans, though? They're a big happy, insular family.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean conflict doesn't arise between them - of course! - but Kindred-style politics aren't the name of the game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T11:33:22-07:00","id":253501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252330#post252330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don\u2019t object to Prometheans being a bit more common that 1e portrayed them; but the notion of a Promethean equivalent of a \u201cPrince of the City\u201d just doesn\u2019t feel like <b>Promethean</b> to me. In this regard, <b>Promethean</b> is more akin to <b>Werewolf</b> than to <b>Vampire</b> or <b>Mage</b>: the Throng or Pack is about as organized as they get.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I\u2019m skipping over further suggestions related to the notion of \u201cPromethean politics\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can actually see a Promethean &quot;Prince of the City&quot;. They just, y'know, wouldn't be ruling over a court of Prometheans (unless they built them as minions! That could work.)<br /> <br /> More like the local VIP than the top of an elaborate pyramid; because the pyramid is so small it only has maybe two or three levels.<br /> <br /> But then, Wasteland. Hmm.<br /> <br /> There really needs to be a way to stay in one place long-term without removing the encouragement for most characters to keep moving. Maybe a Refinement to &quot;concentrate&quot; your Wasteland into a small area (like a garbage dump?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=248822#post248822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity isn't the Integrity analog anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>please be artifice please be artifice please be artifice<br /> <br /> (The anti-Humanity stat proposed over on RPG.net, for the curious. It started at 7 and went <i>down</i> as you shed your limitations.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=252674#post252674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if there were introduced more Magnum Opus options, I fail to see why The Created couldn't work together. On average, a Promethean simply isn't human enough to habor feelings of xenophobia and selfish greed ...</div> </div> </div> </div>... what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-09-2014, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T16:53:16-07:00","id":253672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=253501#post253501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">please be artifice please be artifice please be artifice<br /> <br /> (The anti-Humanity stat proposed over on RPG.net, for the curious. It started at 7 and went <i>down</i> as you shed your limitations.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I had heard of Simulcrae proposed on these forums, but I really like the sound of Artifice. It's especially awesome because OP is trying to put interesting spins for all the splats on Integrity stats. Mummy starts very low, Demon has multiple ratings, Werewolf is about balance in the middle, Beast is about hanging out at either extreme; it would be very fitting if Promethean started high (7 is good, as it's totally possible to become even more Artific-ial) and got more human the lower they became.<br /> <br /> I really, really like it. I know OP won't rip something right out of a fan-creation but...maybe this one time? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T18:08:36-07:00","id":253729,"title":"","content":"did everybody just forget about A Sheltering Storm<br /> <br /> is that what happened here","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T18:15:44-07:00","id":253736,"title":"","content":"I don't think I read that. o.o","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T19:24:45-07:00","id":253764,"title":"","content":"Second part of the line's ongoing chronicle, found in Pandora's Book. About half-again-ten resident Prometheans and a load more visiting Created all in the same place. There's at least three factions represented in the camp (the Bother\u00fad get their proper introduction here) and the largest one of them has an interest in the original printing plates of a book that tells you how to synthesize the <i>aqua vitae</i> from The Water of Life (the corebook's story in the set) and gives you a free Alchemy Specialty.<br /> <br /> The driving event of the story is that the concentration of Azoth is drawing a massive Firestorm is going to strike the camp and the PCs get sent back to the scene of a murder under false pretenses while the rest of the camp packs up and runs like hell; the introductory crawl likewise highlights truly unprecedented Wasteland density/severity, outpourings of Pandorans, regular Firestorms and qashmallim activity as direct consequences of Papillon's little project.<br /> <br /> Large physical congregations of Created have been covered by the line, as has using the Internet and other long-distance communication technology as a workaround that nevertheless produces a different feel to having a local court of flesh-golems in every thirteenth city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T23:45:33-07:00","id":253869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=253764#post253764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Large physical congregations of Created have been covered by the line, as has using the Internet and other long-distance communication technology as a workaround that nevertheless produces a different feel to having a local court of flesh-golems in every thirteenth city.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost exactly what I was thinking. Even if I didn't read any official adventures. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Only Firestorm is a bit in the way here if any large congregation of Created is generating here.<br /> <br /> Myself, I envisioned survaiors camp for Cuprum in the woods ( very like proposed on forums <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/141424-sanctuary-a-community-of-prometheans\">Sanctuary</a> ), or typical &quot;alchemical guild&quot; for Mercurius practicioners.<br /> <br /> As to end goals, Stannum have almost in they main motives idea of destroying or killing they Creator - is he Promethean or Demiurge. It is weird they all want to become humans in the end.<br /> <br /> As we are with Demiurges - I would want them to be more accesible in general. Not &quot;True&quot; Demuirges that makes Progenitors. But that mortals, based on writings of original Demiurge ( like Victor Frankenstein ), could remake a Generative Act.<br /> <br /> Maybe new Linages can come up once in a century, but mortals dabbling in making of artifical life should be real alternative to Promethean creating Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-10-2014, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T03:46:00-07:00","id":253949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=253869#post253869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As we are with Demiurges - I would want them to be more accesible in general. Not &quot;True&quot; Demuirges that makes Progenitors. But that mortals, based on writings of original Demiurge ( like Victor Frankenstein ), could remake a Generative Act.<br /> <br /> Maybe new Linages can come up once in a century, but mortals dabbling in making of artifical life should be real alternative to Promethean creating Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>... you know, these &quot;Alchemists&quot; we've heard talk about. I wonder if their &quot;thing&quot; is that they learned to artificially reproduce <i>Transmutations</i>?<br /> <br /> Because if so, there's already a Zombie Transmutation and a Homunculus Transmutation. I can really see more expansion along these lines. (Golems? Clones? Robots? Heck, the Generative Act itself is a lot like a Transmutation.)<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=253672#post253672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had heard of Simulcrae proposed on these forums, but I really like the sound of Artifice. It's especially awesome because OP is trying to put interesting spins for all the splats on Integrity stats. Mummy starts very low, Demon has multiple ratings, Werewolf is about balance in the middle, Beast is about hanging out at either extreme; it would be very fitting if Promethean started high (7 is good, as it's totally possible to become even more Artific-ial) and got more human the lower they became.<br /> <br /> I really, really like it. I know OP won't rip something right out of a fan-creation but...maybe this one time? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it wasn't a fan creation. Just a suggestion a few people made in the defunct Firestorm Chronicle thread there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=253729#post253729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">did everybody just forget about A Sheltering Storm<br /> <br /> is that what happened here</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-10-2014, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T05:26:25-07:00","id":254020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=253729#post253729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">did everybody just forget about A Sheltering Storm<br /> <br /> is that what happened here</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We, all of us (myself included), have a real issue with remembering the line. Like the constant 'why does the rulebook state so few Demiurges' thing, which is debunked continually, with a new Lineage and thus Demiurge in one of the sample adventures, a whole chapter on them in Saturnine Night, the crossover Prometheans made by vampires, mages and werewolves in another book, the fact that the Zeka have five (IIRC) seperate Demiurges. The books just ever officially retconned the fact.<br /> <br /> Not to mention those messing around with clones. Actually, if there are any devs watching, are we going to see any clones in 2e? I always thought they had a lot of story potential, even used them in a mini-campaign,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 09-10-2014, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T10:49:38-07:00","id":254190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=254020#post254020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We, all of us (myself included), have a real issue with remembering the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why I feel it necessary to stress <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=242611#post242611\">my earlier exhortation.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like the constant 'why does the rulebook state so few Demiurges' thing, which is debunked continually, </div> </div> </div>\u2026*cough*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Promethean Core, &quot;Making Monsters,&quot; p34</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Occasional rumors tell of new demiurges and their Lineages, but <b>no evidence has yet proven their existence. For now,</b> Prometheans make their way through the world as one of five known Lineages, propagating their lines as needed or desired.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Promethean Core, &quot;The Wasteland,&quot; p174</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the oldest Promethean scholars <b>and most studious demiurge researchers</b> have no clear idea of why this effect occurs.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Promethean Core, &quot;Torment,&quot; p180</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans might not <i>literally</i> radiate heat, but their condition does lend itself to a certain suffering nonetheless. No Promethean can escape it, and all Prometheans recognize it, which has led various Promethean <b>and demiurge scholars</b> to apply to this aspect of existence the poetic appellation \u201cthe Endless Torment of Prometheus.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Promethean Core, &quot;The Suffocating Rise of Torment,&quot; p181</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That resentment isn\u2019t enough on its own to cause Torment, but should that creator in any way keep the Promethean from achieving the aims of his Great Work, the Torment builds. It doesn\u2019t matter if the creator is another Promethean <b>or a human demiurge (even one who has somehow miraculously resisted Disquiet).</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> with a new Lineage and thus Demiurge in one of the sample adventures, </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strange Alchemies, &quot;The Question of Origin,&quot; p14-15</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>But what if a player wants to play a character created by a human demiurge?</b> What does that do to the character\u2019s Lineage, if anything? <b>Is such a thing feasible in the game as designed? The answer: Certainly.</b> It just means the Storyteller and the player have a few extra considerations.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Prometheans have very little sense of their kind\u2019s history, and what they do know (or believe) isn\u2019t verifiable. So <b>adding modern demiurges to the mix isn\u2019t going to damage the game\u2019s continuity on that front.</b><br /> [\u2026]<br /> The Divine Fire is the result of human obsession. [\u2026] <b>As such, if demiurges are possible in the modern World of Darkness, they should be even rarer than Prometheans.</b><br /> [\u2026]<br /> If the player comes up with a good character concept and is excited about taking this character through the Pilgrimage, that\u2019s much more important than any quibbles about how a demiurge learned to manipulate the Divine Fire. Odds are, the demiurge doesn\u2019t have it in him to try it again (and historically, bad things tend to happen to demiurges anyway), so the major in-game concern \u2014 what happens if these things are mass produced? \u2014 isn\u2019t going to become a real worry.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strange Alchemies, &quot;Supernatural Beings as Demiurges,&quot; p117</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans are created when someone steals (or passes on) the Divine Fire. It\u2019s usually another Promethean who does this, but <b>humans can do it, too, ordinary mortals whose obsessions, curiosity, loneliness or simple need to create gives them the psychic push necessary to break into the fabric of everything and bring real life to dead meat.</b> (The topic of human demiurges is discussed in the Introduction to this book.) Can a supernatural being create a Promethean? No. <b>Or, at least, no supernatural being has to date created a Promethean.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strange Alchemies, &quot;The Real Truth?&quot; sidebar, &quot;Strangers on a Hill,&quot; p142</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The decision that you, as the Storyteller, have to make is whether Lighthouse is what he claims he is. If Moses Moon, a mortal alchemist, really did create Lighthouse, then he isn\u2019t just some gifted Promethean, he\u2019s a Progenitor. He\u2019s the first in a new Lineage, perhaps the only new Lineage in 200 years (unless you count the nuclear Prometheans). That\u2019s not an insignificant thing, and it stands to throw many of the assumptions that the characters probably have \u2014 indeed, many of the assumptions that Promethean makes \u2014 out the window. That, however, is no reason for it not to be true. You just need to decide if this momentous occurrence works for your chronicle or not.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a whole chapter on them in Saturnine Night, </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saturnine Night, p14</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The methods through which the five <b>best-known</b> demiurges created Prometheans apparently varied as time went on.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saturnine Night, &quot;Modern Demiurges,&quot; p24</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>According to common thought,</b> the last of the five Lineages was created well over 100 years ago. When Victor Frankenstein brought his \u201cmonster\u201d into being, he sparked the Wretched line, and became the fifth and final demiurge. <b>This, however, is not <u>necessarily</u> the whole of the truth.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the crossover Prometheans made by vampires, mages and werewolves in another book, </div> </div> </div>The crossover Prometheans are in the Demiurges chapter of Saturnine Night.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saturnine Night, &quot;Impossibilities,&quot; p32</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>It is commonly held that</b> no supernatural creature, save for one of the Created, can wield the Divine Fire necessary to create a Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saturnine Night, &quot;Doing the Impossible,&quot; p33</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A Storyteller may, however, need for the impossible to happen, and might wish to create circumstances where a vampire, mage or werewolf might be able to create a Promethean. Certainly, motivations to attempt such efforts are easily understandable for most supernatural creatures. It only relies to the Storyteller to implement the \u201chow.\u201d<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Any of these situations should be handled with great care. <b>The introduction of any new Lineage is a serious and phenomenally rare happening. Only <u>five Lineages have, historically, prospered,</u> and while <u>it is certainly possible that other Lineages have either died out or remained obscure enough to stay below the radar,</u> they would still be an extreme rarity.</b> Introducing the idea of supernatural demiurges also has other ramifications, not just on the Promethean paradigm, but on that of the demiurge as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the fact that the Zeka have five (IIRC) seperate Demiurges. </div> </div> </div>You do indeed RC.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saturnine Night, &quot;Nuclear Prometheans,&quot; p76</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what if the rumors are true? What if there really are Prometheans who channel the Pyros through atomic fission?<br /> <b>The question isn\u2019t settled. What follows is a collection of options, and it\u2019s up to the Storyteller which version is suitable for a chronicle.</b> Maybe the Nuclear Prometheans are all the issue of the Zeka, members of the sixth true Lineage. Maybe they\u2019re suitable as players\u2019 characters. Maybe they aren\u2019t. If the Storyteller doesn\u2019t want to use the Zeka as a Lineage, he could rule that the stories of the Nuclear Promethean are simply about a Promethean belonging to one of the \u201ccommon\u201d Lineages who has one of the Nuclear Bestowments detailed in this chapter, and who knows Irradiation Transmutations.<br /> Maybe they don\u2019t exist at all. Maybe none of it\u2019s true. Maybe the testing fields of New Mexico, Nullarbor and Novaya Zemlya are empty, and the spirits of radiation and the Flux-born zombies that sometimes face the Created have simply generated spontaneously.<br /> Maybe the knowledge that there really is nothing worse out there than a Promethean is enough horror on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saturnine Night, &quot;Nobody Knows It All,&quot;p76</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>More than anything else, it needs to be stressed that nobody knows the truth about the Nuclear Prometheans, as presented here.</b> The sum total of Promethean knowledge about their atomic relatives is printed in Promethean: The Created, pp. 218\u2013220. Even so, that\u2019s all the stories collected together. No one Promethean knows all of it, even old, well-traveled, highly knowledgeable individuals such as \u201cVerney.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The books just ever officially retconned the fact. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saturnine Night, &quot;Dirty Liars&quot; sidebar, p34</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn\u2019t we say from the beginning that supernatural creatures can\u2019t create Prometheans?<br /> Well, we did say that, yes. We\u2019ve also said to do what works for your games. We\u2019re by no means suggesting that every vampire, werewolf and mage out there go and create Prometheans as a monthly hobby. We\u2019re merely stating that the Divine Fire might find methods of expression other than humanity. If you\u2019re running a crossover game and exploring themes of humanity and how \u201csupernatural\u201d a person can become before the human in him fades entirely, the notion of creating a Promethean might be an interesting way to express that. As always, the philosophy is \u201cOptions are better than limitations.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>The Promethean lineup essentially runs &quot;Corebook, Storyteller's Guide, Player's Guide, Book Full of Options, Book Full of Options 2: Atomic Boogaloo.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Misplaced quote tag. 11-22-2014, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T12:33:30-07:00","id":254282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=254190#post254190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;Whole mess with demiurges&gt;<br /> (...)<br /> The Promethean lineup essentially runs &quot;Corebook, Storyteller's Guide, Player's Guide, Book Full of Options, Book Full of Options 2: Atomic Boogaloo.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice would be having one option on those question something like: &quot;Most of the times supernaturals can't become demiurges. But from time to time ( and when your story need it ) some very human like monsters can make one of Created.&quot;<br /> <br /> Good would be to have one answer in <b>Promethean 2ed</b>- even vouge like this - on other topics that evolved with whole gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T11:00:51-07:00","id":254403,"title":"","content":"Something I'd like to see a bit more on is Humors. I always felt like they didn't get much talk for how important they were to a Promethean emotional development. I'm not saying it needs to be like the Pillar system, but a little section just talking about how they all relate to your characters development would be cool. <br /> <br /> Also I remember hearing that there's going to be 7 Lineages now, am I right in guessing that they're sticking Zeka and Unfleshed with the rest of the group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T11:23:57-07:00","id":254473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=254403#post254403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I'd like to see a bit more on is Humors. I always felt like they didn't get much talk for how important they were to a Promethean emotional development. I'm not saying it needs to be like the Pillar system, but a little section just talking about how they all relate to your characters development would be cool.<br /> <br /> Also I remember hearing that there's going to be 7 Lineages now, am I right in guessing that they're sticking Zeka and Unfleshed with the rest of the group?</div> </div> </div> </div>no zeka were mentioned in the gen con announcement, but they're adding unfleshed and extempore as full lineages. i'm assuming the zeka are either going to become a humor type for one of the &quot;new&quot; lineages or be written as dark mirror-type antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T11:37:12-07:00","id":254482,"title":"","content":"Oh! In that case, considering Zeka are basically just a really specific type of Extempore, I could see them getting folded in to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T17:30:15-07:00","id":254862,"title":"","content":"<b>PtC 2nd Ed </b>takes the position that your creator can be another Promethean or a demiurge. I always liked that idea (which is why it shows up so frequently in the sourcebooks; the reason it was downplayed in the core was some waffle about game balance, which as we know, is a myth), so it's official as of 2nd Ed. <br /> <br /> Zeka don't show up in 2nd Ed unless I find myself with some spare word count (ha). If I get to a Night Horrors book like I want to, I'll put 'em there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T17:44:20-07:00","id":254875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=254862#post254862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>PtC 2nd Ed </b>takes the position that your creator can be another Promethean or a demiurge.</div> </div> </div> </div>YES!<br /> *ahem* Thank you for making this option a bigger part of the game. I\u2019m eagerly awaiting further spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T19:45:10-07:00","id":254957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=254862#post254862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>PtC 2nd Ed </b>takes the position that your creator can be another Promethean or a demiurge.</div> </div> </div> </div>At last, demiurges get they share of love! And I could easily put any other Generative Act, as they can be anyone.<br /> <br /> Side question - could we see True Demiurges? Those that really make new Progenitors? It could be only mentioning in text, but nice would be pointing to typical demiurge as only lesser being, that is, in reality, remaking things that was once set in stone by TD cnturies ago.<br /> <br /> What will be officially stated position in <b>PtC 2nd Ed </b> on case of supernatural demiurges? &quot;Most of the time it doesn't work. At least to the time you need it in story&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Will we get a hints about previous Linages, like vampires get idea of non-existaned Clans? The Linage of Fire, that died in Great Fire of London, and being changed with Frankenstein's century later could be the thing like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T19:55:43-07:00","id":254964,"title":"","content":"Wait, what? First we have Demiurges, and now we're asking for True Deimurges? What, is there like a Super Demiurge above that? Is their Azoth over 9,000?<br /> <br /> A demiurge is a demiurge-the sheer fact that someone just made a whole, new, living being from impossible laws is astounding, regardless of if they use a new process or an old one.<br /> <br /> &quot;Geez, you create life and people immediately start asking for something better. The consumer base really does have a short attention span&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T20:23:28-07:00","id":254991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=254964#post254964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what? First we have Demiurges, and now we're asking for True Deimurges? What, is there like a Super Demiurge above that? Is their Azoth over 9,000?<br /> <br /> A demiurge is a demiurge-the sheer fact that someone just made a whole, new, living being from impossible laws is astounding, regardless of if they use a new process or an old one.<br /> <br /> &quot;Geez, you create life and people immediately start asking for something better. The consumer base really does have a short attention span&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I get before from corebook and this topics quotes ( thanks <b>Setchel</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) is that there are demiurges reanacting ancient formulas - like guys working on Victor Frankenstein's notes, or using rabbi's <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Loew spell to creat Golem. They are not making new Generative Acts, only copying it.<br /> <br /> And then we have &quot;True&quot; Demiurges that create Progenitor Prometheans. Literal Victor Frnakenstein, Pigmalion, Tamuz god, all of them. They not following someones else footsteps, they make new path for others.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T20:50:47-07:00","id":255013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=254991#post254991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I get before from corebook and this topics quotes ( thanks <b>Setchel</b>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) is that there are demiurges reanacting ancient formulas - like guys working on Victor Frankenstein's notes, or using rabbi's [COLOR=#222222][FONT=arial]Loew spell to creat Golem. They are not making new Generative Acts, only copying it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And meanwhile almost literally <i>every one of the Unfleshed</i> is the creation of a demiurge who used their own process. Legion, Aeolipilus and Tachanka do not share a line of descent.<br /> <br /> Apropos of nothing, I find myself wondering whether the Extempore's inclusion in the 2e core Lineages might factor in the original writeup's &quot;serendipitous throng of Freaks&quot; story seed, given the acknowledged difficulties of the generative act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T20:51:34-07:00","id":255014,"title":"","content":"Asides from the genius of producing a new Lineage, I don't see a point of making too much of a distinguishing point though. It's not something I'd touch on mechanically, and I'd only make a footnote about Demiurges.<br /> <br /> But then again, I never jumped for a Promethean writing position, despite my love for the series, so that says a few things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T21:04:04-07:00","id":255027,"title":"","content":"Indeed. If we get roll-your-own-Lineage guidelines, then we get \u201ctrue demiurges\u201d automatically, without any need to distinguish \u201ctrue\u201d from \u201cregular\u201d \u2014 nor any particular benefit from drawing the distinction, unless it\u2019s a repeatable phenomenon. If we <i>don\u2019t</i> get guidelines for custom Lineages, \u201ctrue demiurges\u201d aren\u2019t really a thing. <br /> <br /> And I\u2019m fine with the creation of a new Lineage being a once-in-a-Millenium kind of thing \u2014 though how that jibes with the Extempore, I\u2019m not sure: the whole notion behind the Extempore is that a Promethean can be created <i>by accident</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T23:23:43-07:00","id":255082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=255027#post255027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I\u2019m fine with the creation of a new Lineage being a once-in-a-Millenium kind of thing \u2014 though how that jibes with the Extempore, I\u2019m not sure: the whole notion behind the Extempore is that a Promethean can be created <i>by accident</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without, we <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V_(comics)#Origin\" target=\"_blank\">wouldn't get the V</a>, don't you think? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T05:28:23-07:00","id":255197,"title":"","content":"I've never liked the idea that Victor Frankenstein's notes or Rabbi Loew's writings would help. Because from what we know about the generative act it's not about the science, really - it's about the all-consuming need to create this new, transgressive life, and that it's almost impossible to repeat (for humans) once they know it can be done. We also know that the Divine Fire can animate just about anything, including steampunky robots, nanotech, a drone, clay, stone, a tree and possibly sand, so I don't think it matters if your stitching is bad and you've put the spleen on the wrong side. I can see it being helpful to a Promethean since the rules work differently for them - they've got the Pyros required already and some practical guidance is useful. But for a would-be Demiurge? To me, it seems as though it would more likely hinder the process, since it says that it can be done. But PtC has always had a funny relationship with science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T05:42:54-07:00","id":255200,"title":"","content":"I think the whole thing with &quot;follow the recipes&quot; is based on alchemical nature of the game. Ancient formulas are to be repeated because the Divine Fire needs perfection, nothing less. You can't possibly repeat act of Creation because on the end of it <b>you are imperfect</b> by Flux radiant and Disquiet you are touched with. You aren't enough pure to be vehicle for absolute of Gods Fire.<br /> <br /> In this light, following recipes that work is &quot;going in the footsteps of forefathers&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-12-2014, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T06:38:36-07:00","id":255223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=254862#post254862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>PtC 2nd Ed </b>takes the position that your creator can be another Promethean or a demiurge ... the reason it was downplayed in the core was some waffle about game balance, which as we know, is a myth</div> </div> </div> </div>... ooh. Now that's interesting. What kind of strange &quot;game balance&quot; is this?<br /> <br /> (As behind-the-scenes stuff goes, this should be spoiler-free, and darn but I'm curious about the expanded of that sentence.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=254282#post254282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice would be having one option on those question something like: &quot;Most of the times supernaturals can't become demiurges. But from time to time ( and when your story need it ) some very human like monsters can make one of Created.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I wouldn't address whether nonhumans can become Demiurges at all. Promethean isn't, after all, a crossover game.<br /> <br /> It seems like it would - should - vary based on the metaphysics and themes of your Chronicle, and from species to species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T07:31:47-07:00","id":255279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=255223#post255223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... ooh. Now that's interesting. What kind of strange &quot;game balance&quot; is this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Invocation of &quot;game balance&quot; is the easiest way to earn a flogging from the master... er, Matt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T08:38:33-07:00","id":255335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=255223#post255223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I wouldn't address whether nonhumans can become Demiurges at all. Promethean isn't, after all, a crossover game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every nWoD game is both pro crossover and anti crossover. Yeah, Prometheans have problems with interaction with other supernaturals and mortals from Disquiet. But other supers also have them - Vampires can work moslty in night and don't have pulse. Werewolves are in torn of Rage. <br /> <br /> I say that one clear sentance in whole <b>Promethean</b> <b>2ed</b> corebook for solving common problem with crossover groups ( and I heard mostly of this situation in our local RPGers ) is rather great adding value, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T08:42:48-07:00","id":255336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=255200#post255200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the whole thing with &quot;follow the recipes&quot; is based on alchemical nature of the game. Ancient formulas are to be repeated because the Divine Fire needs perfection, nothing less. You can't possibly repeat act of Creation because on the end of it <b>you are imperfect</b> by Flux radiant and Disquiet you are touched with. You aren't enough pure to be vehicle for absolute of Gods Fire.<br /> <br /> In this light, following recipes that work is &quot;going in the footsteps of forefathers&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes perfect sense for traditional alchemy.<br /> <br /> That doesn't work for Progenitor creation.<br /> <br /> The act of creating a new life is an act for the desperate. THe Divine Fire does not reach for people who aren't giving themselves-if anything, someone who doesn't have their entire being consumed by their need just don't make for a strong enough 'wire' for it to conduct. THe people making it having to clawing at the fabric of reality with nothing left to have the strength to steal from the Gods and bring down the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> Why do I bring this up?<br /> <br /> How desperate are you using a known method? If you're safe and secure in the idea that doing this will produce this, how desperate can you be?<br /> <br /> Not very. Not enough to pull down the heavens and ignite the body in front of you.<br /> <br /> I imagine Demiurges may use the old rituals as a guideline, no problem, but each Demiurge <i>has to</i> put their own spin on it. What came before won't work again. if a long line of Demiurges shred the journals with each other, each one doing their own based off the previous version, by the end you'd have a completely different ritual from the first inspiration.<br /> <br /> Depending on how common demiurges are now, that may result in new lineages being born all the time. I don't imagine they're long lived, but enough ritual drift would lead to some oddballs.<br /> <br /> Anyways, Prometheans have it easy in that regard, because the Divine Fire isn't overtly keeping out of their hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T16:17:50-07:00","id":255637,"title":"","content":"And there\u2019s some cognitive dissonance between that position and the fact that a Promethean can come to be when a natural disaster leaves a corpse in its wake which subsequently gets caught up in a Firestorm. In the case of these Extempore, there\u2019s no act of desperation involved, because there\u2019s no creator to act desperately. The whole premise behind the Extempore is that all you need to create a Promethean is a corpse that has been immersed in a suitable element and an infusion of Pyros; if a mortal can arrange for these conditions to be met, no desperation is needed. <br /> <br /> In short, it\u2019s not clear to me that <b>Promethean 2e</b> is going to present the task of the demiurge in the same way that 1e did. In fact, with demiurges confirmed as being much more of a thing in 2e than they were in 1e, it wouldn\u2019t surprise me if \u201cdemiurgy\u201d ends up being much easier to pull off than it was in 1e. <br /> <br /> Which is not to say that elements of obsession and madness won\u2019t be in there anymore; but I could see cause and effect being reversed between the two editions: instead of desperation being the key ingredient that enables a mortal to make a Promethean, a Disquiet-like effect gets directed at the aspiring demiurge and threatens to drive him mad if he pursues the task all the way through to completion. That is, the cause is Pyros; the effect is a mentally unbalanced demiurge \u2014 as opposed to 1e, where the cause was desperation and the effect was the spontaneous generation of the Pyros needed to animate the corpse. <br /> <br /> Of course, it\u2019s <i>also</i> possible that matters aren\u2019t quite that clear: it may be that most acts of demiurgy is accompanied by a Firestorm, but that a Firestorm can sometimes be triggered by an act of desperation \u2014 so there may indeed be cases where desperation was the key that allowed the mortal to create the Promethean. <br /> <br /> Remember also that we\u2019re getting mortal alchemists as antagonists in 2e: these will almost certainly be presented as mortals who have developed techniques for acquiring and utilizing Pyros. Their antagonistic nature would fit naturally with the notion that handling Pyros is fundamentally hazardous to a mortal\u2019s (mental) health. And if the generative act is essentially as I described above, then it would follow that most demiurges would be alchemists: it would be their alchemical aptitude, rather than desperation, that lets them perform the generative act. The act of desperation approach would primarily be for those rare demiurges who <i>aren\u2019t</i> alchemists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T16:49:39-07:00","id":255660,"title":"","content":"I explain what I know to be the rule. I can do no more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T22:39:17-07:00","id":255847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=255637#post255637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember also that we\u2019re getting mortal alchemists as antagonists in 2e: these will almost certainly be presented as mortals who have developed techniques for acquiring and utilizing Pyros.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is <i>quite</i> a leap in reasoning, I'll just note.<br /> <br /> Calogero got by on Redemption and occult knowhow, and Moses Moon managed (in the version where he is indeed a demiurge) on just the latter by virtue of having witnessed the generative act and borrowed principles therefrom (to the degree that his notes can help a Promethean with the process).<br /> <br /> Not all alchemy need manipulate the raw Spark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T02:49:58-07:00","id":257123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=255279#post255279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Invocation of &quot;game balance&quot; is the easiest way to earn a flogging from the master... er, Matt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm hoping His wrath will be directed at whoever thought it was good idea to lock Demiurges out of actual <i>gameplay</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=255637#post255637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember also that we\u2019re getting mortal alchemists as antagonists in 2e: these will almost certainly be presented as mortals who have developed techniques for acquiring and utilizing Pyros. Their antagonistic nature would fit naturally with the notion that handling Pyros is fundamentally hazardous to a mortal\u2019s (mental) health. And if the generative act is essentially as I described above, then it would follow that most demiurges would be alchemists: it would be their alchemical aptitude, rather than desperation, that lets them perform the generative act. The act of desperation approach would primarily be for those rare demiurges who <i>aren\u2019t</i> alchemists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still hopeful that Alchemists are humans who have figured out how to perform Transmutations using &quot;regular&quot; alchemy. Y'know, with alembics and chemicals and obsessively-charted symbolism in everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=255336#post255336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How desperate are you using a known method? If you're safe and secure in the idea that doing this will produce this, how desperate can you be?</div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>are</i> no &quot;known methods&quot;. Not among mortals.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's why a Progenitor has to spend years obsessively experimenting, theorizing, tracking down examples of partial success. (Not to mention actually building it, of course.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-15-2014, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T05:09:50-07:00","id":257209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=257123#post257123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still hopeful that Alchemists are humans who have figured out how to perform Transmutations using &quot;regular&quot; alchemy. Y'know, with alembics and chemicals and obsessively-charted symbolism in everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it <i>is</i> <b>Promethean</b>, so I would expect alchemists to utilize <b>Promethean</b>\u2019s metaphysics, where Pyros is the agent of change. That said, manipulating Pyros shouldn\u2019t come naturally to mortals, something that could be reflected in part by requiring alembics and chemicals et al to do something that a Promethean can do without all that hoop-jumping. And the desperation thing? Keep it in as a means of generating Pyros when you don\u2019t have a supply of it (e.g., extracted from a Promethean or harvested from a Firestorm).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T05:26:33-07:00","id":257216,"title":"","content":"Where was it confirmed that Demiurges and mortals in general will be a larger element of the narrative in 2e Promethean? I'm certainly glad if it's the case. I felt that Promethean needed more of it when I read the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T09:12:02-07:00","id":257316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=257123#post257123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There <i>are</i> no &quot;known methods&quot;. Not among mortals.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's why a Progenitor has to spend years obsessively experimenting, theorizing, tracking down examples of partial success. (Not to mention actually building it, of course.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, that's what I'm saying, although not from the same direction.<br /> <br /> The reason there are no known methods is because every method that works has been, conventionally, a one-time alchemical miracle is because each one was the product of a person's deperation They try an unknown method and work on it and work on it until they're so desperate that it grabs the Divine Fire and forces it down, making a mixture of extreme will and alchemical sympathies.<br /> <br /> So let's say someone grabs a hold of, say, Frankentstien's journals. They try to replicate the results, they follow his method. They think this is a known method, it's sure to work.<br /> <br /> They get the form, but not the extreme-desperate-will that way. So it doesn't work. So they build off of what Victor wrote, develop their own ideas, apply new principles, experiment. By the time they're desperate enough to draw down the Fire, the experiment is a whole new affair.<br /> <br /> THere are no known methods because every method that's made burns out with the act. It is a magnum opus, a masterpiece, the strike of lightning that will never come again.<br /> <br /> At least, as of First Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-23-2014, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T12:08:18-07:00","id":257473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>blackhatmatt: </b><br /> PtC 2nd Ed takes the position that your creator can be another Promethean or a demiurge. </div> </div> </div>Does the demiurge still have to be human, or can another supernatural do it? (Personally, I can't see that it makes a difference if they can). Do Prometheans still have to make an offspring in order to make it to mortality? (If they do, and a Lineage can have, in effect, multiple demiurges, it implies a higher number of Prometheans in the world than the first edition setting, albeit not necessarily much).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> eberg: <br /> Invocation of &quot;game balance&quot; is the easiest way to earn a flogging from the master... er, Matt. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but I share MugaSofer's confusion about why Prometheans being variously made by themselves or a demiurge would have any relevence to game balance no matter how real or mythical. Unless it's going to have a mechanical effect of some kind, or unless we are going to have a Lineage-making system after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=255637#post255637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of these Extempore, there\u2019s no act of desperation involved, because there\u2019s no creator to act desperately.</div> </div> </div> </div>There may be the desperation of the dead body's former owner to survive. Which they don't, of course, but the psychic ingredient is provided regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T14:56:14-07:00","id":257620,"title":"","content":"On the desperation thing: I get it, and I see the attraction of the notion \u2014 to an extent. My single biggest problem with the notion is that if every single act of alchemy performed by a mortal is a one-time miracle that shall never be repeated, that greatly limits the viability of alchemists as ongoing characters. This is <i>especially</i> true if what mortal alchemy can do is defined by the Promethean Transmutations: in effect, you\u2019re saying that a given mortal can use any given Transmutation <i>once</i>, on top of whatever other restrictions he has to contend with. <br /> <br /> As I see it, alchemy powered by acts of desperation has its place; just not as the <i>only</i> thing that mortal alchemists can do, or even as the <i>main</i> thing they can do. That\u2019s one reason why I was suggesting the possibility of Pyros-fueled alchemy as their mainstay, with desperation-fueled alchemy supplementing it by letting them transcend the limits of Pyros-fueled alchemy. And if desperation-fueled alchemy can only be done once, it really ought to be accomplishing something truly spectacular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T17:03:26-07:00","id":257690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=257620#post257620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the desperation thing: I get it, and I see the attraction of the notion \u2014 to an extent. My single biggest problem with the notion is that if every single act of alchemy performed by a mortal is a one-time miracle that shall never be repeated, that greatly limits the viability of alchemists as ongoing characters. This is <i>especially</i> true if what mortal alchemy can do is defined by the Promethean Transmutations: in effect, you\u2019re saying that a given mortal can use any given Transmutation <i>once</i>, on top of whatever other restrictions he has to contend with.<br /> <br /> As I see it, alchemy powered by acts of desperation has its place; just not as the <i>only</i> thing that mortal alchemists can do, or even as the <i>main</i> thing they can do. That\u2019s one reason why I was suggesting the possibility of Pyros-fueled alchemy as their mainstay, with desperation-fueled alchemy supplementing it by letting them transcend the limits of Pyros-fueled alchemy. And if desperation-fueled alchemy can only be done once, it really ought to be accomplishing something truly spectacular.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I'm talking about the generative act. Others forms of alchemy don't need desperation. I don't demand desperation for conventional alchemy, just generative acts. That has <i>always</i> been my point.<br /> <br /> 2)The limiting the viability of alchemists as ongoing characters is....Well, look, it's cool that they're there. It's a very nifty expansion of the game, and I can see why people are excited about it.<br /> <br /> But I will lose no sleep saying that alchemists are low on my list of things to care about. It's very much not my problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T22:29:56-07:00","id":257895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=257123#post257123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">lock Demiurges out of actual <i>gameplay</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lacking an especially polite way to say this, I'll stay brief: <i>the hell are you on about?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T23:28:57-07:00","id":257931,"title":"","content":"Alchemists, schmalchemists, give me a race of Igors!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T00:22:52-07:00","id":257954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=254862#post254862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zeka don't show up in 2nd Ed unless I find myself with some spare word count (ha). If I get to a <b>Night Horrors book</b> like I want to, I'll put 'em there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>buhwhaaa?! If ever there was a line for a Night Horrors it'd be Promethean - the game of freaks, loners, one-offs, mutants, and mad scientists!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T07:34:25-07:00","id":258121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=257620#post257620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I see it, alchemy powered by acts of desperation has its place; just not as the <i>only</i> thing that mortal alchemists can do, or even as the <i>main</i> thing they can do. That\u2019s one reason why I was suggesting the possibility of Pyros-fueled alchemy as their mainstay, with desperation-fueled alchemy supplementing it by letting them transcend the limits of Pyros-fueled alchemy. And if desperation-fueled alchemy can only be done once, it really ought to be accomplishing something truly spectacular.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd express this as the difference between Pyros and Azoth, the latter being described in the first ediiton as a more refined and puried version of the former. How I think it should work is most alchemy working by conjuring Pyros, but the more spectacular stuff like creating life working by creating a lasting Azoth, the latter being the one that requires desperate obsession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T12:12:49-07:00","id":258356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=257895#post257895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lacking an especially polite way to say this, I'll stay brief: <i>the hell are you on about?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty simple.<br /> <br /> A lot of people complained about the idea, found in Promethean core, that there was a single Demiurge per Lineage and they died centuries ago. Rather than making them a type of NPC, so players could interact with their mortal Creators and there could be evil slave-driving Demiurge villains and so forth.<br /> <br /> Matt responded with this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=254862#post254862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>PtC 2nd Ed </b>takes the position that your creator can be another Promethean or a demiurge. I always liked that idea (which is why it shows up so frequently in the sourcebooks; the reason it was downplayed in the core was some waffle about game balance, which as we know, is a myth), so it's official as of 2nd Ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was curious to hear the &quot;waffle about game balance&quot; that led to this odd decision, that's all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T13:46:07-07:00","id":258423,"title":"","content":"Do Demiurges have to be evil? I know that there are some Redeemed that are immune to Disquiet, perhaps a fee creators are as well. Sure their obsession drives them to create the Promethean in the first place, but that doesn't mean it continues after the deed is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T15:29:34-07:00","id":258504,"title":"","content":"Obssessed, desperate individuals hardly have the tendencies to be good people.<br /> <br /> That said, that doesn't immeadiately mean they're inherently bad people either. Just...prone to bad behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T19:23:32-07:00","id":258614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=258356#post258356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty simple.<br /> <br /> A lot of people complained about the idea, found in Promethean core, that there was a single Demiurge per Lineage and they died centuries ago. Rather than making them a type of NPC, so players could interact with their mortal Creators and there could be evil slave-driving Demiurge villains and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this a) has <i>fuckall to do with gameplay</i>, \u03b2) is based on a markedly false reading of the way the line turned out and an uncharitable reading of both the corebook and the sample chronicle <i>including a demiurge's creation as the focus of a story</i>, and 3) appears to be a dramatic overstatement of the matter's constituent proportion of Complaints About Promethean relative to, say, the constellation of Disquiet effects.*<br /> <br /> The fact that one of the 2e core Lineages is the one that 1e had as <i>almost categorically the product of a human demiurge</i>, along with the direction 1e took on the matter after the corebook, would seem to heavily indicate that this is on the list of &quot;things that were going to change anyway that it does you no good to complain about for more than a sentence or two in a speculation thread.&quot;<br /> <br /> * Speaking of which, Disquiet rules that help with the throughline of &quot;Prometheans can generally last a little longer in the midst of people that are already ill-perceived by society&quot; that gets mentioned a bit in the corebook and sees its probable culmination in the person of Oleg Wormwood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T07:38:16-07:00","id":258975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=258614#post258614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this a) has <i>fuckall to do with gameplay</i>, \u03b2) is based on a markedly false reading of the way the line turned out and an uncharitable reading of both the corebook and the sample chronicle <i>including a demiurge's creation as the focus of a story</i>, and 3) appears to be a dramatic overstatement of the matter's constituent proportion of Complaints About Promethean relative to, say, the constellation of Disquiet effects.*<br /> <br /> The fact that one of the 2e core Lineages is the one that 1e had as <i>almost categorically the product of a human demiurge</i>, along with the direction 1e took on the matter after the corebook, would seem to heavily indicate that <b>this is on the list of &quot;things that were going to change anyway that it does you no good to complain about</b> for more than a sentence or two in a speculation thread.&quot;<br /> <br /> * Speaking of which, Disquiet rules that help with the throughline of &quot;Prometheans can generally last a little longer in the midst of people that are already ill-perceived by society&quot; that gets mentioned a bit in the corebook and sees its probable culmination in the person of Oleg Wormwood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't <i>complaining</i>, Satchel. I was <i>asking</i> about something Matt mentioned. I'm well aware that this was more or less immediately fixed; indeed, I was replying to a comment in which a developer says so.<br /> <br /> Good idea WRT Disquiet, incidentally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T09:46:46-07:00","id":259019,"title":"","content":"Satchel, please watch the tone, you are coming across as combatitive. I can't use red text when responding from my phone but this is still a moderator request. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T07:10:01-07:00","id":259739,"title":"","content":"Okay now I'm curious, what is this hankering for human creators about? <br /> <br /> I mean storywise, a promethean having daddy issues because their demiurge went mad with disquiet and joined the torch bearing mob I would think get cliche pretty quickly in a promethean game. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T12:51:06-07:00","id":259974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=259739#post259739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Okay now I'm curious, what is this hankering for human creators about?<br /> <br /> I mean storywise, a promethean having daddy issues because their demiurge went mad with disquiet and joined the torch bearing mob I would think get cliche pretty quickly in a promethean game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can sorta understand this. I played an Unfleshed Promethean, who had a really good relationship with his creator (who were naturally human) and I've just started another Promethean Ulgan character who had a short-lived teacher-student relationship with his. Out of the two, I much-much prefer the Mother-Son relationship between my Unfleshed than the teacher-student relationship of the Ulgan. I think its very difficult to have such a mother-son relationship between two Prometheans because even the &quot;mother&quot; Promethean isn't in a mental state to really care enough for a &quot;child&quot; as a human would be.<br /> Add that to the fact that it adds another layer of uniqueness to the individual Promethean, seeing as how they no longer need to fit into the &quot;created by either X,Y,Z,Q,V Generative Act&quot;, I can totally get behind this change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T15:07:32-07:00","id":260128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=259739#post259739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Okay now I'm curious, what is this hankering for human creators about?<br /> <br /> I mean storywise, a promethean having daddy issues because their demiurge went mad with disquiet and joined the torch bearing mob I would think get cliche pretty quickly in a promethean game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This comment originally consisted of a <i>long list</i> of story hooks centred around human creators ... but the software ate it.<br /> <br /> Gah.<br /> <br /> OK, suffice to say, there are ... several ... possibilities beyond that singular idea. Seriously, sit down for a moment and try to think of ideas. If I am any indication, many will come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T15:55:36-07:00","id":260163,"title":"","content":"Indeed. It\u2019s like saying \u201cwhat\u2019s the point of having Fetches in <b>Changeling</b>? The \u2018evil twin\u2019 thing would get old after a while.\u201d<br /> <br /> And, like fetches, you don\u2019t have to incorporate a demiurge into your character\u2019s story if you don\u2019t want to. It\u2019s an option for those who are interested, not a mandate. As opposed to the way that Promethean creators were mandatory in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T00:48:02-07:00","id":260411,"title":"","content":"Dropping mortal demiurges is a side effect of developing Lineages. Lineages are there to present archetypes for new players to seize, and don't make sense in a world where mortals are the primary source of Prometheans. I'm not saying this either a good or a bad thing, just as an observation. I do think that proponents of a Humour-based pseudo-Lineage system might find the reintroduction of MDs (mortal demiurges) as counterintuitive and hinky, since mortals lack Humours, and thus couldn't be said to be imbalanced or whatever might imbue the newly Created with its key Humour.<br /> <br /> Not that I haven't seen the most gossamer of justifications for such traits in my time. Still, I see Humours and MD's as mutually exclusive to some degree, and I certainly don't see Humours as component phenomena of the Pyros or the Azoth, else we'd see angels and 'storms tainted by them as well. And if they did show up (PATENT PENDING), then you'd want to reintroduce the whole shebang back into the Things Modern Humans Forgot. I guess that appeals to some, though I have no desire to encounter Phlegm Angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T07:54:04-07:00","id":260598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=260411#post260411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dropping mortal demiurges is a side effect of developing Lineages. Lineages are there to present archetypes for new players to seize, and don't make sense in a world where mortals are the primary source of Prometheans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to recall seeing mention that many of the new mortal demiurges would be following the recipes of earlier ones, and so producing Prometheans who fit into an existing Lineage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, I see Humours and MD's as mutually exclusive to some degree, and I certainly don't see Humours as component phenomena of the Pyros or the Azoth, else we'd see angels and 'storms tainted by them as well. </div> </div> </div>I don't see how that follows - all the first edition Lineages descend from MD's, and they have Humours. Or when you say &quot;Humour-based pseudo-Lineage system,&quot; do you mean the whole hog replacement of Lineage as an x-splat with Humour? (My own proponence - is that a word? - was only about a quarter of that hog).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T23:24:48-07:00","id":261856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=260598#post260598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to recall seeing mention that many of the new mortal demiurges would be following the recipes of earlier ones, and so producing Prometheans who fit into an existing Lineage.<br /> <br /> I don't see how that follows - all the first edition Lineages descend from MD's, and they have Humours. Or when you say &quot;Humour-based pseudo-Lineage system,&quot; do you mean the whole hog replacement of Lineage as an x-splat with Humour? (My own proponence - is that a word? - was only about a quarter of that hog).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lineages have Humours, but they're the result of fortuitous and unique events happening over the course of millennia, possibly as part of a greater scheme. MD's working from a recipe shouldn't engender the same sort of exception. Humours are discredited as science, and yet mortals being able to replicate the originating creation from a recipe actually manages to <i>be</i> science. This strikes me as against the Principle (whatever it is), and also diminishes the specialness of Prometheans, who no longer are divinely inspired, but are ready-to-make monsters? <br /> <br /> Of course, what if this imbalance is a source of Disquiet too? By yielding up the Sanguine, a Muse's Demiurge loses his own, making him irritable and obsessive and prudish? He then begins to suck it out of others, spreading the Disquiet like a chain reaction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T23:37:44-07:00","id":261860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=261856#post261856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MD's working from a recipe shouldn't engender the same sort of exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's the entire point of the generative ritual - to <i>encode aspects of the alchemical formula that makes a Promethean of a certain Lineage in a format that can be parsed by a sub-transcendent intellect</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humours are discredited as science, and yet mortals being able to replicate the originating creation from a recipe actually manages to <i>be</i> science. </div> </div> </div>When the recipe calls for &quot;+1 miraculous theft born of human desperation and the mercurial whims of an unknowable universe&quot;\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This strikes me as against the Principle (whatever it is), and also diminishes the specialness of Prometheans, who no longer are divinely inspired, but are ready-to-make monsters? </div> </div> </div>Mortal demiurges are almost categorically exhausted by their bringing the seeds of new life into the world. That <i>bad things</i> tend to wind up happening to post-partem demiurges is part and parcel of 1e's note against the specter of mass-produced Created.<br /> <br /> tl;dr This is a bad argument and I refer you to my preceding omnidirectional exhortation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T00:33:53-07:00","id":261885,"title":"","content":"Nah, it's a GREAT argument! You just need the human desperation to see it, but we will get you there, Satch!<br /> <br /> I'd hate to call a MD creation part of a Lineage. It's made the same way, but it's not <i>part</i> of a Lineage. These are the Hackintoshes of the Created. It looks the same, it runs the same, and it's probably made with 10% less slave labor, but &quot;Lineage&quot; is inaccurate. Lineage is reduced from a personal inheritance back to the progenitor to a simple process carried out by a nutbag with a seriously sick sense of curiosity. Which is perfectly tits with me, but for me, I enjoy the baroque grandeur of the Created as children of the gods, midwifed by the insane, and cursed to commit original sin in order to redeem it. MD's haven't been a part of that experience for me, and I'd rather that if they're to be introduced, that they head their own unique Lineages, rather than crystallizing rituals around what was once a transgressive act. <br /> <br /> That is, it's not about mass-production, it's about semantics, dammit! The Pyros never sends angels out on the same mission twice, so why would it respond to the stale ceremonies of mortals trying to recreate what it already achieved? For Prometheans, the need to reproduce and the ability to transfer Azoth and Pyros is inherent, so new Wretched and Golems are a dime a dozen without the necessity of breaking the universe once more. If the Principle demands a new Promethean of a particular shade, it has a vine to pluck. Why would it waste the flameout of a would-be demiurge on more of the same?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T12:37:28-07:00","id":262391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=261856#post261856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humours are discredited as science</div> </div> </div> </div>As, supposedly, is alchemy. But we're still getting Alchemists as antagonists, and we're still getting Demiurges. Why not? Clearly, this stuff doesn't run on the same metaphysics as the real world.<br /> <br /> (Although, honestly, I always thought the Lineage/Humour mapping was a little forced. I usually make it more of a fluffy theory than anything else, in my games.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=261885#post261885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I enjoy the baroque grandeur of the Created as children of the gods, midwifed by the insane, and cursed to commit original sin in order to redeem it. MD's haven't been a part of that experience for me, and I'd rather that if they're to be introduced, that they head their own unique Lineages, rather than crystallizing rituals around what was once a transgressive act.<br /> <br /> That is, it's not about mass-production, it's about semantics, dammit! The Pyros never sends angels out on the same mission twice, so why would it respond to the stale ceremonies of mortals trying to recreate what it already achieved? For Prometheans, the need to reproduce and the ability to transfer Azoth and Pyros is inherent, so new Wretched and Golems are a dime a dozen without the necessity of breaking the universe once more. If the Principle demands a new Promethean of a particular shade, it has a vine to pluck. Why would it waste the flameout of a would-be demiurge on more of the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. I'm not sure I'm parsing this right.<br /> <br /> Are you saying that in order to prevent Promethean-creation seeming routine and boring, we should make them &quot;a dime a dozen&quot; from Promethean creators and <i>never</i> the unique creations of mortal Demiurges?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T20:50:03-07:00","id":264369,"title":"","content":"Stop me if this has been said already, but I think they need to fix the Frankenstein's <b>Unholy Strength</b> bestowment. I mean, the mechanics of it are a little silly--you can't punch someone super hard but you can tear a lamppost out of the ground and throw it? Yeah, I hope they fix that...<br /> <br /> Other things have been said and I'd just like to reiterate\u2026They definitely need to stick to the weirdness of Prometheans, and also stick good and hard to the body horror aspects as well. Also, they should stick to the powerhouse feel that was emphasized in the first edition. Prometheans are one of the toughest, most indestructible supernatural creatures in the NWoD, with city-shaking powers to match, and I definitely think they need to keep that edge. <br /> <br /> And as mentioned by other posts here, transmutations which allow a Promethean to move and control removed body pieces at a distance would certainly make sense to me (moving a hand that's been removed, or controlling your body if your head has been cut off, like some of the powers they had in the fan-made OWoD game <i>Zombie: the Coil</i>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T21:00:57-07:00","id":264371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=264369#post264369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stop me if this has been said already, but I think they need to fix the Frankenstein's <b>Unholy Strength</b> bestowment. I mean, the mechanics of it are a little silly--you can't punch someone super hard but you can tear a lamppost out of the ground and throw it? Yeah, I hope they fix that\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>You're playing a robot made of mismatched corpses vulcanized into motion by animal magnetism that buds off angelic intelligences and turns rocks into monsters. If your threshold of &quot;silly&quot; is the &quot;lift/smash/jump good&quot; power not being a &quot;punch good&quot; power on the grounds of physical logic I have to suggest that you've come to the wrong place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And as mentioned by other posts here, transmutations which allow a Promethean to move and control removed body pieces at a distance would certainly make sense to me (moving a hand that's been removed, or controlling your body if your head has been cut off, like some of the powers they had in the fan-made OWoD game <i>Zombie: the Coil</i>). </div> </div> </div>Your example is a corebook Pandoran Transmutation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T21:20:53-07:00","id":264373,"title":"","content":"Actually Satch, I'm with Hel on this one about Unholy Strength. I know it's a marked difference style of boost that appears not only in Promethean but in books up to and including Demon(as well as before, at least in Werewolf), but that was always an almighty confusion for me too. It makes a sort of balance sense in that it's useful but doesn't pin the Frankenstein's as a pure melee machine, but it's weird. It's weird every time I see it, and I think to myself that there has got be a better idea here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T21:24:37-07:00","id":264375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=264373#post264373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually Satch, I'm with Hel on this one about Unholy Strength. I know it's a marked difference style of boost that appears not only in Promethean but in books up to and including Demon(as well as before, at least in Werewolf), but that was always an almighty confusion for me too. It makes a sort of balance sense in that it's useful but doesn't pin the Frankenstein's as a pure melee machine, but it's weird. It's weird every time I see it, and I think to myself that there has got be a better idea here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think the more pressing matter would be how utterly borked Vitality wound up being as a Transmutation-set, to be frank.<br /> <br /> Good think the word is the power format's changing anyway!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T03:35:28-07:00","id":264487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=264371#post264371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your example is a corebook Pandoran Transmutation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for that...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=264371#post264371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're playing a robot made of mismatched corpses vulcanized into motion by animal magnetism that buds off angelic intelligences and turns rocks into monsters. If your threshold of &quot;silly&quot; is the &quot;lift/smash/jump good&quot; power not being a &quot;punch good&quot; power on the grounds of physical logic I have to suggest that you've come to the wrong place.</div> </div> </div> </div>My threshold of &quot;silly&quot; stems from the game mechanics feeling arbitrary and forced, not the fiction's internal logic. Many players have taken note of this, and as ArcaneArts stated, there probably is a better way to implement the idea here.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, I'd say fixing the Vitality transmutation set is just as important as making the bestowments work in a more comfortable way since both are an intrinsic part of play, would you disagree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","user":"hellovg","date":". 09-24-2014, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T05:49:50-07:00","id":264551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=264373#post264373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes a sort of balance sense in that it's useful but doesn't pin the Frankenstein's as a pure melee machine, but it's weird. It's weird every time I see it, and I think to myself that there has got be a better idea here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! I doubt we're getting this, as apparently there's some innovative-but-secret plan in the works, but I have a half-finished writeup sitting on my harddrive that did this!<br /> <br /> It worked like this:<br /> <br /> All Transmutations are bought as a paired Elpis and Flux fversion, called the Creative and Destructive. (For example, you might buy Shoulders of Atlas, which doubles your lift capacity, as the Creative use - and Hammer Blow, which makes your unarmed attacks deal Lethal damage, as the Destructive use.)<br /> <br /> The Elpis and Flux versions of a Transmutation used different dicepools, so you could specialize. But if you failed a Creative roll, then the Destructive effect would happen to the target instead; and if you failed a Destructive roll, then the effect would happen to the wrong target. (Like an innocent bystander. Or your friends. Or the item you came here to get.)<br /> <br /> This meant you could always turn to the Destructive use of your harmless-seeming Creative powers in a pinch; but if you didn't specialize in them, they'd be less effective that way. On the other hand, even the most evil-seeming villain could pet the dog once in a while with the Elpis half of their power; it just wasn't as good. The same Frankenstein could hurl terrifying torment-laced Lightning and heal their friends with Electroshock Therapy. A Golem could rework metals with their burning red-hot (or acid-coated) hands ... without creating questions of why they couldn't melt a target into slag. The scary serial-killer could drive people insane using the <i>same illusions </i>the friendly Galateid PC uses to misdirect scary enemies.<br /> <br /> I must admit, I really liked that idea. I might finish writing it up sometime as a houserule if the new Transmutations aren't mindblowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-24-2014, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T07:20:20-07:00","id":264591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=264375#post264375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think the more pressing matter would be how utterly borked Vitality wound up being as a Transmutation-set, to be frank.<br /> <br /> Good think the word is the power format's changing anyway!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh don't get me wrong, that was an issue. But just because something's a bigger issue doesn't mean something else isn't an issue.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To be fair, The key pint is that, of course, it's already being worked on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-24-2014, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T07:34:09-07:00","id":264599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=264487#post264487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, I'd say fixing the Vitality transmutation set is just as important as making the bestowments work in a more comfortable way since both are an intrinsic part of play, would you disagree?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would disagree that &quot;fix this Bestowment in particular&quot; is a terribly salient thing to want in light of &quot;the entire powerset is getting overhauled already, the mechanics of Transmutations and Bestowments as a whole have been wonky from the start (there's little to no set logic for what dicepool format a Transmutation uses and several Transmutations are highly subdivided for their cost), and it is not difficult to extrapolate Matt's noted issue with 'this power is so effective you're silly if you don't take it' stuff like Electroshock Recharge and his avowed preference for characters to be competent at what they do into 'Transmutations are going to benefit dramatically from the shift to a more viable format and structure.'&quot;<br /> <br /> Or, in short, &quot;I hope this very specific thing that's part of this much bigger thing that's already getting an overhaul gets an overhaul,&quot; framed as it was, is more of a complaint than a want-to-see and rather goes without saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-24-2014, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T07:35:29-07:00","id":264600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=264551#post264551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! I doubt we're getting this, as apparently there's some innovative-but-secret plan in the works, but I have a half-finished writeup sitting on my harddrive that did this!<br /> <br /> It worked like this:<br /> <br /> All Transmutations are bought as a paired Elpis and Flux fversion, called the Creative and Destructive. (For example, you might buy Shoulders of Atlas, which doubles your lift capacity, as the Creative use - and Hammer Blow, which makes your unarmed attacks deal Lethal damage, as the Destructive use.)<br /> <br /> The Elpis and Flux versions of a Transmutation used different dicepools, so you could specialize. But if you failed a Creative roll, then the Destructive effect would happen to the target instead; and if you failed a Destructive roll, then the effect would happen to the wrong target. (Like an innocent bystander. Or your friends. Or the item you came here to get.)<br /> <br /> This meant you could always turn to the Destructive use of your harmless-seeming Creative powers in a pinch; but if you didn't specialize in them, they'd be less effective that way. On the other hand, even the most evil-seeming villain could pet the dog once in a while with the Elpis half of their power; it just wasn't as good. The same Frankenstein could hurl terrifying torment-laced Lightning and heal their friends with Electroshock Therapy. A Golem could rework metals with their burning red-hot (or acid-coated) hands ... without creating questions of why they couldn't melt a target into slag. The scary serial-killer could drive people insane using the <i>same illusions </i>the friendly Galateid PC uses to misdirect scary enemies.<br /> <br /> I must admit, I really liked that idea. I might finish writing it up sometime as a houserule if the new Transmutations aren't mindblowing.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not misremembering, this was basically how Lores worked in DtF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T05:51:51-07:00","id":265378,"title":"","content":"I really liked how Transmutations worked. Big categories with varying levels, multiple powers at each level, and you just buy for whichever one you want without pre-reqs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T23:02:13-07:00","id":265982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=265378#post265378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really liked how Transmutations worked. Big categories with varying levels, multiple powers at each level, and you just buy for whichever one you want without pre-reqs</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. If those elements change (as opposed to the dicepools etc.) then ... well, I hope they have <i>very</i> good reasons for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-26-2014, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T11:54:53-07:00","id":266913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=265982#post265982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. If those elements change (as opposed to the dicepools etc.) then ... well, I hope they have <i>very</i> good reasons for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The flat experience costs in GMC does present a challenge for this, methinks. Previously the reason why you didn't get a 5 dot Transmutation right off the bat was because for each level within a School that you skipped, there would be an experience penalty. Now that all powers cost the same, what's to stop someone from grabbing a powerful Transmutation like Flesh to Stone with their first purchase after chargen?<br /> <br /> Since a big theme in Promethean is learning and understanding, I actually think that more &quot;trees&quot; (like the tech trees in an RTS or Twilight Imperium) within each School would work well. They have to gain a certain amount of understanding before applying bigger principles, and each Transmutation could represent a greater understanding of strength or Pyros or the supernatural or whatever.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll also be very interested to see how Werewolf's Gifts work in 2e. I think that will give us an idea of just how radical a transformation we could expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T13:19:17-07:00","id":266965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=266913#post266913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The flat experience costs in GMC does present a challenge for this, methinks. Previously the reason why you didn't get a 5 dot Transmutation right off the bat was because for each level within a School that you skipped, there would be an experience penalty. Now that all powers cost the same, what's to stop someone from grabbing a powerful Transmutation like Flesh to Stone with their first purchase after chargen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Changeling 2.0 explicitly nabbed the old!Transmutation mechanics for new!Contracts. They just made them cost the dot rating in XP as a flat cost, with no prerequisites or skill trees.<br /> <br /> It fits with the whole &quot;Prometheans are weird, every one of them is different&quot; thing - walking your own path to Redemption and so on. Transmutations tend to be quite different from each other, not building up gradually along the same lines like Disciplines or Arcana. Still, those are old!Transmutations; who knows what could happen in 2nd ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T14:12:08-07:00","id":266999,"title":"","content":"My issues with Promethean mainly come from having to remember all the various rules for Azoth, Torment and what causes it, the methods of regenerating Pyros etc... I think it could be streamlined in a new Chronicle Book... I don't mean make it more rules-lite, but making the crunch snappier and easier to remember rather than having a rule for everything kind of thing. I find Promethean and Werewolf to be the crunchiest of the nWoD games though YMMV of course.<br /> I don't believe Disquiet really needs to be amped down... It only becomes an issue at higher levels of Azoth where it can stretch out to entire cities. If I wanted to play Promethean myself I think the main pull would be having the game centre on the family of the Throng... Outside of the support of others, as the Promethean's Azoth grows as they 'try to be real', they're going to be walking the roads. Of course some kind of support for those Prometheans on 'road trip' games would be cool also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T04:16:01-07:00","id":268159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=264373#post264373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually Satch, I'm with Hel on this one about Unholy Strength. I know it's a marked difference style of boost that appears not only in Promethean but in books up to and including Demon(as well as before, at least in Werewolf), but that was always an almighty confusion for me too. It makes a sort of balance sense in that it's useful but doesn't pin the Frankenstein's as a pure melee machine, but it's weird. It's weird every time I see it, and I think to myself that there has got be a better idea here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When I ran <b>Promethean</b> before, Franks got 9-again on every Strength roll, including combat. Shockingly, this did not break the game, because as I keep saying, &quot;game balance&quot; is a myth. <br /> <br /> In 2nd ed, all seven Lineages (well, six Lineages and Extempore, who aren't properly a Lineage) have a choice between two Bestowments. One makes getting Beats easier (generally by making an exceptional success happen at 3 successes rather than 5) and one is a weird power (Spare Parts for the Frankensteins, Corpse Tongue for the Osirans).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T10:52:51-07:00","id":268347,"title":"","content":"Interesting... Will there still be the choices available for the weird powers as is? I've only played Promethean once for a one-shot, but I liked some Bestowments more than others... I played an Ulgan in the game I was in and straight away I went for Ephermeral Flesh over Orphean Song, though I like the use of the second one for when Disquiet becomes a problem for the Ulgan too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T17:43:35-07:00","id":268640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=268159#post268159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When I ran <b>Promethean</b> before, Franks got 9-again on every Strength roll, including combat. Shockingly, this did not break the game, because as I keep saying, &quot;game balance&quot; is a myth.<br /> <br /> In 2nd ed, all seven Lineages (well, six Lineages and Extempore, who aren't properly a Lineage) have a choice between two Bestowments. One makes getting Beats easier (generally by making an exceptional success happen at 3 successes rather than 5) and one is a weird power (Spare Parts for the Frankensteins, Corpse Tongue for the Osirans).</div> </div> </div> </div>See, even adding combat to it makes way more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-29-2014, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T19:40:17-07:00","id":268712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=268347#post268347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting... Will there still be the choices available for the weird powers as is? I've only played Promethean once for a one-shot, but I liked some Bestowments more than others... I played an Ulgan in the game I was in and straight away I went for Ephermeral Flesh over Orphean Song, though I like the use of the second one for when Disquiet becomes a problem for the Ulgan too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think we're using Orphean Song because we're downplaying the Orpheus connection, but yeah, every Lineage gets a choice of a) Condition/Beat generator or b) weird power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T19:44:53-07:00","id":268714,"title":"","content":"Two things leap to mind:<br /> <br /> 1) Are other Bestowments still able to be purchased later on?<br /> 2) Does this mean the Unfleshed now have &quot;standardized&quot; Bestowments (and Disquiet, Torment, etc)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T20:17:27-07:00","id":268719,"title":"","content":"So every character gets a choice between long-term character growth on the one hand or a supernatural power of some sort on the other? That has some intriguing implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T21:20:28-07:00","id":268747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=268719#post268719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So every character gets a choice between long-term character growth on the one hand or a supernatural power of some sort on the other? That has some intriguing implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correction, sir: each <i>player</i> gets a choice. A Promethean who gets input on choosing their Bestowment would be a rare beast indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T02:54:30-07:00","id":268888,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I must admit, I'm suspicious of any power that acts as a &quot;Beat generator&quot;. Still, I'd love to see more.<br /> <br /> Aren't Beats supposed to compensate you for roleplaying when it would hurt your character? Are these &quot;powers&quot; actually handicaps?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps they generate beneficial Conditions in certain circumstances, all encouraging you to follow Lineage stereotypes ... hmm. That makes the most sense, although I wouldn't have phrased it that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=268159#post268159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I ran <b>Promethean</b> before, Franks got 9-again on every Strength roll, including combat. Shockingly, this did not break the game, because as I keep saying, &quot;game balance&quot; is a myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed ... a cynic might suggest that if bonuses to Strength were more powerful than other Attributes - because they benefit combat rolls - then everyone would <i>already</i> be buying up Strength to their Attribute maximum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T04:10:38-07:00","id":268953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=268719#post268719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So every character gets a choice between long-term character growth on the one hand or a supernatural power of some sort on the other? That has some intriguing implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fits nicely with the whole &quot;supernatural powers are distractions that don't really get you any closer to humanity&quot; thing Promethean has going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T04:22:08-07:00","id":268955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=268714#post268714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two things leap to mind:<br /> <br /> 1) Are other Bestowments still able to be purchased later on?<br /> 2) Does this mean the Unfleshed now have &quot;standardized&quot; Bestowments (and Disquiet, Torment, etc)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) Nope. You get what you get and you don't get upset. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 2) Yes. Their humour is oil. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=268888#post268888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I must admit, I'm suspicious of any power that acts as a &quot;Beat generator&quot;. Still, I'd love to see more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for the most part, they allow the player to get exceptional successes more easily, which allows the player to place Conditions, which allows the player to get Beats. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T04:43:59-07:00","id":268957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=268955#post268955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(About Unfleshed)<br /> 2) Yes. Their humour is oil.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what about robots based on other technologies than oil ( like superconductors and electricity )? They got changed their interiors after Generative Act, so oil become new electricity to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T11:01:18-07:00","id":269270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=268957#post268957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what about robots based on other technologies than oil ( like superconductors and electricity )? They got changed their interiors after Generative Act, so oil become new electricity to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine their electricity became Azoth, Pyros, and vaguely electricity-related Transmutations (like an Intelligence-boosting power to represent a built-in supercomputer.)<br /> <br /> Oil would be found throughout the body, greasing the moving parts and so on. It isn't a bodily fluid found in <i>humans</i>, but it's suited to their un-fleshed state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T13:14:28-07:00","id":269407,"title":"","content":"Here's a question. The New Dawn, becoming human, I understand it's still the &quot;end state&quot; for Promethean (e.g. No becoming a tree, or 4th dimensional entity), but is it the explicit goal <b>in character</b>? That is to say, do all Prometheans rise with the desire to be human? The knowledge that it's possible? Or is it a possibility they may (or may not) uncover along their journey?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 09-30-2014, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T13:23:34-07:00","id":269415,"title":"","content":"Really when I think of Promethean and when I played, YMMV and every character is different, but my own was on a quest for the endless torment of their existance to stop. There was the hope that they could one day be like everyone else, rather than end it all, which is never an escape as someone could just use their body to make a new Promethean once more. It to me is a story of hope... The Prometheans are a hardy bunch and they do not give in easily to despair... Though they occasionally fall to Torment, eventually they get it out of their systems, take a deep breath so to speak and push on... I find that incredibly admirable and whilst it can seem a depressing game, a Promethean can make choices which make the possibility of a New Dawn a reality for them... Whether a Promethean decides to make some unsavoury choices to gain that grey-tinged rather than black or white morality we call humanity or go another way and stay as they are to find a different way out, that for me makes the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T16:27:55-07:00","id":269591,"title":"","content":"Something I think this new edition needs to focus on is allowing Promethean characters to be <b>proactive</b> rather than just <b>reactive</b>. In 1e, you ramble into town like Bruce Banner and things start happening to you -- maybe you get attacked from Pandorans, maybe your Disfigurements flair and Disquiet kicks in early. But why did you go to the town in the first place? In the book, some ideas include &quot;looking for a job&quot;, &quot;trying to blend in with humanity&quot;, or &quot;drawn by Azoth&quot;, but those are very passive compared to Vampire's &quot;scouting for new blood&quot;, Werewolf's &quot;hunting a spirit&quot;, or Mage's &quot;we're following the leyline to a source of incredible power&quot;. When you try to make long term plans, like maybe running for local office, building a house, or even constructing another Promethean, the game punishes you with the Pandoran/Disquiet/Wasteland Triumvirate and you have to deal with that instead.<br /> <br /> Even the Milestones, which are supposed to guide a Promethean, are totally unknown to the player and -- more importantly -- the character. Which means characters are sometimes going to stumble through the game and miss <i>all of them</i>. There's even a section of the book accounting for this.<br /> <br /> I understand that &quot;getting in the way of stated goals&quot; is essentially the conflict in any story, but that's not what I'm talking about here. What it boils down to is that most of the content presented in 1e makes &quot;languishing under their Pilgrimage&quot; the inciting incident of most stories, and it paints Prometheans as perpetual victims who are only trying to make their way in this crazy world. &quot;Following their heart&quot; is just not enough for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T18:25:05-07:00","id":269691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=269407#post269407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question. The New Dawn, becoming human, I understand it's still the &quot;end state&quot; for Promethean (e.g. No becoming a tree, or 4th dimensional entity), but is it the explicit goal <b>in character</b>? That is to say, do all Prometheans rise with the desire to be human? The knowledge that it's possible? Or is it a possibility they may (or may not) uncover along their journey?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strange Alchemies, p104, &quot;But A Man Nonetheless&quot; - &quot;Playing the Difference&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 <b>When did the Promethean first learn about the Pilgrimage? </b>Some Prometheans hear about the Great Work from the moment they are able to understand the concept, or even before. Others hear about it only as they are about to undertake their independence from their creators. Still others only hear their creator talk of it occasionally, or to other people, and they are never given any context for what it means. Some hear absolutely nothing about the Pilgrimage from their creators, and have to discover its existence from other Prometheans. The circumstances under which the Promethean hears of it, and from whom he hears it, can set the tone for his Pilgrimage. Those who hear of it from a cruel creator may walk it with hesitation, while others may consider the Pilgrimage the thing that took their beloved creators from them.<br /> <br /> Other Prometheans simply find themselves on the Pilgrimage. For some, they\u2019ve somehow always known that their goal was to be come human; it simply took someone else putting it into words for them. Others seek to be near humans, to emulate them, but do not understand why they do these things. The Pilgrimage is an innate part of the Promethean existence \u2014 the Divine Fire is transformative, and rare is the Promethean who is simply content as he is. Prometheans are all driven by the desire for change, to become something else, and most of them find their role models in humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">characterlimit</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T05:34:48-07:00","id":270081,"title":"","content":"Something less related to the content of the game, and more to its look: keep the picture on page 23 of the first edition; it's bloody perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T21:02:33-07:00","id":270575,"title":"","content":"One thing we added is Azothic Memory. Prometheans are &quot;born&quot; with some spotty understanding of the Pilgrimage, the universal milestones, and the drive to complete the Great Work. <br /> <br /> Well, most of them. Maybe not the Extempore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T00:30:44-07:00","id":270653,"title":"","content":"I'd like it if the Extempore had Azothic Memory too.<br /> <br /> Someone who fails their Pilgramage is a tragic story, rich in drama and emotion. Someone who never had a chance isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T05:48:13-07:00","id":270742,"title":"","content":"On the contrary: someone who never had a chance is <i>extremely</i> tragic. And fighting on against fate can be rich in drama and emotion. <br /> <br /> But more to the point, Azothic Memory doesn\u2019t strike me as the sort of thing that if you don\u2019t have it, you can\u2019t complete the Pilgrimage; that is, not having it makes it less likely that you\u2019ll pursue the Pilgrimage, but it doesn\u2019t make anything concerning the Pilgrimage <i>impossible</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T06:02:20-07:00","id":270754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=270575#post270575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing we added is Azothic Memory. Prometheans are &quot;born&quot; with some spotty understanding of the Pilgrimage, the universal milestones, and the drive to complete the Great Work.<br /> <br /> Well, most of them. Maybe not the Extempore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every time you post here I get all giddy and SQUEE! This is an interesting decision - sorta allowing the PCs to know that their goal is to become human and let them understand that they're one of the Created but without the need for their creator or peers to explain it to them. Now you could really run something like Day 1 of their existence without them totally being in the dark. <b>Promethean</b> is a nice game to allow that, though I guess few other lines do have room for that.<br /> <br /> It's a good choice, too, since the Pilgrimage sounds like it'll be much more...not 'enforced' but...much more presented, I guess? Prometheans are defined by being non-human, whether they choose to accept the Pilgrimage or not, and if they do then how do they go about it. So it's a nice reinforcement for something so important. I'm excited.<br /> <br /> I didn't want to drag my girlfriend through a <b>Mummy</b> game only to be followed by a <b>Promethean</b> campaign, because it'd be nice to give her the chance to play as something that was human within the last millennium, but...she might not have a choice, at this rate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T07:28:29-07:00","id":270801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=269591#post269591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the Milestones, which are supposed to guide a Promethean, are totally unknown to the player and -- more importantly -- the character. Which means characters are sometimes going to stumble through the game and miss <i>all of them</i>. There's even a section of the book accounting for this.<br /> <br /> I understand that &quot;getting in the way of stated goals&quot; is essentially the conflict in any story, but that's not what I'm talking about here. What it boils down to is that most of the content presented in 1e makes &quot;languishing under their Pilgrimage&quot; the inciting incident of most stories, and it paints Prometheans as perpetual victims who are only trying to make their way in this crazy world. &quot;Following their heart&quot; is just not enough for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, it would <b>really</b> make more sense if Milestones functioned like Aspirations. Both in terms of the adolescence metaphor and from a mechanical perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T11:17:08-07:00","id":270964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=270742#post270742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the contrary: someone who never had a chance is <i>extremely</i> tragic. And fighting on against fate can be rich in drama and emotion.</div> </div> </div> </div> Tragic yes. But unless that fight against fate has a chance to go either way it lacks drama and the emotional impact is lessened by certainty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=270742#post270742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But more to the point, Azothic Memory doesn\u2019t strike me as the sort of thing that if you don\u2019t have it, you can\u2019t complete the Pilgrimage; that is, not having it makes it less likely that you\u2019ll pursue the Pilgrimage, but it doesn\u2019t make anything concerning the Pilgrimage <i>impossible</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fair point. In retrospect my post was as much a reaction to the Extempore in 1e who could not ever achieve the new dawn as it was to Matt's post.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T12:48:12-07:00","id":271031,"title":"","content":"Journey, not destination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T14:03:04-07:00","id":271089,"title":"","content":"&quot;Universal milestones&quot; is an interesting and important addition. That there are more constants means that the Pilgrimage is less a blind fumble, and gives more grounding to the Refinements, in that there are actual things that they can achieve with some reliability, rather than &quot;just&quot; being philosophical practices. <br /> <br /> The actual existence of Azothic Memory I can take or leave. I think 1e laid out a strong enough arc that adding a new Azothic Memory isn't adding much of anything that wasn't there already. A &quot;Running Monkey&quot; period for the Created is a perfect segment for exploring humanity through a neutral lens. Assuming a Disquiet/Wasteland framework as crushing as currently, of course. And the presence or absence of a Promethean creator in this time is much more poignant if no such Memory drives the newly Created.<br /> <br /> Azothic Memory does step on notions of free will, <i>if </i>it provides reliable guidance to a &quot;correct&quot; path on the Pilgrimage. The drives humans experience keep them alive, but listening to them alone tends to fuck up any higher calling. While Prometheans are given over to a supernatural god-flame, this divinity is bugnuts consumed with a fizzy, frothing reality where nothing remains solid for long, and a predictable Pilgrimage isn't what I'd imagine it has prepared for player characters.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'd like to hear more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T14:21:20-07:00","id":271112,"title":"","content":"What Arcane said. Also, the choice isn\u2019t between \u201cthere is always a way to complete te Pilgrimage\u201d and \u201cthere is never a way to complete it\u201d. 1e\u2019s sample Extempore faced a rather nasty dilemma that he needed to create a progeny before he could Redeem, but had no way of knowing how to do so. One <i>could</i> take that as \u201che\u2019s in an impossible predicament, and doomed to failure\u201d; or you could take it as \u201che hasn\u2019t been sufficiently creative and/or desperate to find a way out of his catch-22 yet\u201d. After all, <b>Promethean</b> specializes in doing the impossible. <br /> <hr /><br /> I\u2019m wondering if \u201cyou must create progeny in order to complete the Pilgrimage\u201d is still going to be a thing in 2e. If the primary reason for having it in there was to encourage the continuation of the species, 2e\u2019s greater emphasis on demiurges largely undermines said rationale. <br /> <br /> Also, to what extent will 2e\u2019s Extempore be \u201ccreated by accident\u201d, and to what extent will they be \u201cthe catch-all category for any Promethean who doesn\u2019t fit any of the regular Lineages\u201d? That is, could a demiurge create an Extempore? <br /> <br /> On demiurges: will there be rules for mortals performing the generative act, or will that be left in the realm of \u201cit works when the Storyteller says it works\u201d? If the former, will Prometheans be able to partake of the demiurge rules, allowing (say) a Frankenstein to create a Galeteid (with the creation of another Frankenstein merely being the easier option)? <br /> <br /> The Unfleshed: I can get behind \u201coil\u201d as their Humour: any machine that has moving parts needs some sort of lubricant to keep those parts moving smoothly. Even human joints have synovial fluid which serves as a lubricant. And I\u2019m guessing that the Unfleshed Element is Metal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T06:28:40-07:00","id":271578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=271112#post271112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unfleshed: I can get behind \u201coil\u201d as their Humour: any machine that has moving parts needs some sort of lubricant to keep those parts moving smoothly. Even human joints have synovial fluid which serves as a lubricant. And I\u2019m guessing that the Unfleshed Element is Metal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Renaissance alchemy did include metal (well, mercury specifically) as an element, although it wasn't quite the same phenomenon as the big four - earlier alchemists also held metals to be good balances of the big four (gold as the perfect one of course) - so metal as the Unfleshed's element fits well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T14:47:17-07:00","id":275004,"title":"","content":"Here's another want: mo'better terminology!<br /> <br /> Nothing against Disfigurements, but they're the reality underneath a human illusion which lacks a name. Why not Facade, or Veneer, or Smokescreen? As the most human thing about them, you have to figure the Created would have a word for their face in the world.<br /> <br /> More words for the Created. Misbegotten, Made Men, Abominations, Strangers. Whatever it takes so there's more go-to terms when talking about them than Promethean and Created, both of which fluster my spellchecker and my smartphone soft keyboard (where I do most of my browsing).<br /> <br /> Terms for the parent and progeny of the Generative Act. Pater/Mater, Offspring, whatever. Something a little less hierarchical than Sire/Childe.<br /> <br /> Fewer silly phrases like Suffocating Rise of Torment and Wasting of the Peaceful Refuge. Torment and Wasteland are fine, but for a scattered and vestigial society such as the Rabble (my own phrase for the entirety of Promethean society), even those are a little too pat in their universality.<br /> <br /> I tend to think of The Walking Dead, how every group has it's own phrase for the zombies: walkers, lamebrains, biters, and so forth. A unified vocabulary is next to impossible for 1k-5k spread across the globe to maintain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T15:19:28-07:00","id":275016,"title":"","content":"I love the thought of 'Veneer' being the name of the human cover that hides the Disfigurements... It brings to me thoughts of a clay pot from a furnace being lacquered or varnished or whatever after its out. Its not so alchemical in nature, but links somewhat to the brewing and furnace properties elsewhere. I suppose 'plating' like as in 'silver plate' etc could be good... Veneer is pretty damn boss though for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T17:30:40-07:00","id":280282,"title":"","content":"New blog post is up asking for votes! This time we're choosing between Refinements... and ALCHEMISTS. <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sewing-parts-together-playtests-begin/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/sewing-parts-...aytests-begin/</a><br /> <br /> I think you can guess which one I threw in for!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T20:22:08-07:00","id":280469,"title":"","content":"Vote Refinements! I want to learn about Phosphorum!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T20:48:43-07:00","id":280507,"title":"","content":"I really do not understand you people's fascination with alchemists. I voted for Refinements and fully 'spect to lose this round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T21:27:27-07:00","id":280554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=280507#post280507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really do not understand you people's fascination with alchemists. I voted for Refinements and fully 'spect to lose this round.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's because people sometimes misunderstand 'updated older thing' to mean 'will have less new/interesting material than a totally new thing.' I'm curious to learn more about what Alchemists' deal is as well but I can't help but think that a Refinements preview might give us more of a glimpse at the bigger picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T21:30:19-07:00","id":280555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=280507#post280507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really do not understand you people's fascination with alchemists. I voted for Refinements and fully 'spect to lose this round.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, \u201creanimated corpses\u201d doesn\u2019t interest me all that much in and of itself. But \u201ccreations animated by alchemical principles, pursuing an alchemy-inspired Magnum Opus\u201d? That\u2019s a different matter entirely. That\u2019s why I have no problem with constructs playing a larger role in the game, <i>and</i> why alchemists interest me so much: to me, the alchemy is the primary draw of the game, and the Prometheans are merely a way of expressing it. Adding <i>more</i> ways that alchemical concepts can be expressed is a good thing as I see it. <br /> <br /> Put another way: alchemy is to <b>Promethean</b> as animism is to <b>Werewolf</b> and techgnosis is to <b>Demon</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T22:57:35-07:00","id":280632,"title":"","content":"Refinements. The alchemy is, as it always has been, a metaphor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T00:15:14-07:00","id":280661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=280632#post280632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Refinements. The alchemy is, as it always has been, a metaphor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmm... no. It's not a metaphor. Alchemy has always been about personal transformation. The fact that Promethean's bodies are their alchemical laboratories, instead of external test-tubes and such doesn't make it not literally alchemy that animates them and facilitates their transformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T00:27:27-07:00","id":280666,"title":"","content":"Alchemists all the way! I want to know when I can become Full Metal one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously, Refinements were 9 of 10 mostly the same as in 1ed. Alchemist were not correctly shown in 1ed corebook ( I didn't seen them at least ). Refinements spoiler would have sens if it will be like <b>DaveB</b> one for Orders - you got whole first Order write-up. And then next one. And next one. Just too see real differences in each of them from 1ed to 2ed.<br /> <br /> As I now see, <b>Matt</b> is more reclusive from this tactic, so more logical is to see on &quot;possible Demiurges, and mostly antagonists&quot; mortals of Prometheans just to see &quot;new&quot; thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And as Refinements are critical to the new edition, even if they aren't chosen now, they <b>will </b>show up later. So Alchemists spoiler is more tactical choice.<span style=\"font-size:10px\"> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-14-2014, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T02:56:05-07:00","id":280764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=280555#post280555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, \u201creanimated corpses\u201d doesn\u2019t interest me all that much in and of itself. But \u201ccreations animated by alchemical principles, pursuing an alchemy-inspired Magnum Opus\u201d? That\u2019s a different matter entirely. That\u2019s why I have no problem with constructs playing a larger role in the game, <i>and</i> why alchemists interest me so much: to me, the alchemy is the primary draw of the game, and the Prometheans are merely a way of expressing it. Adding <i>more</i> ways that alchemical concepts can be expressed is a good thing as I see it.<br /> <br /> Put another way: alchemy is to <b>Promethean</b> as animism is to <b>Werewolf</b> and techgnosis is to <b>Demon</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, of course, that the end goal of alchemy was <i>immortality</i>.<br /> <br /> It was effectively transhumanist, and thus entirely counter to the direction of the Pilgrimage, which posits humanity's natural state as the pinnacle of achievement. (This is probably why they're antagonists.)<br /> <br /> Voting for alchemists, because alchemists are awesome. Still, hard choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:31:50-07:00","id":281034,"title":"","content":"My perspective is largely I'm more interested in the main characters than the antagonists.<br /> <br /> In fact, the general hierarchy is main characters, setting, antagonists.<br /> <br /> By and large because my favorite type of villains are actually foils and dark mirrors, so the more I know about the main characters the more I know about my villains anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:41:11-07:00","id":281043,"title":"","content":"The number of people who want to play an alchemist over a Promethean is small in number, but it's already annoying me.<br /> <br /> I'm surprisingly sensitive on this subject.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It occurs to me I feel the same way about alchemists that Data feels about reanimated corpses.<br /> <br /> It's really the synergy that's awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-14-2014, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T15:13:59-07:00","id":281511,"title":"","content":"In hindsight, I'm boggled how the game didn't have such an obvious antagonist. The whole premise is that these supernatural creatures are vying to become human; it's only logical that a <i>great</i> antagonist is a human vying to become a supernatural creature.<br /> <br /> I'm glad this got spoiled a bit early - my curiosity sated, now we can go on with the basics like Refinements and Integrity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T15:41:05-07:00","id":281536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=281043#post281043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me I feel the same way about alchemists that Data feels about reanimated corpses.<br /> <br /> It's really the synergy that's awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. And to clarify, I don't <i>dislike</i> reanimated corpses; they're a fascinating way to express the principles of alchemy. And as you say, the synergy is awesome. I simply don't want them to be the <i>only</i> way that <b>Promethean</b> supports. Alchemists as a dark reflection of Prometheans is another fascinating option. <br /> <br /> I'm in favor of more options; it's why I <i>also</i> favor the notion of Promethean-like creations that <i>don't</i> have so much in the way of alchemical overtones: &quot;automata&quot; who are to Prometheans as Revenants are to Kindred in <b>Requiem 2e</b>; who are more akin to the Imbued from <b>World of Darkness: Antagonists</b> than to the Pilgrimage-walking Prometheans and who represent what Prometheans would be like if they <i>didn't</i> have the Pilgrimage. They'd provide a different kind of contrast: reanimated corpses sans alchemy<sup>*</sup> rather than alchemy sans reanimated corpses (i.e., alchemists). <br /> <br /> <hr />* Well, not <i>completely</i> &quot;sans alchemy&quot;; they wouldn't be reanimated if the alchemy was absent entirely. But the idea is that they'd have the minimum needed to be animated and no more than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T17:02:18-07:00","id":281644,"title":"","content":"That is an interesting idea, but they would still probably be portrayed as antagonists rather than 'darkly' protagonists. It's the Promethean's nature to be alone (with each other)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T17:29:52-07:00","id":281689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=280661#post280661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mmmm... no. It's not a metaphor. Alchemy has always been about personal transformation. The fact that Promethean's bodies are their alchemical laboratories, instead of external test-tubes and such doesn't make it not literally alchemy that animates them and facilitates their transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemy has always been a metaphor for personal transformation, at least among its serious practitioners. They may ascribe reality to it, but it's still a way to translate abstract ideas about change and process into more communicable means. I'm not saying it's a metaphor <i>within the setting </i>(save where the masses no longer give it any credence), but alchemy in Promethean is still a metaphor to its audience. Alchemists are just another manifestation, realization thereof, and pretty dull in comparison to the Refinements.<br /> <br /> Feel sort of robbed at that too, having read today's blog post. Basically boils down to &quot;yes, there are alchemists in a magical setting, they're exactly what you expected.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T19:29:53-07:00","id":281826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=281644#post281644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is an interesting idea, but they would still probably be portrayed as antagonists rather than 'darkly' protagonists. It's the Promethean's nature to be alone (with each other)</div> </div> </div> </div>As I envision them, they certainly wouldn\u2019t be playable characters: they\u2019d be things that <i>Prometheans</i> would pity, because at least a Promethean has hope (in the form of the Pilgrimage). The only hope <i>they\u2019d</i> have would be to become a Promethean. Their role n the game? Not all that different from clones in 1e, sans the \u201clooks like someone else\u201d stuff: minions and cannon fodder for other antagonists (such as alchemists). <br /> <br /> Put another way: if humans represent the Gold at the end of the Pilgrimage, these drones/automata would represent the Lead at the <i>start</i> of the Pilgrimage: they\u2019d be the baseline condition that Prometheans started out from, but without the ability to progress. And for those who don\u2019t like mortals ever being able to make Prometheans without desperation or an equivalent insanity, the fact that they\u2019d be, at best, <i>proto-</i>Prometheans ought to exempt them from such requirements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T07:23:32-07:00","id":282272,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see an Integrity for Prometheans that works backwards because it measures their inhumanity. They start off at 7 because they're pretty artificial. So Integrity 0 would be human, having achieved the New Dawn, with Integrity 1 the best you can get for your New Dawn roll. That's because your Integrity stat adds to the roll because 'the universe' is rolling the New Dawn pool against you.<br /> <br /> So, with whatever other factors to modify the roll, an Integrity 1 Promethean has one die rolled against them and an Integrity 10 Promethean would have ten","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T15:10:01-07:00","id":282764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These are humans who are so terrified of death, infirmity, and ignorance that they have lost sight of love, fellowship and the value of mundane accomplishment. Bit by bit, they sacrifice their humanity for power and knowledge, until they have turned themselves into something monstrous.<br /> <br /> Where the Created seek to transcend their monstrous condition, leaving behind their power, longevity, and superlative durability in favor of the simple pleasures of humanity, alchemists want to leave their humanity behind in the hopes of becoming something more than human. More frequently, they end up becoming something much less than human. </div> </div> </div>This seems ... a tad anti-transhumanist. In the &quot;transhumanism is inherently wrong&quot; sense.<br /> <br /> I *really* hope they gets toned down and made more sympathetic in the final draft, because Promethean has enough trouble as it is convincing players that the Pilgrimage is a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T15:41:14-07:00","id":282801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=282764#post282764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems ... a tad anti-transhumanist. In the &quot;transhumanism is inherently wrong&quot; sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reading seems to have fundamentally forgotten both the core themes of Promethean and the established effects of prolonged exposure to the Fire on mortal beings.<br /> <br /> &quot;You didn't want to eventually die so you <i>kidnapped and vivisected an unwilling sapient</i>&quot; doesn't get to play the sympathy card. End of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T16:29:48-07:00","id":282917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=282764#post282764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems ... a tad anti-transhumanist. In the &quot;transhumanism is inherently wrong&quot; sense.<br /> <br /> I *really* hope they gets toned down and made more sympathetic in the final draft, because Promethean has enough trouble as it is convincing players that the Pilgrimage is a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it was Dave Brookshaw speaking of Mage and not Matt McFarland speaking of Promethean, I feel like the following is beginning to largely be true of the entire World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game is explicitly anti-transhumanist, in that it's always shown to cost more than it's worth; sorry if that upsets you, but we're making a horror game here.</div> </div> </div> </div>In particular, Promethean, while not expressly anti-transhumanist, has always been very humanist, which causes it to run in different directions. It's both the result of it's themes and it's genre. Sorry if that's a problem, but they're making a horror game here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-15-2014, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T22:33:37-07:00","id":283400,"title":"","content":"I'd go as far as to say that the entire nWoD *is* basically anti-transhumanist, and has always been so. It goes back to something Justin Achilli said a fairly long time ago, about one of the core principles of the nWoD being the fact that the setting considers humanity to actually mean something precious.<br /> <br /> Just the way I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 10-16-2014, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T23:50:17-07:00","id":283540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=282801#post282801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This reading seems to have fundamentally forgotten both the core themes of Promethean and the established effects of prolonged exposure to the Fire on mortal beings.<br /> <br /> &quot;You didn't want to eventually die so you <i>kidnapped and vivisected an unwilling sapient</i>&quot; doesn't get to play the sympathy card. End of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree this is direct result of setting assumptions. But still, I could see some favorable alchemist for Promethean, just like Hunters can sometimes help the monsters goals. I count in corebook for statement like &quot;Most alchemists are hunting for Promethean. Those few that would benevolent, sooner or later will turn on them.&quot; More &quot;Disquiet leads mortals to conflict, less &quot;all transhumanists are looking for your organs&quot;.<br /> <br /> And stating every time &quot;transhumanism is bad&quot; is making bad impressions for games in large portion of some it's possible fandom. Yes, we make here horror game - but not all transhumanism is horror. Just like not all facing ones fears is \u2013 like in psychotherapy. It's sometimes good thing to show what normally lead to horror in setting in other light.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T15:17:11-07:00","id":285456,"title":"","content":"Promethean is - <i>has always been</i> - a game for telling stories about self-improvement. The flawed imitation, pulling itself upwards.<br /> <br /> If the new edition is going to be about self-denial, about cutting off your potential in order to be &quot;normal&quot; ... then I don't think that's a game I want to play.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=283400#post283400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go as far as to say that the entire nWoD *is* basically anti-transhumanist, and has always been so. It goes back to something Justin Achilli said a fairly long time ago, about one of the core principles of the nWoD being the fact that the setting considers humanity to actually mean something precious.<br /> <br /> Just the way I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=282917#post282917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it was Dave Brookshaw speaking of Mage and not Matt McFarland speaking of Promethean, I feel like the following is beginning to largely be true of the entire World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> In particular, Promethean, while not expressly anti-transhumanist, has always been very humanist, which causes it to run in different directions. It's both the result of it's themes and it's genre. Sorry if that's a problem, but they're making a horror game here.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your &quot;horror&quot; story isn't finding horror in <i>humanity,</i> even by metaphor, then I'm not sure I'm interested.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'm not sure it's &quot;horror&quot; in any meaningful sense. It's fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 10-17-2014, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T16:23:39-07:00","id":285486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=285456#post285456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean is - <i>has always been</i> - a game for telling stories about self-improvement. The flawed imitation, pulling itself upwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixing the flaws in your soul that cause the world entire to despise you is digging yourself out of a hole. This is a markedly different thing from shoving these busted almost-people into the dirt so you don't have to outrun the bear.<br /> <br /> Prometheans are looking for self-worth and a place of their own, not apotheosis. Healing a broken hand is not comparable to chopping off a healthy one to graft on one made of an indestructible miracle-alloy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the new edition is going to be about self-denial, about cutting off your potential in order to be &quot;normal&quot; ... then I don't think that's a game I want to play. </div> </div> </div>Tell your false equivalency good riddance from me.<br /> <br /> The alchemists that are going to function as antagonists are the ones who think the trade of &quot;the beautiful parts of the human condition&quot; for &quot;not being ignorant, infirm, or mortal&quot; is a worthwhile one. That is not the sum total of alchemists in Promethean, but it does constitute the ones who receive a focus as antagonists, because the behavior typical of those sorts of characters is pitiful at best and directly antithetical to the pursuit of a whole soul besides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T19:55:17-07:00","id":285636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=285456#post285456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your &quot;horror&quot; story isn't finding horror in <i>humanity,</i> even by metaphor, then I'm not sure I'm interested.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'm not sure it's &quot;horror&quot; in any meaningful sense. It's fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will find horror wherever I decide to look.<br /> <br /> Horror is flexible like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-18-2014, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T21:29:46-07:00","id":285686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=285456#post285456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean is - <i>has always been</i> - a game for telling stories about self-improvement. The flawed imitation, pulling itself upwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. And part of its premise is that humans are a step up from Prometheans, despite all the powers the latter have. Feel free to disagree with the premise; but that <i>is</i> the premise; and hopefully 2e will do a better job at explaining just why being a Promethean <i>sucks</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=285456#post285456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the new edition is going to be about self-denial, about cutting off your potential in order to be &quot;normal&quot; ... then I don't think that's a game I want to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then with all due respect, don\u2019t play it. Or change it to be more to your liking, and play <i>that</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=285456#post285456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your &amp;quot;horror&amp;quot; story isn't finding horror in <i>humanity,</i> even by metaphor, then I'm not sure I'm interested.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outcasts shunned by society, children from disfunctional families\u2026 yeah, there\u2019s no metaphoric horror <i>there\u2026</i> :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T21:38:44-07:00","id":285689,"title":"","content":"May I take a second to say that this argument that MugASofer brings up is rather like a Promethean itself-It just keeps coming back up ever since it started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T07:28:26-07:00","id":285885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=285486#post285486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fixing the flaws in your soul that cause the world entire to despise you is digging yourself out of a hole. This is a markedly different thing from shoving these busted almost-people into the dirt so you don't have to outrun the bear.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm ... not sure what you think my perspective is. Could you expand on this?<br /> <br /> I'm not in favor of killing Prometheans. I'm against<i> mocking</i> people for being afraid of bears.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=285686#post285686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. And part of its premise is that humans are a step up from Prometheans, despite all the powers the latter have. Feel free to disagree with the premise; but that <i>is</i> the premise; and hopefully 2e will do a better job at explaining just why being a Promethean <i>sucks</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The point is that being human <i>is</i> better - not that being a <i>Promethean</i> is better, but hey, who wants superpowers anyway?<br /> <br /> That's something the game has always struggled to get across, and I'm really worried about the idea that it might be lost in 2nd ed. (Hopefully that paragraph will be changed, and that'll be the end of it, and the new edition will be awesome and solve all these problems forever.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 10-18-2014, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T07:33:32-07:00","id":285888,"title":"","content":"I don't really have anything against Promethean as an Anti-Transhumanist game myself, even if I normally really like transhumanism in stories, probably because what really attracts me to transhumanism is the <i>transcendence</i> aspect of it. And Promethean has plenty of that.<br /> <br /> But...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=285686#post285686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outcasts shunned by society, children from disfunctional families\u2026 yeah, there\u2019s no metaphoric horror <i>there\u2026</i> :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really think that you want to imply that the only response to being shunned by society (which can happen entirely out of society's faults) or coming from a dysfunctional family (which in no way is you fault) is to stop being what you are to fit in. Really, I think it's a terrible message and I'm really glad Promethean isn't about that.<br /> <br /> So please think of a better example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/326-ravraxas","name":"Ravraxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T09:10:44-07:00","id":285962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=285885#post285885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm ... not sure what you think my perspective is. Could you expand on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't care for repeating myself and I'm given to understand that vocally expecting people to display reading comprehension is gauche, but:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The alchemists that are going to function as antagonists are the ones who think the trade of &quot;the beautiful parts of the human condition&quot; for &quot;not being ignorant, infirm, or mortal&quot; is a worthwhile one. That is not the sum total of alchemists in Promethean, but it does constitute the ones who receive a focus as antagonists, because the behavior typical of those sorts of characters is pitiful at best and directly antithetical to the pursuit of a whole soul besides.</span> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=285885#post285885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not in favor of killing Prometheans. I'm against<i> mocking</i> people for being afraid of bears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you can take your false equivalence and shove it all the way to the Subterranean Sun. The condemnation is &quot;You did <i>what</i> to get away from the bear?!&quot; not &quot;Haha, look at the wimp who's terrified of the terrifying thing.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T14:37:07-07:00","id":286182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=285962#post285962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The condemnation is &quot;You did <i>what</i> to get away from the bear?!&quot; not &quot;Haha, look at the wimp who's terrified of the terrifying thing.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm <i>definitely</i> favor of that. My ideal Alchemist character would be a Mister Freeze type - tragic motivations, awesome powers, awful methods.<br /> <br /> But:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These are humans who are so terrified of death, infirmity, and ignorance that they have lost sight of love, fellowship and the value of mundane accomplishment. Bit by bit, they sacrifice their humanity for power and knowledge, until they have turned themselves into something monstrous.<br /> <br /> Where the Created seek to transcend their monstrous condition, leaving behind their power, longevity, and superlative durability in favor of the simple pleasures of humanity, alchemists want to leave their humanity behind in the hopes of becoming something more than human. </div> </div> </div>... this implies two things:<ul><li>Their problem is that they consider death etc to be <i>too bad</i>. They should be less afraid of death.</li> <li>A &quot;monstrous condition&quot; - like that of the Created - is characterized by &quot;power, longevity, and superlative durability&quot;. These are things all good people would leave behind, trading them for &quot;simple pleasures&quot;.</li> </ul>In sort, it implies that the tradeoff is a Good Thing for a Bad Thing - like sacrificing a baby to summon a world-destroying demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 10-18-2014, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T15:20:45-07:00","id":286205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=286182#post286182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm <i>definitely</i> favor of that. My ideal Alchemist character would be a Mister Freeze type - tragic motivations, awesome powers, awful methods. [\u2026]<br /> In sort, it implies that the tradeoff is a Good Thing for a Bad Thing - like sacrificing a baby to summon a world-destroying demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you should mention Victor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BTAS, &quot;Deep Freeze,&quot; S3E10</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Walker:</b><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">You're practically immortal, my friend.</span></span><br /> <b>Mr. Freeze:</b><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Yes, eternal life trapped in this wretched shell. What a miserable joke.</span></span><br /> <b>Walker:</b><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Oh, miserable to you, but a godsend to me. Look at me, Mr. Freeze, I'm an old man. I've created wonders in my lifetime, but there is still so much to do! I want to change as you have, to become like you\u2014a being of blessed, eternal cold!</span></span><br /> <b>Mr. Freeze:</b><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> You're insane.</span></span><br /> <b>Walker:</b><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Only you have the know-how to duplicate the accident that made you what you are, what I long to become!</span></span><br /> <b>Mr. Freeze:</b><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> You want to live like this? Abandoned and alone? A prisoner in a world you can see, but never touch? Old and infirm as you are, I'd trade a thousand of my frozen years for your worst day.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The reviewer for </span></span><i>World's Finest Online</i><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">, in covering &quot;Deep Freeze&quot;, noted that Walker and Freeze stood in deliberate contrast to each other. Freeze claims to be dead to emotions, but his compassion betrays him several times during the episode: he initially refuses to subject Walker to the same confinement as Freeze himself, and Batman eventually convinces him to help stop the deaths of innocent people. By contrast, Walker is an outwardly warm, paternalistic figure, but he is as dead to emotions as Freeze claims to be, coldly planning mass murder just to create his own fantasy of a perfect world. His transformation into &quot;the second Mr. Freeze&quot; is more appropriate to his inner self than Freeze's ever was.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T20:18:20-07:00","id":286338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravraxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=285888#post285888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really think that you want to imply that the only response to being shunned by society (which can happen entirely out of society's faults) or coming from a dysfunctional family (which in no way is you fault) is to stop being what you are to fit in. Really, I think it's a terrible message and I'm really glad Promethean isn't about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well\u2026 yes and no. <b>Promethean</b> starts with the notion that the protagonist is, well, not <i>broken</i> per se, as that would imply that there was a time when he was better than he is now; but certainly <i>incomplete</i>, a being who is missing something that everyone else has and the lack of which results in the world turning against him. As well, this fault that causes people to feel uneasy around him is not the result of anything he did; it\u2019s inherent in what he is. And as such, the only way he\u2019s going to get rid of that unease and have a shot at being accepted by society <i>is</i> to change what he is \u2014 or, put in somewhat less inflammatory terms, to \u201cgrow up\u201d. <br /> <br /> So yeah; if you want to, you <i>can</i> read <b>Promethean</b> as \u201csociety shuns you because of what you are, and you\u2019re only going to change that by changing yourself\u201d. And if you want to, you can generalize that from the specifics of the Promethean condition to a general declaration about conformity being good. I don\u2019t particularly want to, and I especially see the latter as an overgeneralization. <br /> <br /> But more to the point, I wasn\u2019t talking about what the moral of the Promethean story is; I was talking about where the human horror is; and the human horror is that it sucks to be the outsider, to never know love or acceptance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T20:27:05-07:00","id":286341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=286338#post286338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But more to the point, I wasn\u2019t talking about what the moral of the Promethean story is; I was talking about where the human horror is; and the human horror is that it sucks to be the outsider, to never know love or acceptance.</div> </div> </div> </div>This principle was one of the two hooks that made me invest in Promethean, and from there that revolutionized a lot of my life, as a person and as a craftsman, as well as making me the WoD fan I am today.<br /> <br /> The other was what Redemption truly meant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T20:59:16-07:00","id":286365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=286338#post286338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah; if you want to, you <i>can</i> read <b>Promethean</b> as \u201csociety shuns you because of what you are, and you\u2019re only going to change that by changing yourself\u201d. And if you want to, you can generalize that from the specifics of the Promethean condition to a general declaration about conformity being good. I don\u2019t particularly want to, and I especially see the latter as an overgeneralization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everybody forgets about Torment.<br /> <br /> I bring up pursuit of self-worth as an aspect of the Pilgrimage in no small part because my last reread of the line highlighted connections between the Promethean condition and those truisms about how people can smell self-loathing from a mile off, how the quality does not bring out the best in those around you for any length of time, and how getting out of a depression is something that requires conscious action on your part.<br /> <br /> Calling Promethean assimilationist, as some have apparently done in the past, ignores that there's an entire core Refinement dedicated to self-reflection and retreat from society, that this same philosophy works to minimize the impact of the one drawback of carrying the Fire that doesn't simply make people and nature reject you, that that very drawback is the one that is unambiguously a problem with your character's emotional locus of control, and that a large part of the Refinement's common practices involve seeing that everything changes, that nothing lasts forever, that everything acts on everything else and <i>changes</i>.<br /> <br /> Knowing that there are Created who think of themselves as &quot;not <i>completely</i> human <i>yet</i>&quot; makes it pretty clear that the Pilgrimage, once stripped of the trappings of artifice and vulcanism and thin veneers of normality, is very much a quest to be able to <i>feel</i> like a human being despite coming from an otherwise awful lot in life. That's part of why alchemy and the optimistic reading of the ending of Pandora's Box are so apropos - lead into gold, the New Dawn after the Saturnine Night, the power of the Transformative Will, Hope at the bottom of the box?<br /> <br /> Fairly high up on Promethean's list of messages is the notion that even if you're having a long terrible night and you feel more like a horrible good-for-nothing monster than a person with rights and feelings and worth, as long as you pick up the pieces, move forward, and keep on making steps, no matter how small the progress, however long it takes, <i>the sun will come out tomorrow and you will be there when it happens.</i><br /> <br /> <u>That</u> is Mortality: <i>this too shall pass.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T21:40:07-07:00","id":286375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=286365#post286365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everybody forgets about Torment.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=286365#post286365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bring up pursuit of self-worth as an aspect of the Pilgrimage in no small part because my last reread of the line highlighted connections between the Promethean condition and those truisms about how people can smell self-loathing from a mile off, how the quality does not bring out the best in those around you for any length of time, and how getting out of a depression is something that requires conscious action on your part.<br /> <br /> Calling Promethean assimilationist, as some have apparently done in the past, ignores that there's an entire core Refinement dedicated to self-reflection and retreat from society, that this same philosophy works to minimize the impact of the one drawback of carrying the Fire that doesn't simply make people and nature reject you, that that very drawback is the one that is unambiguously a problem with your character's emotional locus of control, and that a large part of the Refinement's common practices involve seeing that everything changes, that nothing lasts forever, that everything acts on everything else and <i>changes</i>.<br /> <br /> Knowing that there are Created who think of themselves as &amp;quot;not <i>completely</i> human <i>yet</i>&amp;quot; makes it pretty clear that the Pilgrimage, once stripped of the trappings of artifice and vulcanism and thin veneers of normality, is very much a quest to be able to <i>feel</i> like a human being despite coming from an otherwise awful lot in life. That's part of why alchemy and the optimistic reading of the ending of Pandora's Box are so apropos - lead into gold, the New Dawn after the Saturnine Night, the power of the Transformative Will, Hope at the bottom of the box?</div> </div> </div> </div>Put in more simplistic terms: in <b>Promethean</b>, there <i>is</i> something wrong with you; and whether they know why or not, others react to that. This is where the horror comes from. But the good news is, you can do something about it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=286365#post286365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fairly high up on Promethean's list of messages is the notion that even if you're having a long terrible night and you feel more like a horrible good-for-nothing monster than a person with rights and feelings and worth, as long as you pick up the pieces, move forward, and keep on making steps, no matter how small the progress, however long it takes, <i>the sun will come out tomorrow and you will be there when it happens.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>The sun will come up<br /> Tomorrow;<br /> betcha bottom dollar that tomorrow,<br /> there\u2019ll be sun\u2026</i></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=286365#post286365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>That</u> is Mortality: <i>this too shall pass.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Ironic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T06:57:17-07:00","id":286590,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see some social organizations of Prometheans. I was rereading Pandora's Box, and in the chronicle's chapter of New Orleans, there's some social philosophical groups of Prometheans, as the Motus Liber, Mercy's Mission or Both\u00e9rud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T12:18:22-07:00","id":286837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=286338#post286338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Promethean</b> starts with the notion that the protagonist is, well, not <i>broken</i> per se, as that would imply that there was a time when he was better than he is now; but certainly <i>incomplete</i>, a being who is missing something that everyone else has and the lack of which results in the world turning against him. As well, this fault that causes people to feel uneasy around him is not the result of anything he did; it\u2019s inherent in what he is. And as such, the only way he\u2019s going to get rid of that unease and have a shot at being accepted by society <i>is</i> to change what he is \u2014 or, put in somewhat less inflammatory terms, to \u201cgrow up\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have also felt that the &quot;incompleteness&quot; of a Promethean is vital to what motivates them, and maybe this is sort of what The Obsidian Haberdash-ed One speaks of when he brings up Azothic Memory. If they can feel that they are incomplete, that would spur them on the Pilgrimage for sure. And it is this very incompleteness that somehow makes them truly gifted in terms of alchemy, capable of unholy feats no man can accomplish. I hope this gets played up more in 2e.<br /> <br /> There's irony, too, in how a Promethean is absolutely, 100% the Magnum Opus of their Demiurge and yet still know they are in some way unfinished.<br /> <br /> I do appreciate the inherent tragedy of Promethean; none of them can help that they are monsters. But to paraphrase what I said before, currently Prometheans are the whipping boy of the World of Darkness. I want them to actually <i>earn</i> some of that ire by doing more monstrous things to get by, or by having monstrous urges to complete themselves that even they don't understand. While it's true that The Monster didn't mean to kill that little girl, he did still <i>kill that little girl</i>. The Golem of Prague is deactivated because he may desecrate the Sabbath, or becomes violent. In <b>A.I.: Artificial Intelligence</b> David (Haley Joel Osment) is <i>obsessed</i> with his mother to the point of being disturbing.<br /> <br /> These motivations are far more interesting to me as sources of Disquiet than proximity to Prometheans, or Disfigurements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","user":"Metamurpho","date":". 10-19-2014, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T16:14:46-07:00","id":286980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=286837#post286837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These motivations are far more interesting to me as sources of Disquiet than proximity to Prometheans, or Disfigurements.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be blunt, that seems the job of upping the interlink between Torment and Disquiet from &quot;minor penalty and complementary effects&quot; and having the former come across as more like an organic element of Promethean psychology that has effects outside the context of an episode than a stress-induced overriding imperative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T19:50:10-07:00","id":287133,"title":"","content":"What I'd like from Firestorm Chronicles is to make the Pandorans workable as an enemy for more than just Prometheans. After all, a Mage can run afoul of one of the True Fae, or a vampire be vexed by one of the hosts. One of the fun things of making the nWoD setting into an inclusive toolkit is that one can throw problem in from unexpected angle, Pandorans would be great fun to throw in like that. But now that they only come awake when a Promethean is in proximity they are sadly rather limited creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T21:06:25-07:00","id":287229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=287133#post287133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'd like from Firestorm Chronicles is to make the Pandorans workable as an enemy for more than just Prometheans. After all, a Mage can run afoul of one of the True Fae, or a vampire be vexed by one of the hosts. One of the fun things of making the nWoD setting into an inclusive toolkit is that one can throw problem in from unexpected angle, Pandorans would be great fun to throw in like that. But now that they only come awake when a Promethean is in proximity they are sadly rather limited creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Area-based Firestorms and Lilithim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T23:15:46-07:00","id":287283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=286980#post286980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be blunt, that seems the job of upping the interlink between Torment and Disquiet from &quot;minor penalty and complementary effects&quot; and having the former come across as more like an organic element of Promethean psychology that has effects outside the context of an episode than a stress-induced overriding imperative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not against that. It'll be interesting to see what they'll be doing with Torment. As it stands now, though, it's one of the few things that make Prometheans monstrous aside from &quot;being grotesque in some way&quot;. I want some other reasons that they're monstrous aside from those two things, myself. Perhaps the &quot;being too good at something&quot; idea applies here, maybe expressed in some way by the Unholy Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T05:45:31-07:00","id":288471,"title":"","content":"If you want to bring in pandorans to other gamelines, in Bleeding Edge it mentions the possibility of genetically engineered pandorans that feed off of such energies as mana or vitae and never go dormant.<br /> <br /> You could have such mutant pandorans be the result of centimanni fiddling or even natural mutation if one wants, some energies make more sense for that than others: vampiric vitae, changeling glamour, g-m essence, or demonic aether for example considering either the mutative effect those innately have or their ties to some other realm that is known for being mutative","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:29:31-07:00","id":288996,"title":"","content":"Pandorans are a terrific monster-building system, for the ruleset, though I hope for a simpler means of building them. Currently I use the 3 attribute system from Mirrors for all NPCs, but that's still an imperfect system that creates challenge issues. If Promethean ever gets a Night Horrors book, I hope they take a look at streamlining Transmutations, especially if Centimani are unsupported as PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T23:34:10-07:00","id":290331,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> Kingme here!<br /> I used to be a part of the old forum but now that I hear that new material for my favorite game line, I just had to put in my two bits worth lol.<br /> <br /> I get that the Promethean line seeks for these half living beings to find humanity because, even though, they may have great power, they still are abominations of the natural order.<br /> <br /> That being said,there have been those few individuals that seek to find the joys of the Created condition with all that they are capable of (the refinement of lead). There are even other creat that are loath to give up on their supernatural edge. (I believe that one of these individuals was listed as a character in one of the source books in the New Orleans story line). <br /> <br /> What I would like to see is a bit of &quot;culture&quot; among the created to act as a bulwark against the horrors of the world and as a kind of temporary support group. Just like a throng is. Yes, I know that the rarity of the number of Created and their disquiet/wasteland effect might put any prospect of a Promethean &quot;society&quot; impossible at best; but I believe there are ways around this problem and reasons for a kind of &quot;Underground Railroad&quot; system.<br /> <br /> This would also make more sense in the 2e because appreciably their are ways to mitigate the wasteland and disquiet by taking on Roles. This means that some few Created can stay in one spot for a relatively long period of time and create a &quot;home&quot; for herself. <br /> <br /> Therefore, the felt good of running into more Created, even if there are more or less 100 of them in the world,meant that SOME form of longs instance network must have established over the centuries. (And because Azoth calls to Azoth). And I even have an idea on how to do that: through &quot;signposts&quot; or alchemy Enhanced Pilgrim marks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T00:03:43-07:00","id":290335,"title":"","content":"]<span style=\"font-family:UICTFontTextStyleBody\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Creation of &quot;signposts&quot;: alchemy enhanced pilgrim marks that convey messages, warnings, letters, and teachings to other Created who can read them thus allowing a kind of network or Underground Railroad to exist among the Prometheans.</span></span>[/COLOR]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:UICTFontTextStyleBody\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Sure, they can create marks and signs for other Created. But we're talking about creatures that are hidden among humanity that can exist for far longer than most mortals and are hunted by things that want their precious Vitriol. Signs etched into concert or tree trunks aren't going to cut it. You need something with a little more punch to weather the rigors of the World of Darkness</span></span>[/COLOR]<br /> <span style=\"font-family:UICTFontTextStyleBody\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\"> <br /> Perhaps create a transmutation set to reflect this need to connect to other created.<br /> 1 dot. Create a weak Azoth radiance that lets other Created know that there is a pilgrim Mark.<br /> <br /> 2 dots. Occult or otherwise hide the visual of a pilgrim Mark for others other than fellow Created. Three dots visual, five dots from supernatural senses or who the Promethean deems a worthy subject for the mark.<br /> <br /> 3 dots. Create a shallow psychic imprint that imparts a general impression to the receiver. Warning, safety, food, shelter.<br /> <br /> 4 dots send a detailed message to whoever wants to receive it.<br /> <br /> 5 dots. Anchor an &quot;imaginary friend&quot; to a pilgrim Mark As a Pyros spirit that helps the Promethean to the best of its ability. The spirit gains 1 point of Pyros at the rising of the sun. Two points if it is near the humor of its creator.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:UICTFontTextStyleBody\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">What I find most troubling about Promethean is that you can't seem to enjoy the fact that your alive and that MAYBE you might have some supernatural advantages over the average mundane mortal and see a side of the world that most can't. That's why I like the refinement of lead ( and perhaps this new refinement). At least you can enjoy the moments of light in the sea of darkness that is your half life. Besides, I would imagine that it would be harder to find humanity if you were a self-loathing Debbie downer who saw nothing of value in its existence. </span></span>[/COLOR]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T01:12:27-07:00","id":293551,"title":"","content":"Gentleman Gamer's interview with Matt McFarland reveals that there will be less settings than in B&amp;S, and he confirmed several: Colombus, Ohio; Tacoma, Washington; Johannesburg, South Africa; Prague, Czech Republic; and Tokyo, Japan. Two of the hooks mentioned were &quot;there are ancient Promethean-like creatures hiding under the city&quot; and &quot;Wastelands don't seem to be as bad here for some reason.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T02:20:24-07:00","id":293566,"title":"","content":"Disquiet only reaches its worst level within a Wasteland, which allows for less-nomadic play than 1e. Pandorans are less about Mockeries and more about their original creators. Centimani are explicitly not progressing on the Pilgrimage. Zeky aren't in the 2e core at all, but Matt McFarland /really/ wants to do an Antagonists book that would have them in it. There's talk of stressing a dysphoria feel in Promethean 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T06:20:48-07:00","id":293686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>atamajakki:</b> Colombus, Ohio; Tacoma, Washington; Johannesburg, South Africa; Prague, Czech Republic; and Tokyo, Japan. </div> </div> </div>Hm. So a rust belt city, the home of Apartheid, the home of the <i>the</i> Golem, and a city known for robotics innovations. Sound about right. I hope there's somewhere more rural, though. I like the sound of the Disquiet/Wasteland link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T07:59:31-07:00","id":293727,"title":"","content":"I just moved to Tacoma! It's bad, but i dunno if it's Promethean bad...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T10:19:34-07:00","id":293864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=293551#post293551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gentleman Gamer's interview with Matt McFarland reveals that there will be less settings than in B&amp;S, and he confirmed several: Colombus, Ohio; Tacoma, Washington; Johannesburg, South Africa; Prague, Czech Republic; and Tokyo, Japan. Two of the hooks mentioned were <i><b>&quot;there are ancient Promethean-like creatures hiding under the city&quot;</b></i> and &quot;Wastelands don't seem to be as bad here for some reason.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If it looks like a Promethean and walks like a Promethean but its from before recorded civilization its a...Mummy.<br /> <br /> Actually, I'm pretty sure it will be a nice general story hook for ST's to do with as they please. As a person who has potential &quot;cross-over&quot; (NPC not PC and PC) on my mind a lot, it looks like a good plot hook to drop and Arisen into a campaign for a story arch. Which might really throw both the Arisen and any Osirens for six. Amusing to say the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T01:13:47-07:00","id":295668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=293864#post293864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it looks like a Promethean and walks like a Promethean but its from before recorded civilization its a...Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually wondering right now if the first Nepri might have been created during the Old Kingdom in a failed attempt to replicate the Rite of Return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T04:33:50-07:00","id":295708,"title":"","content":"It sounds good to me, then again I know nothing about Mummy. Is the Rite of Return described anywhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T08:33:15-07:00","id":295883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=295708#post295708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds good to me, then again I know nothing about Mummy. Is the Rite of Return described anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in detail, no. The secrets of the Shan'iatu are effectively lost to us.<br /> <br /> That having been said, we do know that it requires you to kill the target of the Rite and infuse them with Sekhem, which is explicitly measurable. I could see Alchemists messing with &quot;Sekhem&quot; (Azoth) and trying to replicate the Rite with their own supplied corpses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T10:47:28-07:00","id":296003,"title":"","content":"Makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T22:07:47-07:00","id":296577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=295668#post295668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually wondering right now if the first Nepri might have been created during the Old Kingdom in a failed attempt to replicate the Rite of Return.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad idea to say the least.<br /> <br /> Also, not to derail the thread, I'll get back to topic after this post....but.<br /> <br /> Vampire, Mage and Promethean are the three games that cross-over with Mummy quite well I feel. <br /> <br /> Vampire has the historical possibilities of two immortal characters who have to face very different types of immortality (and the effect that these different immoralities have on the characters over the centuries and millennia) . <br /> Mage has a lot of common background similarities that provide a lot of plot hooks for a creative ST. <br /> <br /> Promethean has some similarities as well particularly in regards to identity. Promethean make their own identities over the course of the pilgrimage, Mummy's rediscover their identity over the descent. Interestingly 2E seems to be adding even more stuff that you can riff off between the two. Alchemists are very similar to a group of hunters that capture Mummy's (call Last Dynasty Inc) and use them to create super-medicine (and also make themselves immortal).<br /> <br /> A little wrinkle in the fluff that I have always liked about Promethean and Mummy is that both Pyros and Sekhem are detectable to mundane science, and they are the only &quot;supernatural resources&quot; that are detectable in this way. So there is another link between the two if an ST want's to make something out of it.<br /> <br /> Some Mummy fluff talks about aspects of the Rite of Return leaking into later cultures, but that no one ever managed to recreate it. It implies that most of these bastardized Rites did nothing. Some might have though (its a topic that might be covered to a certain extent by a Mummy supplement next year) might have produced &quot;flawed copies&quot; of the Arisen. Having he Nepri be one such attempt is a good tie between the two games if an ST wanted it to be.<br /> <br /> Fitting in the other types of Promethean is a bit harder though, as their is not so much of an Egyptian link or the idea of the creative act as an attempt at rebirth or immortality. The Tammuz kinda work, as Mummy mentions that the ancient Hebrews defiantly got hold of some stuff from Irem. Ulgan could work as coming from Ubar a spirit infested rival culture to Irem that was destroyed in a war between the two. The others are a much harder fit. <br /> <br /> OK I'll shut up about this now.<br /> <br /> Back to Promethean only discussion. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T23:29:53-08:00","id":300805,"title":"","content":"Everyone go vote on the current blog post for Complex Refinements so we can learn about Phosphorum! <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sundays-eternal-choice/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/sundays-eternal-choice/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T02:28:10-08:00","id":307277,"title":"","content":"Has anyone here ever heard of the video game <i>Haunting Ground</i>? <br /> <br /> I definitely think that inspiration not only for Alchemists (new additions in the 2e), but also Prometheans, could be drawn from that game...<br /> <br /> Also, stop me if this has been mentioned already, but I think this game could benefit from the ability to play around with a few alchemical substances. Like Prometheans could create and distribute various mixtures amongst themselves--or even experiment with. Perhaps the ability to modify plants to produce alchemical compounds, like sunstone and other such elixirs...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactio